WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.168
Tianran: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.737
we wanted to find all the differences

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:06.539
between McDonald's in the US and China.

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.508
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.712
New season, USA versus China.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.514
I'm so excited for you guys to see this

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:17.584
and to meet our new cohost, Tianran.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:20.020
USA versus China, let's go.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:25.291
Drinks from McDonald's in
China come in three sizes,

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:28.194
small, medium, and big.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:32.365
But for some reason the
medium is 444 milliliters,

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:36.703
which in Chinese basically
just means die, die, die,

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:37.871
which is just super unlucky,

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.706
so I guess they really
want you to either get

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.474
the large or the small.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.077
The drinks at a US
McDonald's come four sizes,

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.979
the extra small, where'd it go?

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.147
Sorry, they forgot it.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:50.383
The small, the medium, and the large.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.887
Our large is 80.9% bigger

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.922
than China's largest soda.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.524
Let's see if that's true.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.359
Bound to be a little bit in the lid.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.764
That is blasphemous!

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.567
Shame these people. Shame this clown.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.103
Some of you over the past several years

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.805
have said something to the tune of,

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.239
it doesn't count or it's wrong

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.508
because we add the ice, or
we keep the ice in there,

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.676
and that isn't a true measurement,

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.778
which I don't believe, but fine.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.246
For the first time ever,

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.248
I want to measure this without the ice.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.951
I'm solving this once and for all.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:27.320
So, right away you get even less soda.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.858
Let's get this up to
exactly 32 fluid ounces.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.560
32 ounces of Coca-Cola

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.931
in the supposed 32-ounce McDonald's cup.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.732
I'm so sick of this.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:43.570
Why are they saying 32 fluid ounces?

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.540
Look! Just say 30 or 31. It's fine.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.775
Your move, McDonald's.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.810
Our fries come in three sizes:

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.946
small, medium, and large.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.881
American fries come in three sizes:

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:57.317
small, medium, and large.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.786
We will now weigh our largest fry.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.055
So, what about McNuggets?

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.890
Here in China, you can only get them

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.359
as an order of five or 10,

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:09.062
which is really just two portions of five.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.797
That's cute, China. Real cute.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:14.467
Here in the US, we have way
many more nugget options.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.469
Four-piece, for your infant,

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.105
six-piece, 10-piece, 20-piece,

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:22.108
and our largest, the 40-piece.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.511
All the mathheads watching
will be quick to point out

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:29.516
that this is 300% of
China's largest portion.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:34.687
So, here are all the McDonald's
menu items from China

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.489
that you won't find in the US.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.925
Here are all the
McDonald's items in the US

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.226
you won't find in China.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.095
Oh, my God, I've been
staring at this for so long.

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:44.264
This is incredible. Check out the back!

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:47.267
It's an origami apple! This is the best.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.568
Let's see what we got.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:51.004
A hamburger, mini fries,

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:54.140
a drink, a corn cup.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.076
[gasps] Dun-dun-dun!

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.545
Po!

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:02.282
Oh, my God, this is way
better than the Hamburglar.

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:05.084
What? do I have to build Po as well?

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.421
This is -- [laughs] I'm too old for this.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.156
Anyway, if you don't want a hamburger,

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:13.092
you can also change this
out for a fish fillet

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.395
or for four pieces of nuggets.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:20.200
You can also get the corn cup
changed out for apple slices,

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.902
but they will cost you 1 kuai extra.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:28.007
And with the juice, you can
have either apple juice,

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.976
milk, or water.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:33.546
So only healthy options
here in China's McDonald's.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.981
OK, now on to the toy.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.649
So, this is going to take
a while. Give me a second.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:37.483
Ugh.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:40.987
And then something flips
out from behind his groin.

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:44.257
In here! It's coming together!

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.559
Oh!

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.861
It's a basketball hoop.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:51.898
Oh, my God, this is ingenuity at its best.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.700
Look, we can play hoops with this.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.702
Three, two, one!

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.637
Whoa!

00:03:57.637 --> 00:04:01.241
I noticed that his Happy
Meal, even the box was a toy.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:03.943
In America, our Happy Meal box

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:06.379
is another opportunity
for an advertisement.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:09.582
All-new season of "The Masked
Singer" on Fox. Check it out.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:12.485
Jesus, they're shameless. These kids.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:15.255
Remember before, the
extra-small fry? Found it.

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:17.223
More nuggets, a four-piece.

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.825
Apple slices.

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:21.628
Our toy is decidedly not a puzzle.

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:24.197
Remember when Kermit
the Frog was in there?

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.465
That was weird.

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:26.566
OK, what is this?

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:28.735
Who? What celebrity was the fox?

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.270
Oh, it was Wayne Brady.
OK, I've heard of him.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.338
What, is his head in here?

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:33.806
Oddly enough, shows the stark difference

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.074
between China and the US.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.809
Theirs has this puzzle to put together,

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.678
ours is an ad for a TV show.

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:41.948
[laughs and cries]

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:46.953
OK, so these are our
exclusive beef burgers.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:50.423
Here in China, people mostly eat pork,

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.858
so I think with the beef

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:54.527
they've really had to
go the premium route,

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.362
so you've got some
interesting combinations.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:05:00.166
This is the German sausage
double beef burger,

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:02.969
but in Chinese the name is kind of like

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:05.938
the "anti-vegetarian tyrant."

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:09.242
So they've got some pretty
aggressive marketing for this.

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:13.546
Imagine Terry Crews just
pulsing his pecks while he --

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.947
what is that?

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.082
Ugh.

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:18.985
If this is what they
call a German sausage,

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:21.354
then I think the Germans
will be very angry.

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:24.691
Here we've got a BLT double beef burger.

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:28.728
I'm so sad. What is this?

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:30.263
This is like a BLT sandwich

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:33.266
that's been sat at the bottom
of your bag for a week.

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:34.834
I'm excited about these, though.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:39.305
These are the Angus
max thick beef burgers.

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:42.208
Now, McDonald's have done
premium collaborations

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:44.677
with Michelin-starred chefs in the past,

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:48.214
and they even have these
really super-fancy packaging.

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:51.351
Look at that. Double cheeseburger.

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:55.722
Oh, wow! Look at that.

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:58.358
The meat patty is thicker than my thumb.

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:00.059
That's a proper burger.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.327
Mm.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:04.163
Well, it's very meaty. Incredibly cheesy.

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.733
This is the double cheeseburger,
so I can understand that.

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:08.468
For the vast majority of Chinese people,

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:12.038
their understanding or
access to Western food

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:14.006
may really come from
fast-food restaurants.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:17.510
So this is probably the
gourmet burger experience

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.912
for the vast majority of
the Chinese population.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:23.649
In the US, you can get a
Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:26.018
What the heck? They gave us two tops?

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.387
This is the special two-top

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:28.921
Quarter Pounder with cheese, apparently.

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:31.624
And we also have a double Quarter Pounder,

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:33.226
if you want to increase the meat.

00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:34.994
If someone wants to get
their daily vegetables,

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:37.397
here is the Quarter
Pounder with cheese deluxe.

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:38.765
Swimming in mayonnaise.

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:40.666
We have something in the United
States called the McDouble.

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:43.369
If you want slightly less
cheese on a double cheeseburger,

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:44.203
we got you covered.

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:45.438
Quarter Pounder with bacon.

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:46.839
Every once in a while, they
just take a Quarter Pounder

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:47.807
and put bacon on it,

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:50.009
and they repackage it for a celebrity.

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:53.946
And these are our exclusive
chicken and fish options.

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:55.281
So, I want to start you off with this,

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:59.619
which has since become
McDonald's best spicy burger.

00:06:59.619 --> 00:07:02.588
This is the McSpicy chicken fillet.

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:06.926
Apparently it's 1,000 SHU,

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.828
which is a Scoville unit,

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:12.198
and it's roughly equivalent
to the spiciness you get

00:07:12.198 --> 00:07:13.966
from a spicy and numbing hot pot,

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:16.235
and those guys are pretty spicy.

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:18.037
Mm. Oh, that's delicious.

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:19.539
You don't feel the burn at first,

00:07:19.539 --> 00:07:21.774
and then it's like your tongue
slowly starts to wake up,

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:23.709
and it's like a frog in a pot.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:26.179
It slowly starts to realize
it's being boiled alive,

00:07:26.179 --> 00:07:27.880
and by the end of this burger,

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.048
you're going to want that Coke.

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:33.653
Now, this is McDonald's
best-selling non-spicy burger,

00:07:33.653 --> 00:07:35.521
the grilled chicken sandwich,

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.824
which supposedly has no growth hormones

00:07:37.824 --> 00:07:38.925
in their chicken feed.

00:07:40.393 --> 00:07:43.229
Very heavy on the black
pepper. Oh. Ooh, wow.

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:44.297
I'm very excited about this.

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:46.999
This is the McCrunch
chicken fillet burger,

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:49.836
and in Chinese the name is "katsusui."

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:52.138
It sounds like how it's supposed to taste.

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:54.106
"Ka" is kind of like "crunchy,"

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:56.042
and "tsu" is kind of like

00:07:56.042 --> 00:07:58.077
the juice kind of squirting out.

00:07:58.077 --> 00:08:02.582
So this should be both crunchy and juicy.

00:08:02.582 --> 00:08:06.352
Ooh, that looks like a much
better piece of chicken.

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:10.089
Yes, yes.

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:12.258
I didn't get the "ka,"

00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:14.293
probably because this has gone a bit cold,

00:08:14.293 --> 00:08:16.996
but look at that. It is juicy in there.

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:20.266
OK, this is the
super-spicy chicken fillet.

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:21.300
Look at this guy!

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.803
You know this is going to
be super spicy. It's orange!

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:30.142
It's not that spicy.

00:08:30.142 --> 00:08:32.311
[coughs] Ooh!

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:34.680
It's not as -- oh!

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.883
Oh, my God.

00:08:36.883 --> 00:08:37.917
Very tasty.

00:08:37.917 --> 00:08:40.987
Finish that, and it's

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:42.622
to the hospital you go. Whew.

00:08:42.622 --> 00:08:47.193
And last but, in my opinion,
least, the double fish burger.

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:49.629
Chicken sandwiches.

00:08:49.629 --> 00:08:51.797
There's something that is new-ish,

00:08:51.797 --> 00:08:53.599
the bacon ranch McCrispy.

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:56.335
Hm.

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:57.336
It's just OK.

00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:59.972
There's also a bacon
ranch deluxe McCrispy,

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:01.507
where deluxe equals more vegetables.

00:09:01.507 --> 00:09:05.311
The McCrispy is something that
we ordered and they forgot.

00:09:05.311 --> 00:09:07.513
And then now, piling on the vegetables,

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:09.448
you got the McCrispy deluxe.

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:11.050
Spicy McCrispy.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.019
So they just rebranded the
crispy chicken sandwich

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:14.487
to be the McCrispy?

00:09:15.421 --> 00:09:18.090
How spicy can this be?
This is not spicy at all.

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:25.698
So, McDonald's China has one roll option,

00:09:25.698 --> 00:09:29.135
which is this crispy pork and

00:09:29.135 --> 00:09:31.671
pickled bamboo shoot wrap.

00:09:33.673 --> 00:09:35.207
Mm.

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:36.442
That's tasty. It's nice and crunchy.

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:39.712
Very spicy! [laughs] Wow.

00:09:41.147 --> 00:09:42.048
Mm.

00:09:42.048 --> 00:09:43.583
It's spicy. It's sour.

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:46.485
Anything that has Sichuan peppercorn in it

00:09:46.485 --> 00:09:47.620
is just incredible.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.855
Here we've got the McSpicy wings,

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:54.126
which come in portions of two, four,

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:55.895
or nine.

00:09:55.895 --> 00:09:57.463
Straight up, I wish we had those wings.

00:09:57.463 --> 00:09:58.698
Those wings look really good.

00:09:58.698 --> 00:10:00.333
Also, I don't know if you've noticed,

00:10:00.333 --> 00:10:03.569
but the decoration here on the packet,

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:04.570
this is a collaboration

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:08.808
with a streetwear brand
called Clot, or C-L-O-T,

00:10:08.808 --> 00:10:12.044
and it uses traditional
Chinese aesthetics.

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:14.280
So here you've got the lucky knot,

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:17.917
which is sort of like a symbol
for good luck and longevity.

00:10:17.917 --> 00:10:19.085
As Chinese as it gets.

00:10:19.085 --> 00:10:22.755
And this is also the same
flavor as the McSpicy burger.

00:10:22.755 --> 00:10:25.625
I don't know if there's an
accurate translation for this.

00:10:25.625 --> 00:10:27.960
This is literally called

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:31.364
"such a big chicken chop."

00:10:31.364 --> 00:10:35.468
It's about the same size as
my palm, a little bit bigger.

00:10:35.468 --> 00:10:37.169
The McCrispy chicken.

00:10:38.237 --> 00:10:40.473
Mm. Crispy, wow.

00:10:40.473 --> 00:10:42.008
Mm, yes!

00:10:42.008 --> 00:10:45.711
This is very special.

00:10:45.711 --> 00:10:47.747
We didn't think we'd be
able to get this today.

00:10:47.747 --> 00:10:49.415
This is the

00:10:49.415 --> 00:10:52.952
spicy lobster-flavored chicken tenders.

00:10:52.952 --> 00:10:55.054
The Chinese says "yao yao,"

00:10:55.054 --> 00:10:56.856
which means you have to shake it.

00:10:58.991 --> 00:11:01.027
Oh, let's try these babies.

00:11:01.027 --> 00:11:02.228
There was no need to shake it at all.

00:11:02.228 --> 00:11:04.030
There's no seasoning there at all.

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:07.299
It's just literally chicken tenders.

00:11:08.668 --> 00:11:13.339
It's more of an aspiration
towards lobster, though.

00:11:13.339 --> 00:11:15.741
And we've got crinkle-cut fries.

00:11:15.741 --> 00:11:17.410
Oh, how I've missed you.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:20.012
Mm. Nothing beats a crinkle-cut fry.

00:11:20.012 --> 00:11:23.182
In China, we have a bunch
of different barrel options.

00:11:23.182 --> 00:11:27.520
For example, this one is
the Golden Arches bucket,

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.488
which actually didn't come in a bucket,

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:31.590
they just put everything into a box.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:34.460
The name actually is the
reason why we got this,

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:37.063
because McDonald's in China

00:11:37.063 --> 00:11:40.132
has officially renamed to Jingongmen,

00:11:40.132 --> 00:11:42.168
which literally translates
as Golden Arches,

00:11:42.168 --> 00:11:45.137
and when they did that
they caught a lot of flak.

00:11:45.137 --> 00:11:46.672
Everybody started laughing at them.

00:11:46.672 --> 00:11:49.508
Nobody calls them the
Golden Arches in Chinese.

00:11:49.508 --> 00:11:51.043
It's just McDonald's.

00:11:51.043 --> 00:11:54.480
But legally they are now
known as the Golden Arches.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:58.017
Featuring sauces, you know
what that means, Yuelei.

00:11:58.017 --> 00:11:59.585
Sauce talk.

00:11:59.585 --> 00:12:02.354
Here are all of our exclusive sauces.

00:12:02.354 --> 00:12:04.256
Garlic chili.

00:12:04.256 --> 00:12:05.324
That's pretty much it.

00:12:05.324 --> 00:12:06.992
Oh, and no Sichuan sauce, either.

00:12:06.992 --> 00:12:08.160
That's an American invention,

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.695
just like General Tso's chicken.

00:12:09.695 --> 00:12:12.665
But here in China, you
don't really get sauces

00:12:12.665 --> 00:12:15.501
unless you ask for them.
They come with the nuggets.

00:12:15.501 --> 00:12:18.137
Chinese people expect food to be complete

00:12:18.137 --> 00:12:19.438
when it arrives at your table.

00:12:19.438 --> 00:12:22.041
You don't go and add more sauce to it.

00:12:22.041 --> 00:12:24.910
Sauces. In the United
States, optimal for dipping.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:27.246
Tangy barbecue. Spicy Buffalo.

00:12:27.246 --> 00:12:29.515
It's the USA, so you
know we got that ranch.

00:12:29.515 --> 00:12:30.549
Honey mustard.

00:12:30.549 --> 00:12:33.319
Honey, which is not here.
I don't know where it is.

00:12:33.319 --> 00:12:35.821
Mayonnaise, which also
they did not include.

00:12:35.821 --> 00:12:38.057
Mexican-style salsa.

00:12:38.057 --> 00:12:40.760
These are our exclusive desserts.

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.895
I am going to try every
single one of them.

00:12:42.895 --> 00:12:46.432
We can start with the taro pie.

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:49.301
Taro is kind of like a cross

00:12:49.301 --> 00:12:51.337
between sweet potato and potato.

00:12:51.337 --> 00:12:54.140
It's often used in desserts in Asia.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:58.010
You'll find them in everything
from pies to bubble tea.

00:12:59.278 --> 00:13:02.081
It's a bit like yam with a bit of jam,

00:13:02.081 --> 00:13:03.516
but it's subtly sweet.

00:13:03.516 --> 00:13:06.051
For Chinese people, if you say
a dessert is not very sweet,

00:13:06.051 --> 00:13:07.219
that's actually a compliment.

00:13:07.219 --> 00:13:10.556
Pineapple pie, also one of my favorites.

00:13:11.824 --> 00:13:15.394
Mm. That is heavenly.

00:13:15.394 --> 00:13:16.629
I think I'm going to finish this.

00:13:16.629 --> 00:13:18.964
Now I need to chew for a very long time.

00:13:20.366 --> 00:13:22.501
So, here we've got the strawberry sundae,

00:13:22.501 --> 00:13:23.969
which is kind of melted already,

00:13:23.969 --> 00:13:26.806
but I'm sure it would've been
amazing when it first arrived.

00:13:26.806 --> 00:13:30.109
An affogato and a
matcha-flavored affogato,

00:13:30.109 --> 00:13:33.212
and then here we've got the McFlurrys.

00:13:33.212 --> 00:13:36.582
This is the strawberry McFlurry

00:13:36.582 --> 00:13:38.918
with Oreo cookies.

00:13:38.918 --> 00:13:43.489
Oh, my gosh, that is perhaps
the most sinful thing

00:13:43.489 --> 00:13:44.723
that you could have.

00:13:44.723 --> 00:13:47.159
Oh, but it's so good.

00:13:47.159 --> 00:13:49.395
This is just the regular McFlurry,

00:13:49.395 --> 00:13:51.897
and here is my all-time favorite,

00:13:51.897 --> 00:13:55.801
mango-pomelo-sago-flavored McFlurry.

00:13:55.801 --> 00:13:58.370
Hm. It's very different
with the ice cream.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:00.840
You still got the mango in there,

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:04.176
and the pomelo, it's
very juicy, it's tender,

00:14:04.176 --> 00:14:05.978
like little tiny pips in there

00:14:05.978 --> 00:14:07.646
that kind of pop when you eat them.

00:14:07.646 --> 00:14:08.914
Oh! Just perfect.

00:14:10.115 --> 00:14:12.585
Mm. Brain freeze. Oh!

00:14:12.585 --> 00:14:13.819
In the US, you can get yourself

00:14:13.819 --> 00:14:16.555
a McFlurry with mini M&amp;M's.

00:14:16.555 --> 00:14:21.227
For some reason, mini M&amp;M's
taste better than regular M&amp;M's.

00:14:21.227 --> 00:14:24.096
I love mini M&amp;M's. Mm.

00:14:24.096 --> 00:14:25.698
Hot caramel sundae.

00:14:25.698 --> 00:14:27.933
It's classic. They don't
have this in China?

00:14:27.933 --> 00:14:31.570
God, I mean, what's more
American than an apple pie?

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:33.739
Look at this thing. Let's
crack that bad boy open.

00:14:33.739 --> 00:14:35.541
We got chocolate chip cookies.

00:14:35.541 --> 00:14:37.509
Shakes. You can get three
different types of shakes

00:14:37.509 --> 00:14:39.645
here at a US McDonald's. Chocolate.

00:14:40.913 --> 00:14:41.881
Classic chocolate.

00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:43.449
Strawberry, personal favorite.

00:14:44.316 --> 00:14:45.484
That's so good.

00:14:45.484 --> 00:14:47.419
Vanilla, the classic.

00:14:47.419 --> 00:14:51.590
Our exclusive drinks
include the Fuze iced tea.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:55.127
We've got the Minute Maid orange McFloat,

00:14:55.127 --> 00:14:57.463
bubble tea, soy milk,

00:14:57.463 --> 00:14:59.999
pure milk, Ceylon black tea,

00:14:59.999 --> 00:15:02.434
which in China we would call red tea,

00:15:02.434 --> 00:15:04.870
which just confuses you for fun.

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:07.139
I'm going to go back to here

00:15:07.139 --> 00:15:09.174
because this is the
only thing I want to try

00:15:09.174 --> 00:15:10.175
out of all of them.

00:15:12.077 --> 00:15:13.479
That tastes like orange juice.

00:15:13.479 --> 00:15:15.281
It's just plain old orange juice.

00:15:15.281 --> 00:15:17.283
In the US, you can get
yourself a Dr Pepper,

00:15:17.283 --> 00:15:20.986
a Fanta orange and an
Orange Lavaburst, lemonade.

00:15:20.986 --> 00:15:23.255
You can also get frozen drinks.

00:15:23.255 --> 00:15:26.458
You can get a frozen Fanta
blue raspberry or frozen Coke.

00:15:26.458 --> 00:15:28.127
McDonald's also has smoothies.

00:15:28.127 --> 00:15:32.197
A mango pineapple smoothie
and a strawberry smoothie.

00:15:32.197 --> 00:15:34.099
Yeah, they make a decent
smoothie at McDonald's.

00:15:34.099 --> 00:15:34.900
As you can see,

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:38.103
we have an absolute ton of
breakfast options here in China.

00:15:38.103 --> 00:15:40.973
I think McDonald's has done
fantastic in this regard

00:15:40.973 --> 00:15:45.110
because the Chinese treat
breakfast as a very special meal.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.578
We have a very similar saying to,

00:15:46.578 --> 00:15:48.514
"Eat breakfast like a king,

00:15:48.514 --> 00:15:51.050
lunch like a prince,
dinner like a pauper."

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:55.154
So, starting with the
sausage McMuffin with egg.

00:15:55.154 --> 00:15:56.388
Always a good way to start the day.

00:15:56.388 --> 00:15:59.758
You can get this as a double as well.

00:15:59.758 --> 00:16:01.961
Next we have the ham muffin.

00:16:01.961 --> 00:16:04.663
It's just literally a piece of ham,

00:16:04.663 --> 00:16:06.432
some lettuce, and two muffins,

00:16:06.432 --> 00:16:09.368
so I guess this would
actually be a hamburger.

00:16:09.368 --> 00:16:11.103
You can get this as a double as well.

00:16:11.103 --> 00:16:13.973
Next we have the grilled chicken muffin.

00:16:17.209 --> 00:16:19.478
This chicken's been
sitting around for a while.

00:16:19.478 --> 00:16:23.816
Next we've got the
crispy chicken McMuffin.

00:16:23.816 --> 00:16:28.821
So this is the breakfast version of the

00:16:28.821 --> 00:16:30.889
"such a big chicken chop."

00:16:30.889 --> 00:16:34.893
Breakfast in the US. We have
so many breakfast options,

00:16:34.893 --> 00:16:36.895
starting down here, the sandwiches.

00:16:36.895 --> 00:16:39.131
Egg McMuffin. Maybe the first

00:16:39.131 --> 00:16:41.266
fast breakfast sandwich
to ever hit the market.

00:16:41.266 --> 00:16:43.268
Sausage McMuffin. Sausage and cheese.

00:16:43.268 --> 00:16:44.236
If you hadn't noticed,

00:16:44.236 --> 00:16:46.772
this is all on what we
call an English muffin,

00:16:46.772 --> 00:16:48.173
'cause they're from England.

00:16:48.173 --> 00:16:50.409
There's also a bacon,
egg, and cheese McMuffin.

00:16:50.409 --> 00:16:53.078
But the option that we have most for

00:16:53.078 --> 00:16:55.614
are the scrambled-egg burgers.

00:16:55.614 --> 00:16:57.549
Scrambled-egg grilled chicken burger.

00:16:57.549 --> 00:17:02.287
The scrambled egg is
very luminously yellow.

00:17:02.287 --> 00:17:03.489
Wow, look at that.

00:17:04.957 --> 00:17:06.525
Very peppery.

00:17:06.525 --> 00:17:08.193
They love their pepper here, don't they?

00:17:08.193 --> 00:17:10.462
So, the scrambled-egg sausage burger.

00:17:10.462 --> 00:17:11.997
You'll notice the buns are different now.

00:17:11.997 --> 00:17:14.299
We're no longer on the muffins.
We're back to regular buns.

00:17:14.299 --> 00:17:16.368
Oh, it's squeezing out, isn't it?

00:17:16.368 --> 00:17:18.904
Scrambled-egg cheeseburger.

00:17:18.904 --> 00:17:22.274
This is the brightest burger
I've ever seen in my life.

00:17:22.274 --> 00:17:23.876
It's definitely very portable.

00:17:23.876 --> 00:17:25.978
I think that's one thing that
McDonald's has done very well,

00:17:25.978 --> 00:17:29.615
because Chinese breakfast
traditionally is not too portable

00:17:29.615 --> 00:17:32.084
in the sense that you need to
sit down to a lot of meals,

00:17:32.084 --> 00:17:34.953
like if you want to eat
wonton in the morning

00:17:34.953 --> 00:17:36.789
or if you want to eat
some soups in the morning.

00:17:36.789 --> 00:17:38.290
This you can just take and go.

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:41.393
And, of course, you can
get the scrambled-egg

00:17:41.393 --> 00:17:44.430
German-flavor-sausage burger.

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:45.497
Oh, at least they give you two,

00:17:45.497 --> 00:17:48.400
as opposed to just one tiny sausage.

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.636
Biscuits, biscuits, biscuits.

00:17:50.636 --> 00:17:51.937
Sausage and egg biscuit.

00:17:51.937 --> 00:17:54.306
So, the biscuits are the
same breakfast sandwiches

00:17:54.306 --> 00:17:56.208
you get in English-muffin form,

00:17:56.208 --> 00:17:58.877
but in this biscuit form,
the American biscuit,

00:17:58.877 --> 00:18:01.880
this dry, crumbly, buttery biscuit,

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:04.383
there is a bacon, egg, and cheese one.

00:18:04.383 --> 00:18:06.685
For some reason people in this country

00:18:06.685 --> 00:18:11.123
seem to want just a biscuit and sausage

00:18:11.123 --> 00:18:12.858
with no sauce, no nothing.

00:18:12.858 --> 00:18:16.261
This is as dry as if
you'd go into a barbershop

00:18:16.261 --> 00:18:18.297
and take a handful of hair clippings

00:18:18.297 --> 00:18:21.533
and just shove them in your
mouth. This is that dry.

00:18:21.533 --> 00:18:24.336
In the US we have something
called McGriddles,

00:18:24.336 --> 00:18:26.238
and McGriddles are breakfast sandwiches

00:18:26.238 --> 00:18:29.608
where they replace the
English muffin and/or biscuit

00:18:29.608 --> 00:18:31.143
with pancakes.

00:18:31.143 --> 00:18:33.112
So, first of all, they got the
McDonald's logo right there.

00:18:33.112 --> 00:18:34.313
Too hilarious.

00:18:34.313 --> 00:18:36.615
Somehow, through the miracle of science,

00:18:36.615 --> 00:18:40.185
was able to inject syrup
into these pancakes.

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:42.821
Sensational.

00:18:42.821 --> 00:18:46.191
You can get your McGriddles
in sausage, egg, and cheese

00:18:46.191 --> 00:18:47.392
and then just sausage.

00:18:48.393 --> 00:18:52.297
On to what I was going to
talk about, the congee.

00:18:52.297 --> 00:18:55.100
Congee is a very traditional
breakfast item here in China.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:57.236
It's basically just rice porridge,

00:18:57.236 --> 00:18:59.605
and it's something that is

00:18:59.605 --> 00:19:02.708
kind of like chicken
soup for Chinese people,

00:19:02.708 --> 00:19:04.843
in the sense that if you fall ill,

00:19:04.843 --> 00:19:07.846
you're going to be given one
of these, plain, with nothing.

00:19:07.846 --> 00:19:10.916
This I think is with century egg,

00:19:10.916 --> 00:19:14.286
but the century egg,
it tastes a little bit

00:19:14.286 --> 00:19:16.288
like a blue-cheese version of egg,

00:19:16.288 --> 00:19:19.224
in that it's kind of
like egg that's gone off,

00:19:19.224 --> 00:19:20.692
but in a very nice way.

00:19:20.692 --> 00:19:24.029
And this adds a nice
savoriness to the congee.

00:19:24.029 --> 00:19:26.732
You can also get it with

00:19:26.732 --> 00:19:29.401
pickles and bamboo shoots.

00:19:29.401 --> 00:19:31.170
And if you're going to get congee,

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:32.604
then usually you need to pair it

00:19:32.604 --> 00:19:35.908
with what they've called
an "Asian dough stick."

00:19:35.908 --> 00:19:37.943
This is what we call a youtiao,

00:19:37.943 --> 00:19:40.946
which is literally a stick of fried dough.

00:19:40.946 --> 00:19:43.081
These are absolutely amazing

00:19:43.081 --> 00:19:45.551
when paired with stuff like soy milk

00:19:45.551 --> 00:19:47.419
and, of course, with congee.

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:50.222
You know, you need to eat these fresh.

00:19:50.222 --> 00:19:53.125
Deep-fried, they are so incredibly crispy.

00:19:53.125 --> 00:19:55.360
Oh, wow, well done, McDonald's.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.729
Like, 10 hours later,
these are still crispy.

00:19:57.729 --> 00:20:00.365
I'm very impressed but
also a little bit worried

00:20:00.365 --> 00:20:03.202
because they should never be
this crispy after that long.

00:20:03.202 --> 00:20:05.137
I wonder what they've put in here.

00:20:05.137 --> 00:20:07.706
Last but not least, our
German sausages again.

00:20:07.706 --> 00:20:09.107
It's not just sandwiches, you guys.

00:20:09.107 --> 00:20:12.644
We also have something in the US,

00:20:12.644 --> 00:20:15.514
the Big Breakfast, which
is totally in disarray.

00:20:15.514 --> 00:20:17.849
This is like the advertising
for this breakfast.

00:20:17.849 --> 00:20:19.484
I'm sorry?

00:20:19.484 --> 00:20:22.521
The Big Breakfast with pancakes.

00:20:22.521 --> 00:20:24.823
You can also get hotcakes, aka pancakes.

00:20:24.823 --> 00:20:27.759
There's no way they're back
there, like, ladling the ...

00:20:27.759 --> 00:20:29.761
right? There's no way they're doing that.

00:20:29.761 --> 00:20:31.797
These have to be premade and
they just heat them up, right?

00:20:31.797 --> 00:20:33.165
So, hotcakes and sausage.

00:20:33.165 --> 00:20:34.733
Oh, and they both come with syrup,

00:20:34.733 --> 00:20:36.101
so you know what we gotta do.

00:20:36.101 --> 00:20:39.705
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho, yeah!

00:20:39.705 --> 00:20:41.940
We also have a

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:45.844
morning wrap with ham.

00:20:45.844 --> 00:20:49.147
The wrap itself is basically frozen solid.

00:20:49.147 --> 00:20:53.585
We can exchange that with sausage,

00:20:53.585 --> 00:20:54.987
which is also frozen.

00:20:54.987 --> 00:20:56.955
It's almost like a piece of art now,

00:20:56.955 --> 00:20:59.558
like you're supposed to look
at it instead of eating it.

00:20:59.558 --> 00:21:01.360
Wow, frozen in time.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:03.929
US McDonald's have

00:21:03.929 --> 00:21:06.765
sausage breakfast burritos.

00:21:06.765 --> 00:21:07.799
I mean, I can't even unfold,

00:21:07.799 --> 00:21:09.134
I'm just, like, ripping it apart.

00:21:09.134 --> 00:21:11.470
You got scrambled eggs, the sausage,

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:13.672
it comes with Mexican-style salsa.

00:21:13.672 --> 00:21:14.973
Hey, McDonald's, it's actually pretty good

00:21:14.973 --> 00:21:16.375
considering that this is, like,

00:21:16.375 --> 00:21:19.511
probably the furthest
you can get from salsa

00:21:19.511 --> 00:21:21.246
and still legally be
able to call it salsa.

00:21:21.246 --> 00:21:23.448
If you're not trying to
completely destroy your insides

00:21:23.448 --> 00:21:24.316
first thing in the morning,

00:21:24.316 --> 00:21:27.019
you can get yourself
fruit and maple oatmeal.

00:21:27.019 --> 00:21:28.020
Seems like your breakfast

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:30.455
is trying to escape
your body an hour later,

00:21:30.455 --> 00:21:32.057
might actually be able to hold this down.

00:21:32.057 --> 00:21:35.861
Et voilà, ze options from le bakery.

00:21:35.861 --> 00:21:37.296
So, we have macarons.

00:21:37.296 --> 00:21:39.164
Right now we have two different flavors,

00:21:39.164 --> 00:21:42.501
chocolate and berries.

00:21:42.501 --> 00:21:44.503
These actually look really legit.

00:21:46.271 --> 00:21:49.107
Pat yourself on the back.
This is really good.

00:21:49.107 --> 00:21:51.576
And these things are lamingtons.

00:21:51.576 --> 00:21:53.478
I've never actually had lamingtons.

00:21:53.478 --> 00:21:56.982
Apparently, they're basically
Australian sponge cakes

00:21:56.982 --> 00:21:59.117
which are covered in coconut flakes,

00:21:59.117 --> 00:22:01.286
and this is a lemon-flavored one.

00:22:02.254 --> 00:22:04.089
Surprisingly addictive.

00:22:04.089 --> 00:22:06.458
We have the McCafé bakery.

00:22:06.458 --> 00:22:10.362
At the McCafé bakery, you
get, you know, sweet treats,

00:22:10.362 --> 00:22:11.630
not necessarily for breakfast

00:22:11.630 --> 00:22:13.498
but probably leaning more
towards breakfast time.

00:22:13.498 --> 00:22:15.834
Ba-bam, blueberry muffin.

00:22:15.834 --> 00:22:19.037
A cinnamon roll with
cream cheese frosting.

00:22:19.037 --> 00:22:22.441
It looks like it's squishy.
It most certainly is not.

00:22:22.441 --> 00:22:24.976
I mean, come on, who doesn't
love an apple fritter?

00:22:24.976 --> 00:22:27.479
An apple fritter is a doughnut
that tastes like apple

00:22:27.479 --> 00:22:31.049
and is shaped like it was
just squoze in someone's hand

00:22:31.049 --> 00:22:32.284
for some strange reason.

00:22:32.284 --> 00:22:36.655
These are our McCafé drink options,

00:22:36.655 --> 00:22:41.293
starting with the extra-milky
latte with oat milk.

00:22:41.293 --> 00:22:43.028
A latte is two-thirds milk,

00:22:43.028 --> 00:22:44.229
and then you add oat milk in there,

00:22:44.229 --> 00:22:47.099
I don't think we're going
to have much coffee.

00:22:47.099 --> 00:22:49.968
Oh. Oh, wow, that is surprisingly good.

00:22:49.968 --> 00:22:52.337
In China, oat milk has
really, really taken off

00:22:52.337 --> 00:22:55.207
because a lot of people did
not grow up drinking milk.

00:22:55.207 --> 00:22:57.709
A lot of Chinese people
are lactose intolerant.

00:22:57.709 --> 00:23:01.680
And so oat milk is definitely
a very healthy alternative,

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:03.248
and that's why we have the

00:23:03.248 --> 00:23:05.951
extra-strong chocolate with oat milk.

00:23:05.951 --> 00:23:08.019
You can also get this without oat milk.

00:23:08.019 --> 00:23:09.988
Extra-strong matcha milk.

00:23:09.988 --> 00:23:11.156
Extra-strong matcha --

00:23:11.156 --> 00:23:13.692
oh, we have so much matcha.

00:23:13.692 --> 00:23:16.528
Extra-strong chocolate smoothie,

00:23:16.528 --> 00:23:20.332
extra-strong milk and vanilla smoothie,

00:23:20.332 --> 00:23:25.070
and the matcha milk with matcha jelly.

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:27.372
Matcha, matcha, oh, I'm going to --

00:23:27.372 --> 00:23:31.276
We absolutely love matcha here
in China. I don't know why.

00:23:32.544 --> 00:23:35.981
It tastes like grass and frozen grass.

00:23:35.981 --> 00:23:39.050
Coffees and coffees and
coffees and coffees.

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:43.422
McDonald's has a assortment
of featured drinks,

00:23:43.422 --> 00:23:46.625
espresso drinks, mochas, iced lattes.

00:23:46.625 --> 00:23:47.793
Let's get all that on the screen.

00:23:47.793 --> 00:23:49.461
See? All these things.

00:23:49.461 --> 00:23:51.863
This is the cold brew. This is so strong.

00:23:53.198 --> 00:23:54.800
I think each of you should
eventually take a sip.

00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:56.935
You will not believe how
strong the cold brew is.

00:23:56.935 --> 00:23:58.904
Oh, my God.

00:23:58.904 --> 00:23:59.938
French vanilla latte.

00:24:00.839 --> 00:24:03.275
This is the exact
opposite. This is so sweet.

00:24:03.275 --> 00:24:05.377
Mocha. Who doesn't want hot chocolate

00:24:05.377 --> 00:24:06.778
first thing in the morning?

00:24:06.778 --> 00:24:08.280
Hilarious, people are buying that.

00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:10.615
Ooh, this is the premium roast coffee.

00:24:10.615 --> 00:24:11.716
I know I've been kind of dissing on it,

00:24:11.716 --> 00:24:14.119
but their actual coffee, the
actual McDonald's coffee,

00:24:14.119 --> 00:24:15.253
I think is very good.

00:24:15.253 --> 00:24:17.389
They're a good contender in
the coffee game, I think,

00:24:17.389 --> 00:24:18.490
in the fast-food coffee game.

00:24:18.490 --> 00:24:20.225
Especially the horrible
PR nightmare they had

00:24:20.225 --> 00:24:22.227
when they, like, destroyed
that lady's crotch

00:24:22.227 --> 00:24:23.528
with their superhot coffee.

00:24:23.528 --> 00:24:25.497
It is a comeback story, McDonald's.

00:24:25.497 --> 00:24:27.966
Almost killing a woman
with second-degree burns

00:24:27.966 --> 00:24:29.334
from boiling-hot coffee

00:24:29.334 --> 00:24:32.237
to these nice little fun café drinks.

00:24:32.237 --> 00:24:35.140
I would happily pour
this all over my crotch.

00:24:35.140 --> 00:24:37.108
You can get the iced-coffee drinks.

00:24:37.108 --> 00:24:38.777
Don't like this. This is the mocha.

00:24:38.777 --> 00:24:43.715
McDonald's in China also
has a late-night menu.

00:24:43.715 --> 00:24:46.184
They only have one item,
but this is worth it.

00:24:46.184 --> 00:24:50.422
I got it last night. These
are marinated chicken bones.

00:24:50.422 --> 00:24:51.523
They don't sound very appealing,

00:24:51.523 --> 00:24:54.860
but the Chinese name
is wordplay on an idiom

00:24:54.860 --> 00:24:59.030
which kind of means "the
highest level of artistry."

00:24:59.030 --> 00:25:01.800
And when I opened up this box,

00:25:01.800 --> 00:25:03.468
[gasps]

00:25:03.468 --> 00:25:06.371
I literally heard angels going, "Aah!"

00:25:06.371 --> 00:25:10.008
This is actually a street food

00:25:10.008 --> 00:25:14.079
from someplace up in Northeast
China called Shenyang.

00:25:14.079 --> 00:25:15.881
Chinese people love fiddly stuff,

00:25:15.881 --> 00:25:19.017
and meat on the bone is
just that much more tasty.

00:25:20.886 --> 00:25:23.555
Ah, still incredible, even cold.

00:25:23.555 --> 00:25:26.958
You know, the box actually
says "marinated chicken bones."

00:25:26.958 --> 00:25:29.528
"Be careful, it may contain bones."

00:25:29.528 --> 00:25:32.163
And you're actually supposed
to spit the bones out,

00:25:32.163 --> 00:25:35.567
but I'm having so much
fun eating this thing,

00:25:35.567 --> 00:25:37.536
I actually eat the bones too.

00:25:37.536 --> 00:25:41.139
It's spicy, it's sour, it's sweet.

00:25:41.139 --> 00:25:43.608
Ah, and just absolutely divine.

00:25:43.608 --> 00:25:46.111
I can see how people would be
inspired after eating this.

00:25:48.146 --> 00:25:51.149
So, McDonald's came to China in 1990,

00:25:51.149 --> 00:25:53.985
and then it opened in Beijing in '92.

00:25:53.985 --> 00:25:56.621
Back then, that was the largest
McDonald's in the world.

00:25:56.621 --> 00:25:58.323
They had 700 seats.

00:25:58.323 --> 00:26:02.360
On opening day, they served 40,000 people.

00:26:02.360 --> 00:26:03.828
And people didn't go there for the food.

00:26:03.828 --> 00:26:05.597
It was a place to be seen.

00:26:05.597 --> 00:26:08.333
Like, McDonald's was a window to the West.

00:26:08.333 --> 00:26:10.502
It was a cosmopolitan place

00:26:10.502 --> 00:26:14.773
to experience capitalism, in a way.

00:26:14.773 --> 00:26:18.109
But over time it became
a trendy hangout spot

00:26:18.109 --> 00:26:19.611
for city kids after school.

00:26:19.611 --> 00:26:21.212
They'd go there to do their homework.

00:26:21.212 --> 00:26:24.382
It still very much is middle class.

00:26:24.382 --> 00:26:28.219
I remember actually when I came
to visit China 20 years ago,

00:26:28.219 --> 00:26:32.390
my aunts greeted me at the
airport with bags of McDonald's,

00:26:32.390 --> 00:26:35.026
and I was actually kind of offended

00:26:35.026 --> 00:26:38.029
that they would bring junk food to meet me

00:26:38.029 --> 00:26:39.397
as opposed to real Chinese food,

00:26:39.397 --> 00:26:42.567
but for them McDonald's
was the best of the best.

00:26:42.567 --> 00:26:45.003
It was all the prestige.

00:26:45.003 --> 00:26:47.372
Hey, to me, McDonald's,
when it comes to fast food,

00:26:47.372 --> 00:26:50.809
is No. 1 in the US, dare I say the world.

00:26:50.809 --> 00:26:52.544
If you just want a good hot meal

00:26:52.544 --> 00:26:54.079
where you know exactly what
it's going to taste like

00:26:54.079 --> 00:26:56.881
and get it and go, McDonald's never fails.

00:26:56.881 --> 00:26:58.817
Waiting in line, getting
it at the drive-through,

00:26:58.817 --> 00:27:00.118
you get it lickety-split.

00:27:00.118 --> 00:27:03.121
Now they leaned really big
into delivery since COVID,

00:27:03.121 --> 00:27:05.957
and, man, McDonald's is
showing up right away,

00:27:05.957 --> 00:27:08.126
and I love it. It's dangerous.

00:27:08.126 --> 00:27:08.960
I can't remember the last time

00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:10.929
I've eaten inside at a McDonald's.

00:27:10.929 --> 00:27:13.064
So, I usually dine in at McDonald's,

00:27:13.064 --> 00:27:16.201
but I find that in China
they focus more on delivery,

00:27:16.201 --> 00:27:17.969
and they promise to get
everything delivered

00:27:17.969 --> 00:27:20.872
within 30 minutes, which
they actually keep to,

00:27:20.872 --> 00:27:22.540
and that's incredibly impressive.

00:27:22.540 --> 00:27:24.709
Last night I ordered the chicken carcass.

00:27:24.709 --> 00:27:26.678
It took 28 minutes.

00:27:26.678 --> 00:27:28.880
Got a Big Mac earlier.
That was 10 minutes.

00:27:28.880 --> 00:27:31.116
So they're very, very punctual.

00:27:31.116 --> 00:27:33.051
They're also open for very long,

00:27:33.051 --> 00:27:34.819
from 7 till 10 p.m.,

00:27:34.819 --> 00:27:36.488
and there are many 24-hour branches,

00:27:36.488 --> 00:27:38.490
so extremely convenient.

00:27:38.490 --> 00:27:40.458
Now, McDonald's is an American brand,

00:27:40.458 --> 00:27:43.094
so they have American
classics on the menu,

00:27:43.094 --> 00:27:45.363
hamburgers, chicken sandwiches,

00:27:45.363 --> 00:27:48.266
but they kind of
assimilated and made popular

00:27:48.266 --> 00:27:49.968
the burger culture in this country.

00:27:49.968 --> 00:27:51.202
It's hard to say, because I feel like

00:27:51.202 --> 00:27:52.971
the American taste is McDonald's.

00:27:52.971 --> 00:27:54.673
I think McDonald's has actually adapted

00:27:54.673 --> 00:27:56.574
pretty well to Chinese tastes.

00:27:56.574 --> 00:27:59.177
Besides the McSpicy burger and wings

00:27:59.177 --> 00:28:00.879
and the grilled chicken sandwich,

00:28:00.879 --> 00:28:02.914
which have all become bestsellers,

00:28:02.914 --> 00:28:05.717
McDonald's actually
uses chicken thigh meat

00:28:05.717 --> 00:28:08.553
instead of breast meat in
all of its chicken burgers,

00:28:08.553 --> 00:28:10.088
except for the McChicken.

00:28:10.088 --> 00:28:11.723
And I think that's because Chinese people

00:28:11.723 --> 00:28:14.059
think chicken breast is dry,

00:28:14.059 --> 00:28:17.028
and they've also got lots
of time-limited specials

00:28:17.028 --> 00:28:20.899
when it comes to the desserts,
like the mantou burger,

00:28:20.899 --> 00:28:22.867
which is kind of like a Chinese bun,

00:28:22.867 --> 00:28:25.036
and even cilantro sundae.

00:28:25.036 --> 00:28:27.005
McDonald's, everyone's
going after McDonald's.

00:28:27.005 --> 00:28:28.573
Burger King's been going after McDonald's

00:28:28.573 --> 00:28:30.141
since, what, the '60s?

00:28:30.141 --> 00:28:31.443
Every burger chain

00:28:31.443 --> 00:28:34.579
try to get some sort
of edge on McDonald's.

00:28:34.579 --> 00:28:38.383
We're fancier, we got
different varieties of stuff.

00:28:38.383 --> 00:28:41.720
McDonald's is No. 1,
here, now, and forever.

00:28:41.720 --> 00:28:44.756
The McDonald's logo should be
on the American flag, dammit!

00:28:44.756 --> 00:28:48.093
So, China is McDonald's
second-largest market

00:28:48.093 --> 00:28:50.061
by store count, after the US.

00:28:50.061 --> 00:28:54.699
In China, there are over
5,000 McDonald's locations,

00:28:54.699 --> 00:28:57.969
but KFC has over 9,000.

00:28:57.969 --> 00:28:59.070
They actually came here first,

00:28:59.070 --> 00:29:02.107
so it's KFC, then McDonald's,

00:29:02.107 --> 00:29:04.442
then a local brand called Dicos,

00:29:04.442 --> 00:29:07.579
which does both fried chicken and burgers,

00:29:07.579 --> 00:29:10.348
so they're really just
fighting an uphill battle.

00:29:12.617 --> 00:29:15.553
In China, a Big Mac costs 25 yuan.

00:29:15.553 --> 00:29:18.289
A Big Mac in the US costs $5.29.

00:29:18.289 --> 00:29:19.324
Make it a Big Mac meal

00:29:19.324 --> 00:29:24.229
with a medium fries and
medium Coke, and it's 36 yuan.

00:29:24.229 --> 00:29:26.898
If you want to go large,
that's 4 yuan extra

00:29:26.898 --> 00:29:29.534
for a grand total of 40 yuan.

00:29:29.534 --> 00:29:30.368
If you make it a meal

00:29:30.368 --> 00:29:31.936
with a medium fries and medium drink,

00:29:31.936 --> 00:29:34.773
price goes up to $9.29.

00:29:34.773 --> 00:29:38.710
Upgrade that to a large, and it's $10.79.

00:29:38.710 --> 00:29:42.647
Our Big Mac large meal costs 86% more.

00:29:42.647 --> 00:29:44.783
So our Big Mac meal is cheaper,

00:29:44.783 --> 00:29:48.019
but at the same time
the average daily wage

00:29:48.019 --> 00:29:52.090
of a cabby in Beijing is
about 200 yuan, give or take,

00:29:52.090 --> 00:29:55.527
and so this would be 20% of their salary.

00:29:55.527 --> 00:29:56.995
So it's still not really something

00:29:56.995 --> 00:30:00.098
that you would eat on a regular
basis, but maybe splurge on.

00:30:02.400 --> 00:30:03.468
Let's talk nutrition.

00:30:03.468 --> 00:30:05.470
This is that very Big Mac, again.

00:30:05.470 --> 00:30:08.039
In the US, it's 590 calories

00:30:08.039 --> 00:30:09.474
and all this stuff.

00:30:09.474 --> 00:30:13.878
In China, our Big Mac has 524 calories,

00:30:13.878 --> 00:30:17.482
26 grams of fat, 45 grams of carbs,

00:30:17.482 --> 00:30:19.684
27 grams of protein,

00:30:19.684 --> 00:30:22.987
and 877 milligrams of sodium.

00:30:22.987 --> 00:30:24.322
What if we did a combo?

00:30:24.322 --> 00:30:26.958
Starting with the medium fries,

00:30:26.958 --> 00:30:29.360
this adds 320 calories to the meal,

00:30:29.360 --> 00:30:30.595
and all this stuff.

00:30:30.595 --> 00:30:34.599
While a medium fries in
China contains 290 calories,

00:30:34.599 --> 00:30:37.001
13 grams of total fat,

00:30:37.001 --> 00:30:40.004
35.9 grams of carbs,

00:30:40.004 --> 00:30:42.340
we're not sure if it contains any sugars,

00:30:42.340 --> 00:30:43.641
4 grams of protein,

00:30:43.641 --> 00:30:47.679
and 252 milligrams of sodium.

00:30:47.679 --> 00:30:49.314
But you need something to drink.

00:30:49.314 --> 00:30:50.748
Add in a medium Coke to that,

00:30:50.748 --> 00:30:54.452
and this kicks your meal
up another 210 calories.

00:30:54.452 --> 00:30:55.453
We'll do the same.

00:30:55.453 --> 00:30:58.256
Here's everything in a
medium Coke in China.

00:30:58.256 --> 00:31:01.526
148 calories. That leaves the grand total

00:31:01.526 --> 00:31:06.064
for the China meal at 962 calories.

00:31:06.064 --> 00:31:08.233
While in the US, the total
ends up looking like this.

00:31:08.233 --> 00:31:12.237
1,120 calories and all this other stuff.

00:31:12.237 --> 00:31:14.138
Get a load of that sodium, though.

00:31:14.138 --> 00:31:15.139
Guh!

00:31:15.306 --> 00:31:17.575
Tianran: From calorie
counts to portion sizes,

00:31:17.575 --> 00:31:19.244
we wanted to find all the differences

00:31:19.244 --> 00:31:22.480
between Domino's in China and in the US.

00:31:22.480 --> 00:31:24.148
This is "Food Wars."

00:31:27.151 --> 00:31:30.555
Here in China, Domino's
comes in three sizes:

00:31:30.555 --> 00:31:34.125
the 7-inch small, which is
only available for two pizzas,

00:31:34.125 --> 00:31:36.394
the fruit deluxe and the cocoa brownie,

00:31:36.394 --> 00:31:37.762
hand-tossed only;

00:31:37.762 --> 00:31:42.200
the 9-inch regular; and the 12-inch large.

00:31:42.200 --> 00:31:45.470
In the US, our Domino's
pizzas come in four sizes:

00:31:45.470 --> 00:31:48.907
small, 10-inch; medium, 12-inch;

00:31:48.907 --> 00:31:50.875
large, 14-inch;

00:31:50.875 --> 00:31:54.112
and the XL, 16 inches.

00:31:54.112 --> 00:31:56.014
No, there's nothing on your screen.

00:31:56.014 --> 00:31:58.149
The pizza is in fact that greasy.

00:32:00.218 --> 00:32:03.187
We have three types of crust,

00:32:03.187 --> 00:32:06.424
pan crust, hand-tossed,

00:32:06.424 --> 00:32:09.594
and the thin crust,

00:32:09.594 --> 00:32:13.231
and eight different crust
options, including stuffed crusts,

00:32:13.231 --> 00:32:15.633
which are only available
outside of the US.

00:32:15.633 --> 00:32:17.602
The UK has them. We have them.

00:32:17.602 --> 00:32:21.706
Sweet-potato-stuffed crust.

00:32:21.706 --> 00:32:22.674
You see that?

00:32:22.674 --> 00:32:24.275
The orangey bit in there.

00:32:26.611 --> 00:32:27.645
That's pretty good, actually.

00:32:27.645 --> 00:32:30.348
It reminds me a little bit of a mooncake

00:32:30.348 --> 00:32:32.383
in that it's sweet and savory.

00:32:33.885 --> 00:32:37.555
Stuffed sausage crust.

00:32:37.555 --> 00:32:40.124
Just a little sausage
peeking out of the hole.

00:32:40.124 --> 00:32:43.594
Boletus crust. And
basically it's a mushroom.

00:32:43.594 --> 00:32:45.697
It's a variety of mushroom,

00:32:45.697 --> 00:32:48.132
of which there are many different species.

00:32:48.132 --> 00:32:50.401
They're actually poisonous,

00:32:50.401 --> 00:32:51.936
so you need to cook them properly.

00:32:51.936 --> 00:32:55.006
If they're undercooked, they
will cause hallucinations.

00:32:55.006 --> 00:32:57.141
The mushroom seller I met,

00:32:57.141 --> 00:33:00.244
her husband actually
was poisoned four times,

00:33:00.244 --> 00:33:04.082
and once he saw a bunch of
skulls either side of him.

00:33:04.082 --> 00:33:06.484
Once he saw a mountain of gold.

00:33:06.484 --> 00:33:08.186
One other time he just beats up a fridge,

00:33:08.186 --> 00:33:10.254
and the last time he slept for three days.

00:33:15.293 --> 00:33:17.261
It just tastes like wet mushroom.

00:33:17.261 --> 00:33:19.097
Actually, we do have mushrooms

00:33:19.097 --> 00:33:20.698
that make you hallucinate
in the US as well,

00:33:20.698 --> 00:33:22.667
although you can't get them at Domino's.

00:33:22.667 --> 00:33:26.571
Salted-egg-yolk-stuffed crust.

00:33:26.571 --> 00:33:30.308
It's recommended that this is
paired with the chicken pizza,

00:33:30.308 --> 00:33:33.011
so you basically have the
whole family in there.

00:33:33.011 --> 00:33:33.978
That is delicious.

00:33:33.978 --> 00:33:37.515
It tastes like a million
calories. Such a guilty pleasure.

00:33:37.515 --> 00:33:38.549
Mm-hmm.

00:33:38.549 --> 00:33:42.053
The meat-floss-stuffed crust.

00:33:42.053 --> 00:33:44.389
It's not the most appetizing name, is it?

00:33:44.389 --> 00:33:47.225
It looks a little bit like lint,

00:33:47.225 --> 00:33:51.129
but it tastes like bacon cotton candy.

00:33:51.129 --> 00:33:53.031
Usually it's made of pork,

00:33:53.031 --> 00:33:56.601
but you can also get it as
beef or chicken or fish.

00:33:56.601 --> 00:33:58.436
I don't think it quite works in crust

00:33:58.436 --> 00:34:00.738
when crust is already so dry.

00:34:00.738 --> 00:34:03.741
We also have something
called the double decker thin

00:34:03.741 --> 00:34:06.144
and the double decker thick.

00:34:06.144 --> 00:34:07.011
Correct me if I'm wrong.

00:34:07.011 --> 00:34:10.515
I think this is actually the
double decadence from the UK.

00:34:12.383 --> 00:34:15.186
I mean, it is pretty
much a pizza sandwich.

00:34:15.186 --> 00:34:19.957
US Domino's, we have five
different dough varieties.

00:34:19.957 --> 00:34:22.760
A better way of saying that is
five different crust options.

00:34:22.760 --> 00:34:24.996
Dough varieties, yeah, same thing.

00:34:24.996 --> 00:34:27.331
Anyway, first one down here
is a gluten-free crust,

00:34:27.331 --> 00:34:29.667
and I want to note that it
only comes in the small,

00:34:29.667 --> 00:34:31.202
because from Domino's perspective,

00:34:31.202 --> 00:34:33.571
if you want gluten-free pizza,
you're eating it by yourself.

00:34:33.571 --> 00:34:36.374
Next is the hand-tossed, kind
of the classic style, right?

00:34:36.374 --> 00:34:37.542
Everyone's seen the hand-tossed.

00:34:37.542 --> 00:34:39.811
To me, it's the default setting.

00:34:39.811 --> 00:34:42.814
After that, this is the
crunchy thin, cut into squares.

00:34:42.814 --> 00:34:45.650
That's a tavern cut, for
all you in the Midwest.

00:34:45.650 --> 00:34:49.587
Another crust/dough variety is the pan.

00:34:49.587 --> 00:34:51.923
This is a thick boy.
Only comes in a medium.

00:34:51.923 --> 00:34:54.659
And, of course, the last
one is the Brooklyn style,

00:34:54.659 --> 00:34:56.828
which you can only get in
the large or the extra large,

00:34:56.828 --> 00:35:00.631
and it's thin and also has
these really big slices.

00:35:00.631 --> 00:35:02.300
I can't tell. That's eight slices, right?

00:35:02.300 --> 00:35:03.367
No, six slices, right?

00:35:03.367 --> 00:35:04.569
So, it should be eight.

00:35:04.569 --> 00:35:06.070
I don't know. Can someone in post

00:35:06.070 --> 00:35:08.306
increase the contrast on that

00:35:08.306 --> 00:35:10.608
to maybe make the lines
a little more obvious?

00:35:13.077 --> 00:35:17.181
Our Domino's largest pizza
has a diameter of 12 inches,

00:35:17.181 --> 00:35:19.750
or 30.5 centimeters,

00:35:19.750 --> 00:35:21.185
and an area of

00:35:21.185 --> 00:35:25.022
730.6 centimeters squared

00:35:25.022 --> 00:35:29.861
and costs 88 yuan, or 12.81 USD.

00:35:29.861 --> 00:35:33.731
Breaking that down, our pizza is 0.11 yuan

00:35:33.731 --> 00:35:35.533
per square centimeter.

00:35:35.533 --> 00:35:40.171
Take our large 14-inch, or
35.56-centimeter, pizza,

00:35:40.171 --> 00:35:44.475
with an area of 993.1 square centimeters.

00:35:44.475 --> 00:35:48.045
That's 0.15 cents per square centimeter,

00:35:48.045 --> 00:35:51.015
or 0.96 yuan.

00:35:51.015 --> 00:35:53.284
That means our US Domino's
pizza per square inch

00:35:53.284 --> 00:35:56.587
is roughly 12.5% cheaper than in China.

00:35:58.689 --> 00:36:02.393
Our Domino's categorizes their
pizzas into three groups,

00:36:02.393 --> 00:36:05.596
indulgent, classic, and value.

00:36:05.596 --> 00:36:09.133
Let's take a look at the indulgent first.

00:36:09.133 --> 00:36:13.437
French-style liver mousse ham pizza.

00:36:13.437 --> 00:36:15.873
I'm not even sure what a liver mousse is.

00:36:15.873 --> 00:36:17.808
I assume it's meant to be foie gras.

00:36:17.808 --> 00:36:19.577
It smells like foie gras.

00:36:22.580 --> 00:36:26.317
Oh, but it is weird with pizza, man.

00:36:26.317 --> 00:36:28.019
No, that should not be eaten with pizza.

00:36:28.019 --> 00:36:29.487
That is super weird.

00:36:29.487 --> 00:36:30.321
Why?

00:36:30.321 --> 00:36:31.923
Mm, no.

00:36:31.923 --> 00:36:34.892
Let's grab some New Zealand lamb.

00:36:36.694 --> 00:36:40.264
It may be New Zealand lamb,
but they've used a lot of cumin

00:36:40.264 --> 00:36:42.533
and basically turned
it into a lamb skewer.

00:36:42.533 --> 00:36:45.102
Definitely miles better after that.

00:36:45.102 --> 00:36:48.372
The sultan durian pizza.

00:36:48.372 --> 00:36:52.777
That is a really healthy,
big piece of durian.

00:36:52.777 --> 00:36:57.048
Abalone and scallop indulgent pizza.

00:36:57.048 --> 00:36:58.115
I mean, just why?

00:36:58.115 --> 00:37:01.852
Abalone is super expensive,
and it's popular in China

00:37:01.852 --> 00:37:05.356
because its name sounds like
"to get explosively rich,"

00:37:05.356 --> 00:37:07.592
so you'll often find
it served at weddings,

00:37:07.592 --> 00:37:08.726
at Chinese New Year.

00:37:12.730 --> 00:37:13.764
Ugh.

00:37:13.764 --> 00:37:14.732
Let's clean our palate.

00:37:14.732 --> 00:37:18.569
We'll get some Australian/New
Zealand wagyu beef.

00:37:20.571 --> 00:37:22.373
I'd eat the beef by itself.

00:37:22.373 --> 00:37:24.308
I'd remove everything else.

00:37:24.308 --> 00:37:27.078
Crayfish and chicken.

00:37:27.078 --> 00:37:30.214
I think they've gone full NOLA here,

00:37:30.214 --> 00:37:33.150
because the chicken are
meant to be Orlean chicken,

00:37:33.150 --> 00:37:35.653
and then we've got them craw daddies, too.

00:37:35.653 --> 00:37:36.887
Chicken and crawdads?

00:37:36.887 --> 00:37:38.322
I love New Orleans food,

00:37:38.322 --> 00:37:40.124
so yeah, I would
definitely try that pizza.

00:37:40.124 --> 00:37:43.060
South American rib eye steak.

00:37:43.060 --> 00:37:47.098
The burdock prawn bacon indulgent pizza.

00:37:47.098 --> 00:37:48.699
We've got peas, we've got prawns,

00:37:48.699 --> 00:37:50.201
we've got some cherry tomatoes.

00:37:50.201 --> 00:37:52.637
This is the Japanese-style-eel pizza,

00:37:52.637 --> 00:37:55.973
and on the description, it actually says,

00:37:55.973 --> 00:37:59.844
"May contain soft bones. Eat with care."

00:38:01.712 --> 00:38:02.947
Oh, they're very tasty, though.

00:38:02.947 --> 00:38:06.951
Here we have the Australian/South American

00:38:06.951 --> 00:38:10.054
grain-fed diced beef, so
they either weren't sure

00:38:10.054 --> 00:38:11.789
where the beef was sourced from

00:38:11.789 --> 00:38:14.358
or if they run out of beef from Australia,

00:38:14.358 --> 00:38:15.626
they go to South America.

00:38:15.626 --> 00:38:20.231
And over here we have a
pineapple shrimp pizza.

00:38:20.231 --> 00:38:23.234
You know, for those of you
who hate Hawaiian pizzas,

00:38:23.234 --> 00:38:25.936
this must be so much more triggering.

00:38:25.936 --> 00:38:28.339
No. I think it's actually
worse than a Hawaiian.

00:38:28.339 --> 00:38:33.210
Also in the indulgent lineup
is our regular durian pizza.

00:38:33.210 --> 00:38:34.812
This is actually a best seller.

00:38:34.812 --> 00:38:38.149
It costs 9 yuan less than the sultan.

00:38:38.149 --> 00:38:40.618
Oh, yeah. No, that's great.

00:38:40.618 --> 00:38:43.287
Mm. Oh, that's delicious.

00:38:43.287 --> 00:38:46.357
Here we have the
okonomiyaki surf and turf.

00:38:46.357 --> 00:38:47.925
Look at that. That's
actually pretty decent.

00:38:47.925 --> 00:38:50.961
It's even got the furikake intact.

00:38:50.961 --> 00:38:54.799
Look at that. These
little superthin flakes.

00:38:54.799 --> 00:38:55.900
Mm, that's decent.

00:38:55.900 --> 00:38:58.135
Well done. Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:38:58.135 --> 00:38:59.236
Very meaty, too.

00:38:59.236 --> 00:39:03.641
Bacon, meat floss, potato pizza,

00:39:03.641 --> 00:39:08.512
and it is absolutely
blanketed in meat floss

00:39:08.512 --> 00:39:11.315
and a gigantic potato wedge.

00:39:11.315 --> 00:39:13.784
It's a little bit like the Hawaiian pizza,

00:39:13.784 --> 00:39:16.354
except instead of a juicy pineapple

00:39:16.354 --> 00:39:20.491
you have sweet
bacon-flavored cotton candy.

00:39:20.491 --> 00:39:21.926
Mm, not sure if like.

00:39:21.926 --> 00:39:24.628
The Domino's US menu
obviously is not as robust

00:39:24.628 --> 00:39:26.797
as China's Domino's menu,

00:39:26.797 --> 00:39:29.033
but there are some specialty
pizzas you can get here

00:39:29.033 --> 00:39:31.902
that you can't get there, including these.

00:39:31.902 --> 00:39:36.874
First one here is the
Extravagan, two capital Z's, a.

00:39:36.874 --> 00:39:39.377
This looks like a rebranding
of what would be called

00:39:39.377 --> 00:39:40.945
a supreme pizza here. Right?

00:39:40.945 --> 00:39:43.414
Now, if you hate vegetables, don't worry.

00:39:43.414 --> 00:39:46.517
You can get the same pizza
but just MeatZZa version.

00:39:46.517 --> 00:39:49.987
We got sausage, ham,

00:39:49.987 --> 00:39:52.523
pepperoni, possibly hamburger.

00:39:53.924 --> 00:39:56.060
This could have been just a
sausage and pepperoni pizza,

00:39:56.060 --> 00:39:58.195
and it probably would've tasted
the same. I'm just saying.

00:39:58.195 --> 00:39:59.029
Philly cheesesteak.

00:39:59.029 --> 00:40:01.198
Philadelphia, let us know in the comments

00:40:01.198 --> 00:40:04.535
how insulted you are that the
sandwich that bears your name

00:40:04.535 --> 00:40:07.872
is now in pizza form. And
this thing looks terrifying.

00:40:07.872 --> 00:40:10.274
Steak, cheese. Like that.

00:40:10.274 --> 00:40:13.511
Onion and green pepper, oh, and mushrooms.

00:40:15.379 --> 00:40:16.213
Yeah, I mean, it's not bad.

00:40:16.213 --> 00:40:17.381
I don't know if I want a
whole thing of this, though.

00:40:17.381 --> 00:40:18.649
I already had just one bite,
I'm like, yeah, I got it.

00:40:18.649 --> 00:40:19.850
It's more the novelty of, yeah,

00:40:19.850 --> 00:40:21.485
I guess that does taste
like a Philly cheesesteak,

00:40:21.485 --> 00:40:23.754
but also, now I gotta
eat this whole pizza.

00:40:23.754 --> 00:40:24.588
Hm.

00:40:24.588 --> 00:40:27.124
A Cali chicken bacon ranch,

00:40:27.124 --> 00:40:29.927
which I'm going to go ahead and assume is,

00:40:29.927 --> 00:40:30.828
what do you think?

00:40:30.828 --> 00:40:34.064
Chicken, bacon, some sort of ranch.

00:40:34.064 --> 00:40:35.933
I don't know what makes it California.

00:40:37.668 --> 00:40:39.036
That's not bad.

00:40:39.036 --> 00:40:40.037
Buffalo chicken.

00:40:40.037 --> 00:40:43.240
In China, they had all
these really interesting

00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:46.243
flavor combinations that
I'm sure someone was just

00:40:46.243 --> 00:40:50.581
really trying to capture the
breadth of Chinese tastes.

00:40:50.581 --> 00:40:52.349
Here, everything is like,

00:40:52.349 --> 00:40:55.319
this exists somewhere else.
We just did a pizza form.

00:40:55.319 --> 00:40:57.054
Case in point, Buffalo chicken.

00:40:57.054 --> 00:40:58.255
Hey, do you like wings?

00:40:58.255 --> 00:40:59.089
Yeah.

00:40:59.089 --> 00:41:00.658
Do you want it in pizza form?

00:41:00.658 --> 00:41:01.592
No.

00:41:01.592 --> 00:41:03.661
Too bad. Buffalo chicken.

00:41:03.661 --> 00:41:06.197
Another one here, spinach and feta.

00:41:07.198 --> 00:41:08.065
No.

00:41:08.065 --> 00:41:11.735
Because I just bit into
a thing of feta cheese.

00:41:11.735 --> 00:41:12.570
No.

00:41:12.570 --> 00:41:14.872
Another specialty pizza we
have exclusive to the US

00:41:14.872 --> 00:41:17.541
and not in China is a
Wisconsin six-cheese,

00:41:17.541 --> 00:41:20.344
which, assuming from the name, has,

00:41:20.344 --> 00:41:22.413
let me go ahead and guess, six cheeses?

00:41:22.413 --> 00:41:23.481
And they put Wisconsin on there

00:41:23.481 --> 00:41:25.082
because Wisconsin is the cheese state.

00:41:25.082 --> 00:41:26.217
Shout-out to Wisconsin.

00:41:26.217 --> 00:41:29.119
On to our classic offerings,

00:41:29.119 --> 00:41:32.556
beginning with the
salted-egg-yolk-flavored chicken,

00:41:32.556 --> 00:41:35.626
which, as you can see, was
very welcomed by the crew.

00:41:35.626 --> 00:41:37.428
We're already missing two pieces.

00:41:37.428 --> 00:41:40.698
The Chinese name for this is golden sands,

00:41:40.698 --> 00:41:45.336
which is a specific way of
cooking the salted egg yolk

00:41:45.336 --> 00:41:49.039
so that it becomes a sort of frothy paste

00:41:49.039 --> 00:41:51.442
that can be used to coat various things.

00:41:51.442 --> 00:41:54.812
It's a salty, sweet umaminess.

00:41:54.812 --> 00:41:57.348
Teriyaki beef potato pizza.

00:41:57.348 --> 00:41:58.916
Teriyaki beef, yes.

00:41:58.916 --> 00:42:01.919
The pizza itself is already quite starchy.

00:42:01.919 --> 00:42:04.989
It's all carbs, and then
a potato on top of that.

00:42:04.989 --> 00:42:06.524
It's a staple and a staple.

00:42:07.825 --> 00:42:09.894
Most of these pizzas are sweet.

00:42:09.894 --> 00:42:11.662
Peking duck pizza.

00:42:12.596 --> 00:42:13.797
I'm very conflicted about this.

00:42:13.797 --> 00:42:15.566
I like that they're representing us,

00:42:15.566 --> 00:42:20.571
but this looks very blasphemous to me.

00:42:20.638 --> 00:42:21.739
That actually sounds amazing.

00:42:23.507 --> 00:42:26.010
Nope, nope, nope, nope.

00:42:26.010 --> 00:42:27.444
Blasphemous. No.

00:42:27.444 --> 00:42:28.712
OK, never mind.

00:42:28.712 --> 00:42:29.747
I'd still try it, though.

00:42:29.747 --> 00:42:32.983
Here we've got the tuna seafood deluxe.

00:42:32.983 --> 00:42:35.319
Not that big a fan of
seafood pizza, myself.

00:42:35.319 --> 00:42:39.657
Truffle-flavored sauce,
mushroom, and chicken pizza.

00:42:39.657 --> 00:42:41.892
Two types of mushrooms in that pizza,

00:42:41.892 --> 00:42:45.563
but note that the truffle
is a flavored sauce,

00:42:45.563 --> 00:42:49.533
so that's not included as one
of the types of mushrooms.

00:42:49.533 --> 00:42:51.735
Ah, no.

00:42:51.735 --> 00:42:53.504
Normal pizza, yes.

00:42:53.504 --> 00:42:54.838
Chorizo pizza.

00:42:54.838 --> 00:42:57.741
I don't know why there's
peas on all of the pizza,

00:42:57.741 --> 00:43:01.478
but look, I'm gonna take it
for just regular meat toppings.

00:43:01.478 --> 00:43:03.747
Yes, chorizo, get in here!

00:43:05.916 --> 00:43:09.520
Tastes like Bolognese sauce,
but it's OK. I can dig it.

00:43:09.520 --> 00:43:11.889
Especially after all of this
stuff, I'll take anything.

00:43:11.889 --> 00:43:15.092
And now our value options,

00:43:15.092 --> 00:43:18.228
beginning with the Texas barbecue.

00:43:18.228 --> 00:43:21.498
Now, the description says it has

00:43:21.498 --> 00:43:24.001
Texas-style meat.

00:43:24.001 --> 00:43:26.103
I assume it's ham.

00:43:26.103 --> 00:43:29.206
Again, it's sweet, but here
since it's a barbecue sauce,

00:43:29.206 --> 00:43:30.808
maybe a honey glaze, I'm OK with that.

00:43:30.808 --> 00:43:32.776
The lychee chicken pizza.

00:43:32.776 --> 00:43:34.478
Don't know why it's paired up like that.

00:43:34.478 --> 00:43:37.648
This is actually a pretty
meme-errific pizza.

00:43:37.648 --> 00:43:40.451
The name is very punny,

00:43:40.451 --> 00:43:45.456
and it references a
middle-aged Chinese influencer

00:43:45.456 --> 00:43:48.092
who screams at the top of his lungs,

00:43:48.092 --> 00:43:50.027
"Aoligei!"

00:43:50.027 --> 00:43:53.297
Which kind of just
translates to, "Come on."

00:43:53.297 --> 00:43:55.432
Many times people have said

00:43:55.432 --> 00:43:58.302
that I kind of look like
that guy, and it's just,

00:43:58.302 --> 00:43:59.536
I don't know what they're talking about.

00:43:59.536 --> 00:44:01.205
There's no resemblance whatsoever.

00:44:01.205 --> 00:44:02.306
Aoligei!

00:44:04.675 --> 00:44:06.243
All I taste is the lychee.

00:44:06.243 --> 00:44:08.145
The potato bacon pizza.

00:44:08.145 --> 00:44:11.915
This is one of Domino's
all-time bestsellers,

00:44:11.915 --> 00:44:15.319
and the name in Chinese
actually says "American style."

00:44:15.319 --> 00:44:18.722
I don't know, is this what
you guys eat over in yonder?

00:44:19.723 --> 00:44:20.524
Nope.

00:44:20.524 --> 00:44:21.358
Here we go.

00:44:21.358 --> 00:44:25.863
Here's a taste of America.
Mm-hmm. Land of the free.

00:44:27.931 --> 00:44:28.899
Who am I to judge?

00:44:28.899 --> 00:44:31.368
I don't know what kind of potato wedges

00:44:31.368 --> 00:44:33.570
Americans like to put on their pizza.

00:44:33.570 --> 00:44:35.706
Korean-style fried chicken,

00:44:35.706 --> 00:44:39.443
also with sesame seeds, seaweed,

00:44:39.443 --> 00:44:42.880
marinara sauce, and
what looks like onions.

00:44:45.349 --> 00:44:47.251
Hey, that's a winner.

00:44:47.251 --> 00:44:48.852
Winner, winner, chicken dinner.

00:44:48.852 --> 00:44:50.954
Veggie deluxe. Not touching it.

00:44:50.954 --> 00:44:52.890
Over here we have something special.

00:44:52.890 --> 00:44:56.393
These are our two smallest
pizzas, the 7-inchers.

00:44:56.393 --> 00:44:59.530
This is the fruit deluxe.

00:44:59.530 --> 00:45:03.801
Peach, blueberry jam,
pineapple, coconut gel.

00:45:05.302 --> 00:45:06.737
Mm!

00:45:06.737 --> 00:45:07.805
You know what's best?

00:45:07.805 --> 00:45:09.306
It's actually meant to be sweet.

00:45:09.306 --> 00:45:10.808
If I've tried one dessert pizza,

00:45:10.808 --> 00:45:11.775
I'm going to try the other one,

00:45:11.775 --> 00:45:14.945
the cocoa-flavored-brownie pizza

00:45:14.945 --> 00:45:18.782
with brownie cubes and cocoa powder.

00:45:18.782 --> 00:45:20.317
It's actually not so bad.

00:45:20.317 --> 00:45:23.053
It reminds me a little bit

00:45:23.053 --> 00:45:26.323
of Nutella on buttered toast.

00:45:26.323 --> 00:45:27.891
I can dig it.

00:45:27.891 --> 00:45:28.892
Still here.

00:45:28.892 --> 00:45:30.561
Man, that's a lot of pizza.

00:45:30.561 --> 00:45:32.663
We at the US Domino's have sandwiches,

00:45:32.663 --> 00:45:34.431
specifically these seven.

00:45:34.431 --> 00:45:38.168
Most of them are just versions of pizza

00:45:38.168 --> 00:45:39.369
that are also in sandwich form,

00:45:39.369 --> 00:45:41.004
first one being the Buffalo chicken.

00:45:41.004 --> 00:45:42.072
Let's get a look in there.

00:45:42.072 --> 00:45:43.974
The chicken, cheese, and the sauce.

00:45:43.974 --> 00:45:45.275
The chicken habanero.

00:45:45.275 --> 00:45:46.276
I like a habanero thing

00:45:46.276 --> 00:45:47.911
because it has the sweet and the spicy,

00:45:47.911 --> 00:45:52.683
pineapple and jalapeños,
together in one bite.

00:45:52.683 --> 00:45:55.419
This one, bleh, Mediterranean veggie.

00:45:55.419 --> 00:45:57.020
Feta cheese and spinach.

00:45:57.020 --> 00:45:59.089
That's in the Mediterranean area, I guess.

00:45:59.089 --> 00:46:02.626
Banana peppers, which I don't
think exist outside of the US.

00:46:02.626 --> 00:46:04.895
Oh, the Philly cheesesteak. Ugh.

00:46:04.895 --> 00:46:07.131
It's double depressing because, I mean,

00:46:07.131 --> 00:46:09.433
the Philly cheesesteak is a sandwich.

00:46:09.433 --> 00:46:10.834
It has a specific way of being made.

00:46:10.834 --> 00:46:13.003
This is not what a Philly cheesesteak

00:46:13.003 --> 00:46:15.405
is supposed to look
like. Why do this? Right?

00:46:15.405 --> 00:46:18.442
Over here we got the chicken bacon ranch.

00:46:18.442 --> 00:46:20.544
Bro, they were generous with the ranch.

00:46:20.544 --> 00:46:21.645
Look at that.

00:46:21.645 --> 00:46:24.314
Lots of bacon and chicken and the cheese.

00:46:24.314 --> 00:46:25.349
Nice.

00:46:25.349 --> 00:46:28.519
An Italian sandwich. Mamma mia.

00:46:28.519 --> 00:46:32.389
Salami, cheese, ham, and another salami.

00:46:32.389 --> 00:46:36.527
And, of course, what is more Italian than

00:46:36.527 --> 00:46:38.362
banana peppers?

00:46:38.362 --> 00:46:40.197
And the chicken Parm
sandwich, chicken Parmesan,

00:46:40.197 --> 00:46:44.535
which is, again, an incredibly popular,

00:46:44.535 --> 00:46:46.537
already well-established sandwich

00:46:46.537 --> 00:46:48.172
that Domino's for some reason

00:46:48.172 --> 00:46:50.174
felt they needed to deconstruct

00:46:50.174 --> 00:46:52.309
and then reconstruct in a different way.

00:46:52.309 --> 00:46:54.144
I don't want any of these.

00:46:54.144 --> 00:46:55.579
No sandwiches here in China,

00:46:55.579 --> 00:46:58.582
but what we do have is rib eye steak.

00:46:59.583 --> 00:47:00.784
Waiter!

00:47:08.525 --> 00:47:11.862
Oh, whoa!

00:47:11.862 --> 00:47:13.864
That's a big piece of steak.

00:47:15.632 --> 00:47:16.767
Hm.

00:47:21.438 --> 00:47:23.407
Let's talk pasta and rice.

00:47:23.407 --> 00:47:24.408
We have both!

00:47:24.408 --> 00:47:26.677
Here are our pasta options.

00:47:26.677 --> 00:47:28.078
All come with spaghetti,

00:47:28.078 --> 00:47:32.449
or you can pay one extra
yuan to upgrade to penne.

00:47:32.449 --> 00:47:35.118
Spag Bol. Looks decent. Smells good.

00:47:35.118 --> 00:47:37.387
Lot of Bolognese on the pasta.

00:47:37.387 --> 00:47:39.590
Spaghetti basil.

00:47:39.590 --> 00:47:42.793
I'm pretty sure that's just a carbonara.

00:47:42.793 --> 00:47:47.497
Here we've got a seafood pasta
with scallop and squid roe.

00:47:47.497 --> 00:47:48.899
Here we've got the rice options.

00:47:48.899 --> 00:47:50.601
Chorizo baked rice.

00:47:50.601 --> 00:47:53.303
You've got some chorizo,
you've got some pepperoni.

00:47:53.303 --> 00:47:56.840
Truffle-flavored baked rice
with chicken and bacon.

00:47:56.840 --> 00:47:58.842
Not gonna touch that.
Don't like my truffles.

00:47:58.842 --> 00:48:02.379
And just a nice wholesome curry beef rice.

00:48:02.379 --> 00:48:05.515
Curry sauce, beef, rice.

00:48:05.515 --> 00:48:06.717
What could go wrong?

00:48:06.717 --> 00:48:10.254
No rice dishes in the US, but
we do have our own pastas,

00:48:10.254 --> 00:48:11.521
four specifically.

00:48:11.521 --> 00:48:15.459
This is the fourth Domino's "Food Wars"

00:48:15.459 --> 00:48:17.094
that I have been a part of.

00:48:17.094 --> 00:48:21.999
I want to again state that I
think the pastas at Domino's

00:48:21.999 --> 00:48:24.201
are an absolute abomination.

00:48:24.201 --> 00:48:26.503
So if you're watching from outside the US

00:48:26.503 --> 00:48:29.806
and you think this looks
weird, you are correct.

00:48:29.806 --> 00:48:33.076
This pasta is so weird!

00:48:33.076 --> 00:48:35.679
Italian sausage marinara.

00:48:35.679 --> 00:48:37.748
I mean, I can't even break
through the skin of this thing.

00:48:37.748 --> 00:48:39.082
Come on, man.

00:48:39.082 --> 00:48:40.784
Chicken carbonara.

00:48:40.784 --> 00:48:42.352
Ugh.

00:48:42.352 --> 00:48:43.987
Oh, it hurts my soul.

00:48:43.987 --> 00:48:46.456
Ugh! Pasta primavera.

00:48:46.456 --> 00:48:49.660
Whatever primavera means, it ain't this.

00:48:49.660 --> 00:48:54.564
And last, chicken Alfredo. Ugh.

00:48:54.564 --> 00:48:55.999
Both countries have wings.

00:48:55.999 --> 00:49:00.137
In China, you can only get
your wings in orders of four,

00:49:00.137 --> 00:49:03.040
unless you go for the wings combo.

00:49:03.040 --> 00:49:06.610
Now, here we have four exclusive flavors.

00:49:06.610 --> 00:49:08.645
Cantonese roast.

00:49:08.645 --> 00:49:11.915
Sweet in a fruity sort of sweetness,

00:49:11.915 --> 00:49:14.785
and you've got that barbecue smell.

00:49:15.786 --> 00:49:17.688
It tastes like Chinatown.

00:49:17.688 --> 00:49:20.924
Next we have the Orleans flavor.

00:49:20.924 --> 00:49:23.260
Oh, it's very spicy. Wow.

00:49:24.461 --> 00:49:27.764
Oh. Oh, my gosh.

00:49:27.764 --> 00:49:31.501
We also have the honey and
the barbecue-flavored wings,

00:49:31.501 --> 00:49:33.670
and I believe in the US
you just have them combined

00:49:33.670 --> 00:49:34.838
as a honey barbecue,

00:49:34.838 --> 00:49:37.607
but here we get an extra flavor out of it.

00:49:37.607 --> 00:49:39.743
I'm sure some of you might have noticed

00:49:39.743 --> 00:49:42.446
our wings look a little bit different.

00:49:42.446 --> 00:49:46.016
A wing is made up of three parts,

00:49:46.016 --> 00:49:50.120
the drum, the flat, and the tip.

00:49:50.120 --> 00:49:53.290
Usually it's removed because
it doesn't have much meat,

00:49:53.290 --> 00:49:55.392
but here in China we love fiddly food.

00:49:55.392 --> 00:49:58.929
Basically, here in China,
we love the tip so much

00:49:58.929 --> 00:50:03.033
that we even have an
entire dish devoted to

00:50:03.033 --> 00:50:04.334
just the tip.

00:50:05.369 --> 00:50:06.903
One thing I do love on the menu, though,

00:50:06.903 --> 00:50:09.206
is the Domino's wings.

00:50:09.206 --> 00:50:13.543
In the US, you can get wing
orders in eight, 16, or 32.

00:50:13.543 --> 00:50:16.213
We only have four exclusive flavors,

00:50:16.213 --> 00:50:18.849
starting down here at the hot.

00:50:18.849 --> 00:50:23.153
Then the honey barbecue,
sweet mango habanero,

00:50:23.153 --> 00:50:24.955
and last, the garlic Parmesan.

00:50:24.955 --> 00:50:27.824
On the presentation,
this is especially hm,

00:50:27.824 --> 00:50:29.092
but they are very good.

00:50:29.092 --> 00:50:30.527
I mean, I'd still get pizza over wings,

00:50:30.527 --> 00:50:33.196
but if you're going to get wing sides,

00:50:33.196 --> 00:50:34.965
Domino's wings, not bad.

00:50:34.965 --> 00:50:37.401
We also have roast skewers.

00:50:37.401 --> 00:50:40.570
Now, these are something that
are popular street foods.

00:50:40.570 --> 00:50:44.074
Here we've got some chicken satay skewers.

00:50:44.074 --> 00:50:45.609
We've got beef skewers.

00:50:45.609 --> 00:50:50.013
These also come in the lamb
version, incredibly delicious,

00:50:50.013 --> 00:50:52.983
and also

00:50:52.983 --> 00:50:55.118
roast sausages.

00:50:55.118 --> 00:50:57.521
I think these are usually
what kids like to eat.

00:50:57.521 --> 00:50:59.756
I don't usually see adults eating these.

00:50:59.756 --> 00:51:03.460
These would be sweet sausages,
but they're very filling.

00:51:03.460 --> 00:51:07.431
China also has seafood options,
namely our golden shrimp,

00:51:07.431 --> 00:51:09.633
which actually look a little bit orange,

00:51:09.633 --> 00:51:13.070
pollock bites, and regular fish bites.

00:51:13.070 --> 00:51:16.206
Our other sides include chicken rolls.

00:51:16.206 --> 00:51:20.977
I believe it's smoked chicken,
mayo, and egg and peas.

00:51:20.977 --> 00:51:23.814
Those peas. Peas make it
into every single menu item

00:51:23.814 --> 00:51:24.948
here at Domino's.

00:51:24.948 --> 00:51:28.752
Mini hot dogs wrapped
in a very cute blanket.

00:51:28.752 --> 00:51:31.188
It's almost like it outgrew its blanket.

00:51:31.188 --> 00:51:34.791
Healthy salad, star-shaped hash browns,

00:51:34.791 --> 00:51:38.328
onion rings, and potato wedges.

00:51:38.328 --> 00:51:39.763
Both countries have garlic bread,

00:51:39.763 --> 00:51:41.665
but ours, we do it a little differently.

00:51:41.665 --> 00:51:43.834
Ours is stuffed with
cheese and other stuff.

00:51:43.834 --> 00:51:45.669
For instance, this one right here,

00:51:45.669 --> 00:51:49.139
jalapeño and bacon.

00:51:49.139 --> 00:51:51.708
Why this over pizza?

00:51:51.708 --> 00:51:56.113
Another one we have here
is the spinach and feta.

00:51:56.113 --> 00:51:58.081
We have twists. We have bites.

00:51:58.081 --> 00:52:02.819
Starting over here, we've got
the Parmesan bread twists.

00:52:02.819 --> 00:52:04.888
Looks like it's kind of doing this,

00:52:04.888 --> 00:52:07.057
like please don't give me diarrhea.

00:52:07.057 --> 00:52:09.292
[toilet flushing]

00:52:09.292 --> 00:52:10.527
Garlic bread twists.

00:52:11.928 --> 00:52:13.830
Do you want this taking
up space in your stomach?

00:52:13.830 --> 00:52:14.664
I don't.

00:52:14.664 --> 00:52:16.099
Just get more pizza.

00:52:16.099 --> 00:52:18.201
I mentioned it before. We got dips.

00:52:18.201 --> 00:52:19.035
What are dips?

00:52:19.035 --> 00:52:22.572
From what I can tell, just big portions

00:52:22.572 --> 00:52:24.741
of something to dip these breads in.

00:52:24.741 --> 00:52:27.410
First one is, oh, my good Lord.

00:52:27.410 --> 00:52:29.546
Going to go ahead and assume
this is the five-cheese.

00:52:29.546 --> 00:52:32.782
Look at that, Yuelei.
Look at the oil on this.

00:52:32.782 --> 00:52:33.617
Ugh.

00:52:37.687 --> 00:52:38.588
You know what it tastes like?

00:52:38.588 --> 00:52:41.424
Like pizza, but without the sauce.

00:52:41.424 --> 00:52:43.860
And not to be outdone,
looks like the cheese one,

00:52:43.860 --> 00:52:47.330
but this one, you guessed it, has

00:52:49.366 --> 00:52:50.767
marinara sauce.

00:52:50.767 --> 00:52:54.571
So if you got sick of having bread

00:52:54.571 --> 00:52:56.740
with the sauce and cheese on it,

00:52:56.740 --> 00:52:59.075
you can just get the
sauce and cheese baked

00:52:59.075 --> 00:53:00.977
and then the bread baked separately

00:53:00.977 --> 00:53:03.346
and just dip them!

00:53:03.346 --> 00:53:04.781
Who wants this instead of pizza?

00:53:04.781 --> 00:53:06.183
I don't understand, but all right.

00:53:06.183 --> 00:53:10.453
We have square garlic
bread and garlic bread.

00:53:10.453 --> 00:53:12.088
I actually don't know
what the difference is

00:53:12.088 --> 00:53:13.356
besides the shape,

00:53:13.356 --> 00:53:16.660
but they both come with
this honey mayo dip.

00:53:16.660 --> 00:53:19.095
I actually thought this was mustard.

00:53:21.198 --> 00:53:23.433
I think it's mustard, mayo, and honey.

00:53:23.433 --> 00:53:25.902
I think the bread is just
an excuse to eat this dip,

00:53:25.902 --> 00:53:27.504
because it is actually pretty good.

00:53:27.504 --> 00:53:29.806
We also have soups.

00:53:29.806 --> 00:53:34.344
You can get a nice bowl
of pumpkin cream bacon,

00:53:34.344 --> 00:53:38.848
classic borscht, or
cream of mushroom soup.

00:53:38.848 --> 00:53:39.749
Desserts.

00:53:39.749 --> 00:53:42.786
Unfortunately, both China
and the US have lava cakes,

00:53:42.786 --> 00:53:44.187
so it is not exclusive,

00:53:44.187 --> 00:53:46.323
but we have a couple things
that you can't get in China,

00:53:46.323 --> 00:53:50.126
specifically these cinnamon bread twists

00:53:50.126 --> 00:53:53.730
and the Domino's marbled cookie brownie.

00:53:53.730 --> 00:53:55.498
Come on, who doesn't like brownies?

00:53:55.498 --> 00:53:57.901
And you can tell they put a
little cookie dough in there.

00:53:57.901 --> 00:53:59.903
It's a cookie-brownie hybrid.

00:53:59.903 --> 00:54:03.340
And we got this icing that
you would dip in here,

00:54:03.340 --> 00:54:04.874
and I'm not going to do it.

00:54:04.874 --> 00:54:08.812
I've decided I'm taking a stand
against all twisted bread.

00:54:08.812 --> 00:54:10.547
Not happening, sorry.

00:54:10.547 --> 00:54:13.984
Here in China, our
exclusive dessert options

00:54:13.984 --> 00:54:17.754
are limited to durian pie.

00:54:17.754 --> 00:54:18.888
I believe this is durian.

00:54:18.888 --> 00:54:20.223
I had a sniff.

00:54:20.223 --> 00:54:21.992
It's durian.

00:54:21.992 --> 00:54:23.560
You can always tell if
something is durian.

00:54:23.560 --> 00:54:24.761
Just put your nose to it.

00:54:24.761 --> 00:54:26.529
Pineapple pie,

00:54:26.529 --> 00:54:30.667
and we have one of two

00:54:30.667 --> 00:54:32.936
Portuguese egg tarts.

00:54:32.936 --> 00:54:37.440
Drinks. In the US, you can
get Sprite, Fanta orange,

00:54:37.440 --> 00:54:40.777
Dasani water, and Dr Pepper.

00:54:40.777 --> 00:54:45.148
This is emblic leafflower

00:54:45.148 --> 00:54:47.917
and coconut jelly.

00:54:47.917 --> 00:54:49.819
I had to do quite a bit of research

00:54:49.819 --> 00:54:51.888
to figure out what an emblic is.

00:54:51.888 --> 00:54:54.557
Apparently it's some kind of fruit

00:54:54.557 --> 00:54:56.926
that actually has a lot
to do with Buddhism,

00:54:56.926 --> 00:55:00.297
but it has great cooling

00:55:00.297 --> 00:55:02.232
and cough-relieving properties,

00:55:02.232 --> 00:55:05.602
so this is perfect for summer
when it's too hot outside.

00:55:07.570 --> 00:55:08.405
Oh.

00:55:10.273 --> 00:55:12.108
It's kind of nice, but
it also kind of tastes

00:55:12.108 --> 00:55:15.478
like I'm drinking green
perfume, if that makes sense.

00:55:15.478 --> 00:55:17.580
It's very, very floral.

00:55:17.580 --> 00:55:21.818
This is coconut and musk melon.

00:55:21.818 --> 00:55:23.286
Hm.

00:55:23.286 --> 00:55:24.220
Oh, that's tasty.

00:55:24.220 --> 00:55:28.158
It's a little bit too
rich, so nay to that.

00:55:28.158 --> 00:55:29.659
And this,

00:55:29.659 --> 00:55:33.797
this is carambola and olive.

00:55:33.797 --> 00:55:35.699
It's such a weird combination, right?

00:55:35.699 --> 00:55:38.034
So, a carambola is this thing.

00:55:39.169 --> 00:55:42.739
It's a star fruit, but I've
never had it as a drink.

00:55:42.739 --> 00:55:47.077
And together with Chinese olive? OK.

00:55:47.077 --> 00:55:48.712
Learn something new every day.

00:55:50.647 --> 00:55:53.516
Mm. Oh, that was a pleasant surprise.

00:55:53.516 --> 00:55:55.785
There was actually some coconut
jelly at the bottom, too,

00:55:55.785 --> 00:55:56.986
that was very inviting.

00:55:56.986 --> 00:56:01.224
We also just have a regular
mango and passion fruit drink.

00:56:01.224 --> 00:56:04.794
Oh, and bottled water.

00:56:08.031 --> 00:56:11.234
Domino's entered China in 1997,

00:56:11.234 --> 00:56:14.537
but for about two decades, they
pretty much just floundered

00:56:14.537 --> 00:56:16.873
and nobody really took notice of them.

00:56:16.873 --> 00:56:18.641
It was only really in recent years

00:56:18.641 --> 00:56:21.378
that they've become very youthful

00:56:21.378 --> 00:56:25.415
with all sorts of wacky
flavors, as you've seen,

00:56:25.415 --> 00:56:27.951
and because it's not
as common as McDonald's

00:56:27.951 --> 00:56:32.322
or KFC in China, a Domino's
opening in, for example,

00:56:32.322 --> 00:56:36.426
a tier-two, tier-three
city is big news to locals,

00:56:36.426 --> 00:56:39.295
and a lot of people actually
post about it on social media.

00:56:39.295 --> 00:56:41.464
"Oh, look, a Domino's
has come to our town."

00:56:41.464 --> 00:56:43.166
It's something to be proud of.

00:56:43.166 --> 00:56:44.167
Domino's in the US,

00:56:44.167 --> 00:56:47.337
I feel like it's been
Domino's versus Pizza Hut,

00:56:47.337 --> 00:56:49.973
Pizza Hut versus Domino's
since I think the '80s.

00:56:49.973 --> 00:56:52.409
Yes, there's other
nationwide pizza chains.

00:56:52.409 --> 00:56:54.210
Papa Johns sucked up
a lot of the attention

00:56:54.210 --> 00:56:55.445
online for a while.

00:56:55.445 --> 00:56:56.946
There's Little Caesars,
there's a bunch of other ones,

00:56:56.946 --> 00:56:59.215
but it really is Domino's and Pizza Hut

00:56:59.215 --> 00:57:00.016
have been neck and neck.

00:57:00.016 --> 00:57:02.118
I mean, they're kind of interchangeable.

00:57:02.118 --> 00:57:03.386
Now people watching are
going to be like, "No,

00:57:03.386 --> 00:57:05.321
one's better than the other."

00:57:05.321 --> 00:57:06.923
Honestly, I don't think I
could taste the difference

00:57:06.923 --> 00:57:09.793
if you put them side by
side, but with Domino's,

00:57:09.793 --> 00:57:11.394
as far as the reputation, you always know

00:57:11.394 --> 00:57:13.663
you're going to get a
good pizza, a hot pizza,

00:57:13.663 --> 00:57:16.566
it's going to be decently
priced, which is nice.

00:57:16.566 --> 00:57:19.969
Here in China, Domino's
main rivals are, of course,

00:57:19.969 --> 00:57:22.305
Pizza Hut, who dominates the market

00:57:22.305 --> 00:57:25.175
with a steady 5% market share.

00:57:25.175 --> 00:57:28.812
Next in line is a local
brand called Champion Pizza,

00:57:28.812 --> 00:57:31.815
with 5.6% of the market share.

00:57:31.815 --> 00:57:33.817
And third comes Domino's,

00:57:33.817 --> 00:57:37.086
at 5.3% of the market share.

00:57:37.086 --> 00:57:41.758
Like in the States, Domino's
China has a guarantee

00:57:41.758 --> 00:57:44.327
to deliver your pizza within 30 minutes.

00:57:44.327 --> 00:57:46.996
Otherwise, they will give
you all sorts of discounts.

00:57:46.996 --> 00:57:49.065
This really sets them apart

00:57:49.065 --> 00:57:50.834
from other pizza players here in China,

00:57:50.834 --> 00:57:53.536
because they use their own
proprietary delivery service,

00:57:53.536 --> 00:57:57.240
whereas most restaurants
in China use a third party

00:57:57.240 --> 00:57:59.776
akin to something like Uber Eats.

00:57:59.776 --> 00:58:01.377
It's also something that's become

00:58:01.377 --> 00:58:04.147
a bit of a double-edged
sword, because people

00:58:04.147 --> 00:58:08.017
will actively try and game
their 30-minute delivery window

00:58:08.017 --> 00:58:12.388
by switching off corridor
lights, removing door numbers,

00:58:12.388 --> 00:58:13.957
and just generally trying to get

00:58:13.957 --> 00:58:15.892
their delivery drivers lost,

00:58:15.892 --> 00:58:20.096
and about half of all of Domino's

00:58:20.096 --> 00:58:23.132
salary payments go towards
their delivery drivers,

00:58:23.132 --> 00:58:26.302
which shows you how big of
a delivery force they have,

00:58:26.302 --> 00:58:28.204
which is actually kind of quite nice.

00:58:28.204 --> 00:58:29.739
Convenience, I mean, Domino's is probably

00:58:29.739 --> 00:58:31.908
one of the most convenient pizza chains

00:58:31.908 --> 00:58:33.142
in the United States.

00:58:33.142 --> 00:58:35.478
You can get a Domino's pizza,
you can get it in the app,

00:58:35.478 --> 00:58:37.380
it's easy to use, the
pizza's at your place

00:58:37.380 --> 00:58:39.716
in probably 30 minutes,
depending where you live.

00:58:39.716 --> 00:58:41.417
Some would say too convenient.

00:58:43.953 --> 00:58:45.855
The Domino's in China doesn't disclose

00:58:45.855 --> 00:58:47.390
their nutritional information,

00:58:47.390 --> 00:58:50.593
but based on third-party
independent research,

00:58:50.593 --> 00:58:55.164
we found that a large
hand-tossed pepperoni pizza

00:58:55.164 --> 00:58:59.636
has 1,466.4 calories,

00:58:59.636 --> 00:59:01.771
64 grams of protein,

00:59:01.771 --> 00:59:04.841
66.4 grams of fat,

00:59:04.841 --> 00:59:08.378
155.2 grams of carbs,

00:59:08.378 --> 00:59:12.682
and 3,257.6 milligrams

00:59:12.682 --> 00:59:13.816
of sodium.

00:59:13.816 --> 00:59:17.086
Our large pepperoni is
370 calories per slice,

00:59:17.086 --> 00:59:20.924
or 2,960 for the entire pie.

00:59:20.924 --> 00:59:25.328
Also, 299% of your daily sodium.

00:59:25.328 --> 00:59:29.032
Oy! That's a salty pie.

00:59:29.032 --> 00:59:33.803
Domino's China's most
calorific pizza is this,

00:59:33.803 --> 00:59:37.874
the large salted-egg-yolk-flavored
chicken pizza

00:59:37.874 --> 00:59:40.343
with stuffed sausage crust.

00:59:40.343 --> 00:59:43.279
Now, one slice is 230 calories,

00:59:43.279 --> 00:59:48.251
and the full pizza is 1,841 calories.

00:59:48.251 --> 00:59:49.986
Our Domino's pizza with the most calories

00:59:49.986 --> 00:59:52.855
is the Cali chicken bacon ranch.

00:59:52.855 --> 00:59:56.059
An extra-large slice is 560 calories,

00:59:56.059 --> 01:00:00.063
and the full pie, 3,360 calories.

01:00:02.699 --> 01:00:05.568
Two ingredients you won't
find in Domino's in China

01:00:05.568 --> 01:00:08.972
are potassium bromate and ractopamine.

01:00:08.972 --> 01:00:11.507
Both have been banned for use in China.

01:00:11.507 --> 01:00:13.710
Potassium bromate is used
as a dough conditioner,

01:00:13.710 --> 01:00:16.846
and it's classified as
a category 2B carcinogen

01:00:16.846 --> 01:00:19.415
by the International Agency
for Research on Cancer.

01:00:19.415 --> 01:00:21.751
Ractopamine is FDA-approved,

01:00:21.751 --> 01:00:23.753
and it promotes muscle-mass development,

01:00:23.753 --> 01:00:27.290
limits fat deposition, and
reduces feed consumption.

01:00:27.290 --> 01:00:29.792
Although it is considered
safe for human consumption,

01:00:29.792 --> 01:00:33.096
China requires all meats
sold to be free of the drug

01:00:33.096 --> 01:00:35.498
and never fed the product to begin with.

01:00:35.498 --> 01:00:38.067
There is no direct link
stating ractopamine

01:00:38.067 --> 01:00:40.603
is specifically used in
the meat at Domino's,

01:00:40.603 --> 01:00:43.306
but on their stewardship
page under "Animal Care,"

01:00:43.306 --> 01:00:45.908
they state, quote, "It's
important to highlight

01:00:45.908 --> 01:00:48.678
that Domino's does not
own, raise, transport

01:00:48.678 --> 01:00:51.948
or process the animals
used for our products.

01:00:51.948 --> 01:00:54.851
Domino's purchases pork,
beef and poultry ingredients

01:00:54.851 --> 01:00:57.353
from suppliers who obtain their products

01:00:57.353 --> 01:00:59.689
from farmers and ranchers
who raise and care

01:00:59.689 --> 01:01:01.958
for their animals in
compliance with local,

01:01:01.958 --> 01:01:05.428
state and federal guidelines,
industry best practices

01:01:05.428 --> 01:01:08.364
and the support of farm
and animal veterinarians."

01:01:08.364 --> 01:01:12.168
That is a very long legalese
way of Domino's saying,

01:01:12.168 --> 01:01:14.537
"Hey, we don't farm the meat.

01:01:14.537 --> 01:01:16.305
We buy them from other people,

01:01:16.305 --> 01:01:17.573
and they're saying they're
doing it the right way,

01:01:17.573 --> 01:01:19.809
so we don't know."

01:01:19.909 --> 01:01:22.378
Tianran: From exclusive
items to portion sizes,

01:01:22.378 --> 01:01:24.080
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:01:24.080 --> 01:01:26.716
between KFC in China and the US.

01:01:26.716 --> 01:01:28.418
This is "Food Wars."

01:01:31.521 --> 01:01:35.425
Here in China, we can get
KFC in three portion sizes:

01:01:35.425 --> 01:01:39.662
one piece, two pieces, and six pieces.

01:01:39.662 --> 01:01:42.999
In the US, KFC chicken comes
in seven portion sizes.

01:01:42.999 --> 01:01:47.537
These first four are one-piece à la carte;

01:01:47.537 --> 01:01:48.604
two-piece with a combo,

01:01:48.604 --> 01:01:51.340
that's a side, a biscuit, and a drink;

01:01:51.340 --> 01:01:53.976
three-piece, also with a combo;

01:01:53.976 --> 01:01:58.281
and the four-piece, also with the combo.

01:01:59.682 --> 01:02:01.084
And, of course, we have buckets.

01:02:01.084 --> 01:02:03.786
We have three main core buckets.

01:02:03.786 --> 01:02:05.021
The snack bucket,

01:02:05.021 --> 01:02:08.191
which contains five pieces
of chicken and six wings;

01:02:08.191 --> 01:02:10.326
the family bucket,

01:02:10.326 --> 01:02:13.863
which gets you an extra corn on the cob,

01:02:13.863 --> 01:02:16.833
some mashed potato, and three drinks;

01:02:16.833 --> 01:02:19.035
and the super family bucket,

01:02:19.035 --> 01:02:22.105
where you get dessert and mashed potato,

01:02:22.105 --> 01:02:24.407
more of both on top of that as well.

01:02:24.407 --> 01:02:28.211
And then we have buckets, where
you can get an eight-piece,

01:02:28.211 --> 01:02:31.714
a 12-piece, or the 16-piece.

01:02:31.714 --> 01:02:35.084
Now, if we're going strictly
on just chicken and not wings,

01:02:35.084 --> 01:02:39.622
the US's largest is
166-point-repeating-6% bigger

01:02:39.622 --> 01:02:42.625
than China's largest chicken portion size.

01:02:42.625 --> 01:02:44.227
Next we have fries.

01:02:44.227 --> 01:02:46.996
Now, here in China, we
get them in three sizes:

01:02:46.996 --> 01:02:50.133
small, medium, and large.

01:02:50.133 --> 01:02:51.834
We got two fry sizes in the US:

01:02:51.834 --> 01:02:54.570
the individual and the large.

01:02:54.570 --> 01:02:57.039
Let's weigh the large
fries in both countries.

01:02:59.308 --> 01:03:01.477
[Joe laughs]

01:03:01.477 --> 01:03:03.012
I never grow tired of that.

01:03:03.012 --> 01:03:06.015
Here in China, our drinks
come in three sizes:

01:03:06.015 --> 01:03:09.018
small, medium, and large.

01:03:09.018 --> 01:03:10.953
American drinks come
in the following sizes:

01:03:10.953 --> 01:03:14.657
regular, 20 ounces; and large, 30 ounces.

01:03:14.657 --> 01:03:15.925
But that's not all.

01:03:15.925 --> 01:03:20.163
You can also get a half-gallon container.

01:03:20.163 --> 01:03:21.130
Guzh!

01:03:21.130 --> 01:03:24.767
The Jesus piece of any
beverage of your choosing.

01:03:24.767 --> 01:03:27.103
Damn!

01:03:27.103 --> 01:03:28.805
Hope you're sharing that, Joe.

01:03:34.377 --> 01:03:36.345
Here's everything you'll
find in a KFC China

01:03:36.345 --> 01:03:39.749
that you won't find in the US.

01:03:39.749 --> 01:03:41.450
We have a lot to get through.

01:03:41.450 --> 01:03:43.719
Here's everything you'll
find at a KFC in the US

01:03:43.719 --> 01:03:45.588
you won't find in China.

01:03:45.588 --> 01:03:47.323
One exclusive that we have here in China

01:03:47.323 --> 01:03:50.726
that you cannot find in the US are wings.

01:03:50.726 --> 01:03:52.094
[record scratch]
That's right.

01:03:52.094 --> 01:03:53.663
It's tough times for the US economy

01:03:53.663 --> 01:03:55.698
in just about every sector.

01:03:55.698 --> 01:03:56.532
Earlier this year,

01:03:56.532 --> 01:04:01.170
KFC laid off several favorite
menu items, including wings,

01:04:01.170 --> 01:04:04.841
Nashville-hot-sauced
anything, strawberry lemonade,

01:04:04.841 --> 01:04:07.577
chocolate chip cookies, and
pretty much popcorn chicken.

01:04:07.577 --> 01:04:10.179
They still exist in the famous
bowls but not on their own.

01:04:10.179 --> 01:04:11.848
We still got them here,

01:04:11.848 --> 01:04:14.083
and they're available in two styles:

01:04:14.083 --> 01:04:18.888
the crispy spicy wings and
the New Orleans grilled wings.

01:04:18.888 --> 01:04:23.092
Now, you might be wondering,
what are New Orleans wings?

01:04:23.092 --> 01:04:27.430
Apparently KFC might
have invented the flavor,

01:04:27.430 --> 01:04:30.867
and it's kind of like
how General Tso's chicken

01:04:30.867 --> 01:04:33.569
is not actually from China.

01:04:33.569 --> 01:04:37.907
New Orleans chicken is
kind of just a misnomer.

01:04:37.907 --> 01:04:41.777
It's a honey-baked spicy wing with a,

01:04:41.777 --> 01:04:43.346
I think a Cajun mix.

01:04:43.346 --> 01:04:45.147
US chicken styles.

01:04:45.147 --> 01:04:47.516
One chicken style you
can get here in the US

01:04:47.516 --> 01:04:51.287
you can't get in China is
this: the extra crispy.

01:04:51.287 --> 01:04:52.488
It's exactly what it sounds.

01:04:52.488 --> 01:04:53.823
They fry it, like, twice

01:04:53.823 --> 01:04:55.758
or with more breading, I don't know,

01:04:55.758 --> 01:04:57.760
but it gives that extra-crispy crunch.

01:04:57.760 --> 01:04:59.195
Volume up.

01:04:59.195 --> 01:05:02.899
[chicken crunching]

01:05:02.899 --> 01:05:03.833
In some parts of the country,

01:05:03.833 --> 01:05:05.701
you can get Kentucky grilled.

01:05:05.701 --> 01:05:07.003
Grilled chicken, not fried.

01:05:07.003 --> 01:05:08.237
I mean, fried's in the title,

01:05:08.237 --> 01:05:09.605
so I don't know what you're
doing getting grilled chicken

01:05:09.605 --> 01:05:11.207
at KFC.

01:05:11.207 --> 01:05:14.443
And for sandwiches, we
have a spicy option.

01:05:14.443 --> 01:05:15.678
I just wanted to talk a little bit

01:05:15.678 --> 01:05:17.613
about our chicken recipes here.

01:05:17.613 --> 01:05:20.583
So, this is the original recipe,

01:05:20.583 --> 01:05:23.019
but we also have an additional recipe

01:05:23.019 --> 01:05:26.289
called the golden crispy chicken.

01:05:26.289 --> 01:05:28.491
Now, you can tell that there's
quite a bit of a difference.

01:05:28.491 --> 01:05:31.160
It is significantly more "golden"

01:05:31.160 --> 01:05:33.362
in that I guess it is
lighter-yellow-colored

01:05:33.362 --> 01:05:34.897
than the original.

01:05:34.897 --> 01:05:38.034
But there's also a very healthy sprinkling

01:05:38.034 --> 01:05:40.169
of chili powder on top,

01:05:40.169 --> 01:05:45.007
and the batter is a lot
harder and crunchier.

01:05:45.007 --> 01:05:46.208
I guess it's probably more

01:05:46.208 --> 01:05:48.611
of a localized version of the chicken.

01:05:48.611 --> 01:05:50.446
That looks delicious.

01:05:50.446 --> 01:05:52.982
That's like extra crispy and spicy?

01:05:52.982 --> 01:05:54.617
Yeah, I definitely want to try that.

01:05:54.617 --> 01:05:58.087
Here we have our exclusive
burgers and roll.

01:05:58.087 --> 01:05:59.455
We'll get to that later.

01:05:59.455 --> 01:06:01.557
First off, I just want
to draw your attention

01:06:01.557 --> 01:06:05.094
to the rattan-pepper-flavor

01:06:05.094 --> 01:06:07.463
spa chicken burger.

01:06:07.463 --> 01:06:09.565
I had a really tough
time trying to figure out

01:06:09.565 --> 01:06:11.334
what spa meant.

01:06:11.334 --> 01:06:15.137
And I found actually on
one advertising poster

01:06:15.137 --> 01:06:18.574
in fine print that spa was not an acronym.

01:06:18.574 --> 01:06:21.510
It just meant that the
chicken is juicy and tender

01:06:21.510 --> 01:06:24.246
because this is made of chicken breast

01:06:24.246 --> 01:06:25.448
instead of chicken thigh,

01:06:25.448 --> 01:06:28.084
which you'll remember from another episode

01:06:28.084 --> 01:06:29.585
is the norm here in China

01:06:29.585 --> 01:06:31.120
because Chinese people think

01:06:31.120 --> 01:06:32.855
that chicken thigh is juicy and tender,

01:06:32.855 --> 01:06:36.225
whereas breast is really dry
and it's basically chalky.

01:06:36.225 --> 01:06:40.863
So I guess the "spa" is an
attempt to get rid of that stigma

01:06:40.863 --> 01:06:42.999
by saying, "Ah, look,
it's so soft and tender,

01:06:42.999 --> 01:06:45.401
like the chicken's just
come out of a massage

01:06:45.401 --> 01:06:46.936
or a spa treatment."

01:06:46.936 --> 01:06:50.206
If you haven't had hot pot or
had Sichuan flavors before,

01:06:50.206 --> 01:06:52.508
this might be a really big turnoff

01:06:52.508 --> 01:06:56.345
because the taste of the
rattan pepper is so strong.

01:06:56.345 --> 01:06:57.346
The chicken is all right.

01:06:57.346 --> 01:06:58.481
You know, it's tender.

01:06:58.481 --> 01:07:00.850
I can't say it's just come out of a spa.

01:07:00.850 --> 01:07:05.254
The spicy chicken sandwich.
Looks basically the same.

01:07:05.254 --> 01:07:07.156
Well, for one, it's not spicy.

01:07:07.156 --> 01:07:08.758
And second, it's actually not as tasty

01:07:08.758 --> 01:07:10.926
as the spa chicken.

01:07:10.926 --> 01:07:12.728
I do actually — no, you know
what, I take it all back.

01:07:12.728 --> 01:07:15.264
I do actually feel that the spa chicken

01:07:15.264 --> 01:07:16.599
is a little bit more tender.

01:07:16.599 --> 01:07:18.434
This one does feel drier.

01:07:18.434 --> 01:07:21.137
The crispy chicken sandwich.

01:07:21.137 --> 01:07:23.072
It's pretty much the
same as everything else.

01:07:23.072 --> 01:07:26.742
I think they're really just
adding different condiments,

01:07:26.742 --> 01:07:30.946
but the gist of it is always
lettuce, the mayo, and chicken.

01:07:30.946 --> 01:07:32.715
That's it. And the bun, of course.

01:07:32.715 --> 01:07:36.018
And the New Orleans chicken burger.

01:07:36.018 --> 01:07:38.087
Of course, they're going to
put this in a burger as well

01:07:38.087 --> 01:07:41.157
if they've gone and invented
an entire flavor category.

01:07:41.157 --> 01:07:42.525
That's actually not bad.

01:07:42.525 --> 01:07:45.027
And we have one more chicken option,

01:07:45.027 --> 01:07:48.497
the old Beijing chicken roll,

01:07:48.497 --> 01:07:50.900
or, as listed on their website,

01:07:50.900 --> 01:07:53.069
the dragon twister.

01:07:53.069 --> 01:07:56.038
So, they called it "old Beijing style,"

01:07:56.038 --> 01:07:59.341
and I now understand
that "old Beijing" means

01:07:59.341 --> 01:08:01.544
that you're going to chuck
some cucumber in there.

01:08:01.544 --> 01:08:04.914
There's probably leek in there as well.

01:08:04.914 --> 01:08:06.816
There's going to be tianmian sauce.

01:08:06.816 --> 01:08:08.984
Let's give the dragon a taste.

01:08:10.986 --> 01:08:12.488
It just tastes sweet.

01:08:12.488 --> 01:08:14.056
There is a crunch from the cucumbers,

01:08:14.056 --> 01:08:16.826
but the cucumber's kind of gone a bit ...

01:08:16.826 --> 01:08:18.527
it's kind of gone a bit sad as well.

01:08:18.527 --> 01:08:21.530
Now we've got the beef burger options.

01:08:21.530 --> 01:08:25.367
This is the classic
American-style beef burger.

01:08:26.602 --> 01:08:31.107
Imagine this being, like,
the introductory course

01:08:31.107 --> 01:08:35.344
to American flavors for
someone who's never left China.

01:08:35.344 --> 01:08:37.480
They're going to be
sorely disappointed. Ugh.

01:08:37.480 --> 01:08:40.549
You can also get double
beef burgers at KFC

01:08:40.549 --> 01:08:42.918
in your classic American style.

01:08:42.918 --> 01:08:44.787
Ugh, no, thank you.

01:08:44.787 --> 01:08:48.657
Or the smoked pepper flavor.

01:08:50.025 --> 01:08:52.695
If you want a burger, go to
McDonald's, go to Burger King.

01:08:52.695 --> 01:08:57.600
There's also a fish burger,
the deep-sea cod burger,

01:08:57.600 --> 01:08:59.368
which you can get as a double as well.

01:08:59.368 --> 01:09:01.504
I do have my hopes up for this one.

01:09:01.504 --> 01:09:02.638
Not very high, mind you,

01:09:02.638 --> 01:09:04.306
but I do have some hope for this one.

01:09:04.306 --> 01:09:08.177
This is the bacon wagyu beef burger.

01:09:08.177 --> 01:09:09.411
It's a premium burger,

01:09:09.411 --> 01:09:11.747
as you can tell because
it comes in its own box,

01:09:11.747 --> 01:09:14.917
which prevents it from becoming
squished into sandwiches

01:09:14.917 --> 01:09:15.851
like these guys.

01:09:19.488 --> 01:09:20.389
No.

01:09:20.389 --> 01:09:21.724
No.

01:09:21.724 --> 01:09:22.625
No.

01:09:22.625 --> 01:09:24.593
I don't care if it really is wagyu or not.

01:09:24.593 --> 01:09:26.128
In fact, it actually tastes a little bit

01:09:26.128 --> 01:09:28.097
like the consistency of Spam.

01:09:28.097 --> 01:09:30.399
You can get that as a double or a triple,

01:09:30.399 --> 01:09:33.536
but just skip it in my opinion.

01:09:33.536 --> 01:09:36.639
We have one exclusive sandwich to the US.

01:09:36.639 --> 01:09:38.274
It's this: the Chicken Little,

01:09:38.274 --> 01:09:41.610
which I guess is a
bite-size chicken sandwich.

01:09:41.610 --> 01:09:43.579
A little tender in here also.

01:09:44.446 --> 01:09:46.382
Hey, KFC, if I had one note,

01:09:46.382 --> 01:09:47.983
maybe relax on the mayo on this.

01:09:47.983 --> 01:09:49.785
Are you kidding me? Look at this.

01:09:49.785 --> 01:09:51.086
The sauce, whatever this is, like,

01:09:51.086 --> 01:09:52.621
bro, it is dripping.

01:09:52.621 --> 01:09:54.723
Pickles, not a fan.

01:09:54.723 --> 01:09:56.025
Get out of here.

01:09:59.862 --> 01:10:02.431
Why this over the chicken
sandwich, I have no idea.

01:10:02.431 --> 01:10:05.267
I mean, unless you have a kid

01:10:05.267 --> 01:10:07.136
or a picky eater, skip these.

01:10:07.136 --> 01:10:09.205
We've also got other chicken options,

01:10:09.205 --> 01:10:14.109
beginning with our Hong Kong-style
crispy big chicken thigh.

01:10:14.109 --> 01:10:15.544
If you've watched our other episodes,

01:10:15.544 --> 01:10:20.082
you'll know that Hong Kong
style usually is used to denote

01:10:20.082 --> 01:10:25.087
a sort of sweet
honey-roasted flavor profile.

01:10:25.621 --> 01:10:27.189
Would've been oven-baked.

01:10:27.189 --> 01:10:28.023
Look at this glaze.

01:10:28.023 --> 01:10:28.991
That's beautiful.

01:10:30.826 --> 01:10:31.860
Mm.

01:10:31.860 --> 01:10:34.096
It's sweet without being cloying.

01:10:34.096 --> 01:10:35.030
It's savory.

01:10:35.030 --> 01:10:36.765
It's incredibly meaty.

01:10:36.765 --> 01:10:41.537
There's also the secret
recipe whole chicken.

01:10:41.537 --> 01:10:44.139
Look at that! An entire chicken!

01:10:44.139 --> 01:10:45.908
See, it's about the size of my face,

01:10:45.908 --> 01:10:47.209
and I've got a pretty long face.

01:10:47.209 --> 01:10:48.244
You've done well.

01:10:48.244 --> 01:10:49.945
You've done well, Colonel.

01:10:49.945 --> 01:10:51.981
Mm. I forgive you for the burgers.

01:10:51.981 --> 01:10:54.350
Heck yeah, dude. I totally
want one of those, man.

01:10:54.350 --> 01:10:55.985
Just bite right into that big leg

01:10:55.985 --> 01:10:57.453
like in medieval times.

01:10:57.453 --> 01:10:59.488
This here is the

01:10:59.488 --> 01:11:03.092
hot and spicy chicken with bone,

01:11:03.092 --> 01:11:05.828
and apparently it's scapular meat,

01:11:05.828 --> 01:11:07.763
so your collarbone.

01:11:07.763 --> 01:11:11.000
I've never had collarbone chicken meat,

01:11:11.000 --> 01:11:13.936
so this is definitely a first for me.

01:11:13.936 --> 01:11:17.072
It tastes a little bit
like a chicken nugget

01:11:17.072 --> 01:11:18.407
but with a bone inside.

01:11:18.407 --> 01:11:22.745
And we've also got popcorn
chicken and nuggets.

01:11:22.745 --> 01:11:24.680
You might be wondering what these are.

01:11:24.680 --> 01:11:27.916
KFC is trying to squeeze
in on the pizza business.

01:11:27.916 --> 01:11:30.853
This is KFC's K pizza.

01:11:30.853 --> 01:11:34.456
This is a chicken and mushroom K pizza.

01:11:34.456 --> 01:11:35.291
Look at that.

01:11:35.291 --> 01:11:37.159
Ultrathin crust.

01:11:37.159 --> 01:11:38.727
That's actually pretty good.

01:11:38.727 --> 01:11:41.697
I think I actually like this
more than Domino's pizzas.

01:11:41.697 --> 01:11:45.167
And this one is very special.

01:11:45.167 --> 01:11:50.072
This is the K pizza dapanji flavor.

01:11:50.072 --> 01:11:53.742
So, dapanji means "big plate of chicken."

01:11:53.742 --> 01:11:58.013
It's a Xinjiang dish which
is usually a chicken stew,

01:11:58.013 --> 01:12:02.184
comes on a giant dish, with
potatoes and bell peppers,

01:12:02.184 --> 01:12:05.321
and you also get some
hand-pulled noodles thrown in.

01:12:05.321 --> 01:12:08.791
In fact, the origin story
of the big plate of chicken,

01:12:08.791 --> 01:12:12.061
supposedly was either invented

01:12:12.061 --> 01:12:15.064
by a Sichuanese or a Hunanese immigrant

01:12:15.064 --> 01:12:18.300
who was serving these
dishes up to truckers.

01:12:18.300 --> 01:12:20.035
And they're very hearty.

01:12:20.035 --> 01:12:20.969
They're super tasty.

01:12:20.969 --> 01:12:23.605
You always eat them in a group,

01:12:23.605 --> 01:12:24.840
but I'm just going to pig out

01:12:24.840 --> 01:12:27.209
and eat one by myself on a pizza.

01:12:27.209 --> 01:12:28.310
Mm.

01:12:31.413 --> 01:12:34.216
KFC, this is legit good.

01:12:34.216 --> 01:12:36.318
Announcement!

01:12:36.318 --> 01:12:39.621
KFC has recently added
nuggets back onto the menu,

01:12:39.621 --> 01:12:41.623
so they're technically
not an exclusive anymore,

01:12:41.623 --> 01:12:42.725
but I'll show them off here.

01:12:42.725 --> 01:12:45.127
You can get them in eight and 12 pieces.

01:12:45.127 --> 01:12:46.595
Here's the nugget eight pieces.

01:12:46.595 --> 01:12:48.697
Get in there, Yuelei. Nugget vision.

01:12:49.465 --> 01:12:51.133
Now, remember before when I said

01:12:51.133 --> 01:12:52.735
they didn't have popcorn chicken anymore?

01:12:52.735 --> 01:12:55.337
I mean, this is pretty ... right?

01:12:55.337 --> 01:12:57.439
It's a little bit bigger
than popcorn chicken.

01:12:57.439 --> 01:12:58.941
When I said nuggets, you
were probably thinking

01:12:58.941 --> 01:13:00.409
what I was thinking,
like McNuggets, right?

01:13:00.409 --> 01:13:01.443
Like, nuggets.

01:13:01.443 --> 01:13:04.346
So this being a nugget is very strange.

01:13:04.346 --> 01:13:05.547
Really good, though.

01:13:05.547 --> 01:13:07.049
We also have chicken tenders.

01:13:07.049 --> 01:13:09.952
They come in orders of eight, 12, and 16.

01:13:09.952 --> 01:13:11.854
The crispiness on this. I have to.

01:13:11.854 --> 01:13:13.589
[chicken crunching]

01:13:13.589 --> 01:13:15.791
Mm!

01:13:15.791 --> 01:13:17.459
Now, to complement your chicken,

01:13:17.459 --> 01:13:22.030
we have a plethora of sauces
and condiments to offer,

01:13:22.030 --> 01:13:25.234
namely, sweet vinegar and sweet chili,

01:13:25.234 --> 01:13:26.935
which we couldn't find today,

01:13:26.935 --> 01:13:31.340
and the Sichuan pepper spicy chili powder.

01:13:31.340 --> 01:13:33.008
You can't eat these dry.

01:13:33.008 --> 01:13:35.177
You can get a bunch of exclusive sauces,

01:13:35.177 --> 01:13:39.114
and you know what that means.

01:13:39.114 --> 01:13:40.048
Sauce talk.

01:13:40.048 --> 01:13:41.517
Sauce talk.

01:13:41.517 --> 01:13:43.952
Starting off, the Buffalo ranch.

01:13:43.952 --> 01:13:45.988
Thank you, nuggets. Let's go.

01:13:47.756 --> 01:13:51.026
Yeah! The KFC sauce, really good.

01:13:51.026 --> 01:13:53.395
Barbecue sauce, honey barbecue, excuse me.

01:13:53.395 --> 01:13:54.630
Eh.

01:13:54.630 --> 01:13:55.764
Classic ranch.

01:13:55.764 --> 01:13:57.866
I don't know what the ranch
situation out there in China is,

01:13:57.866 --> 01:14:00.235
but here, we're doing
all right with ranch.

01:14:00.235 --> 01:14:03.372
The ranch situation in America, solid.

01:14:03.372 --> 01:14:06.041
We also have a honey mustard
sauce, a honey sauce,

01:14:06.041 --> 01:14:07.075
and a hot sauce.

01:14:07.075 --> 01:14:08.877
All three today, they did not have.

01:14:08.877 --> 01:14:13.015
Here in China, KFC has something
called the DIY kitchen.

01:14:13.015 --> 01:14:15.684
And they also have stuff
from third-party vendors.

01:14:15.684 --> 01:14:18.020
Without further ado, let's dig in.

01:14:18.020 --> 01:14:20.956
First off, we have the chicken nuggets

01:14:20.956 --> 01:14:24.560
and the hot and spicy chicken with bone.

01:14:24.560 --> 01:14:28.997
If I was hungry and I wanted
KFC, I'm going to order KFC.

01:14:28.997 --> 01:14:31.400
I'm not going to go and cook it myself.

01:14:31.400 --> 01:14:34.236
Isn't that the whole point
of takeout? Of fast food?

01:14:34.236 --> 01:14:36.004
It's cooked for you.

01:14:36.004 --> 01:14:37.105
If you're so inclined,

01:14:37.105 --> 01:14:40.242
you can also make KFC's

01:14:40.242 --> 01:14:42.811
famous egg tarts at home.

01:14:42.811 --> 01:14:47.382
KFC's also offering
secret-recipe chicken fillets

01:14:47.382 --> 01:14:49.084
from a third-party vendor.

01:14:49.084 --> 01:14:53.722
The whole-cut sirloin steak,
also from a third party.

01:14:53.722 --> 01:14:56.959
KFC also selling you pasta now.

01:14:56.959 --> 01:15:00.128
They come in mushroom and
black pepper, carbonara,

01:15:00.128 --> 01:15:01.363
and spag Bol.

01:15:01.363 --> 01:15:04.933
Actually, oh, this is the spag Bol.

01:15:04.933 --> 01:15:07.536
You've got your Bolognese.

01:15:07.536 --> 01:15:09.738
You've got various condiments.

01:15:09.738 --> 01:15:11.840
Yeah, no to KFC pasta.

01:15:11.840 --> 01:15:13.408
No to KFC pasta.

01:15:13.408 --> 01:15:14.776
No to their burgers.

01:15:14.776 --> 01:15:15.978
Chicken is your lane.

01:15:15.978 --> 01:15:17.513
Stay in that lane.

01:15:17.513 --> 01:15:19.348
They've also got rice.

01:15:19.348 --> 01:15:20.649
They come in four flavors.

01:15:20.649 --> 01:15:23.886
The original-flavor chicken

01:15:23.886 --> 01:15:26.622
Japanese-style fried rice.

01:15:26.622 --> 01:15:28.257
What's Japanese about it?

01:15:28.257 --> 01:15:29.358
I can't tell.

01:15:29.358 --> 01:15:31.860
And this one is the baked rice.

01:15:31.860 --> 01:15:36.398
This one is the French-style
roast chicken cheese

01:15:36.398 --> 01:15:37.232
baked rice.

01:15:37.232 --> 01:15:40.502
And probably the most understandable

01:15:40.502 --> 01:15:43.672
of the offerings in the
DIY kitchen, the ice cream.

01:15:43.672 --> 01:15:45.574
So KFC have partnered up with Oatly.

01:15:45.574 --> 01:15:48.710
As you can tell, Oatly is
just everywhere in China.

01:15:48.710 --> 01:15:50.112
It's so big.

01:15:50.112 --> 01:15:52.948
KFC also has this.

01:15:52.948 --> 01:15:56.485
It's called the Modern ice cream,

01:15:56.485 --> 01:15:59.755
although here in China
we call it the "Madier."

01:15:59.755 --> 01:16:01.456
And it's got a really interesting history.

01:16:01.456 --> 01:16:04.159
This originates from a
city in northeast China

01:16:04.159 --> 01:16:06.895
called Harbin, where they hold
the Ice and Snow Festival,

01:16:06.895 --> 01:16:08.397
if you know about that.

01:16:08.397 --> 01:16:11.934
And, basically, modern
Harbin was more or less

01:16:11.934 --> 01:16:14.436
built by the Russians.

01:16:14.436 --> 01:16:18.006
The "Modern" gets its name from a hotel

01:16:18.006 --> 01:16:19.908
that was built by a Russian,

01:16:19.908 --> 01:16:24.246
which also had a bakery and
sold yogurt and ice cream.

01:16:24.246 --> 01:16:26.548
So this has become an institution,

01:16:26.548 --> 01:16:29.885
especially if you go
to Harbin in the winter

01:16:29.885 --> 01:16:32.955
for the Snow and Ice festival,
when it's, like, minus 20.

01:16:32.955 --> 01:16:34.923
People are still queuing up on the street

01:16:34.923 --> 01:16:37.025
to get yourself one of these Popsicles.

01:16:37.025 --> 01:16:39.027
It's been a while.

01:16:39.027 --> 01:16:42.030
Let's see if the ice cream
is still good to eat.

01:16:42.898 --> 01:16:44.666
It does feel a little bit soft.

01:16:44.666 --> 01:16:49.438
Oh, it's like Frosty the
Snowman once summer's set in.

01:16:49.438 --> 01:16:50.973
You can just have a peek.

01:16:53.675 --> 01:16:55.210
I'll be able to drink it soon.

01:16:55.210 --> 01:16:57.579
Mm. Salvageable.

01:16:57.579 --> 01:16:59.615
What still is going strong on the menu

01:16:59.615 --> 01:17:00.415
is the pot pie.

01:17:00.415 --> 01:17:01.883
Man, this thing is hot. Aye!

01:17:02.818 --> 01:17:04.019
I don't want to disrespect

01:17:04.019 --> 01:17:06.421
any of the pot-pie-heads watching,

01:17:06.421 --> 01:17:08.790
but I've never seen anyone order this.

01:17:08.790 --> 01:17:10.559
I've never seen anyone eat this.

01:17:10.559 --> 01:17:11.893
This thing is gigantic.

01:17:11.893 --> 01:17:13.695
You can't get this as a side.

01:17:13.695 --> 01:17:16.765
So someone in this country,

01:17:16.765 --> 01:17:19.067
assuming lots of people are walking into

01:17:19.067 --> 01:17:22.904
Kentucky Fried Chicken
and getting a pot pie,

01:17:22.904 --> 01:17:24.006
I don't know why you're doing this.

01:17:24.006 --> 01:17:25.407
Pot pie is perfectly fine.

01:17:25.407 --> 01:17:28.010
I feel like this could
totally go on the menu.

01:17:28.010 --> 01:17:29.578
If you want to fight me in
the comments, go for it.

01:17:29.578 --> 01:17:31.713
But I've never met a person
who gets this and eats it.

01:17:31.713 --> 01:17:33.615
And this is kind of my job.

01:17:33.615 --> 01:17:34.883
We'll do a taste test later.

01:17:34.883 --> 01:17:37.252
As for now, moving on. The famous bowl.

01:17:37.252 --> 01:17:39.187
I don't think this exists
outside of America,

01:17:39.187 --> 01:17:40.422
so let me go ahead and explain it.

01:17:40.422 --> 01:17:44.459
It basically is every
side plus popcorn chicken,

01:17:44.459 --> 01:17:46.128
or in this case nuggets, in one thing.

01:17:46.128 --> 01:17:50.232
Mashed potatoes, gravy, cheese, corn,

01:17:50.232 --> 01:17:52.834
and, yeah, bits of chicken.

01:17:52.834 --> 01:17:54.603
Look, it's not that I don't
like all these things,

01:17:54.603 --> 01:17:56.938
but together in one dish is kind of eh.

01:17:56.938 --> 01:17:58.674
So what you're really
doing is getting a side

01:17:58.674 --> 01:18:00.208
of mashed potatoes and gravy

01:18:00.208 --> 01:18:02.611
and sprinkling some cheese,
corn, and chicken on it.

01:18:02.611 --> 01:18:04.312
I don't know if people were
complaining on the internet.

01:18:04.312 --> 01:18:05.547
The famous bowl is so good,

01:18:05.547 --> 01:18:07.315
now they have the mac 'n' cheese bowl,

01:18:07.315 --> 01:18:10.719
which is mac 'n' cheese
with chicken on it.

01:18:10.719 --> 01:18:11.553
And these are the nuggets.

01:18:11.553 --> 01:18:12.387
Remember I said before,

01:18:12.387 --> 01:18:13.455
the popcorn chicken is still in this?

01:18:13.455 --> 01:18:16.024
I mean, isn't this popcorn chicken?

01:18:16.024 --> 01:18:18.460
Are these too big to be popcorn chickens?

01:18:18.460 --> 01:18:20.829
Is this nuggets that have
replaced the popcorn chicken?

01:18:20.829 --> 01:18:22.497
I want answers.

01:18:22.497 --> 01:18:24.566
The nuggets are fine, and
the mac 'n' cheese too,

01:18:24.566 --> 01:18:27.202
but together they don't add anything.

01:18:27.202 --> 01:18:28.770
The only thing it's doing is being like,

01:18:28.770 --> 01:18:30.005
"Why get it in two containers?

01:18:30.005 --> 01:18:30.972
Just get it in one."

01:18:30.972 --> 01:18:34.076
Speaking of mac 'n' cheese,
exclusive sides in the US,

01:18:34.076 --> 01:18:35.944
you can get your mac 'n' cheese

01:18:35.944 --> 01:18:38.046
without chunks of chicken in it.

01:18:38.046 --> 01:18:39.347
Just regular mac 'n' cheese.

01:18:39.347 --> 01:18:40.482
Our biscuits.

01:18:42.317 --> 01:18:43.285
Oh, so dry.

01:18:43.285 --> 01:18:44.486
Coleslaw.

01:18:46.054 --> 01:18:47.556
China, you don't want this.

01:18:47.556 --> 01:18:50.859
I mean, how do you even explain coleslaw?

01:18:50.859 --> 01:18:53.595
Shredded lettuce. Shredded
cabbage, excuse me.

01:18:53.595 --> 01:18:54.863
I don't even know what it is.

01:18:54.863 --> 01:18:58.333
With, what, mayo and carrots?

01:18:58.333 --> 01:19:01.203
And corn.

01:19:01.203 --> 01:19:03.905
Like McDonald's, KFC also has

01:19:03.905 --> 01:19:06.341
a late-night street-food menu.

01:19:06.341 --> 01:19:09.111
But unlike McDonald's,
which only has one item,

01:19:09.111 --> 01:19:12.914
the chicken carcass, KFC has four

01:19:12.914 --> 01:19:17.586
and two different types
of chicken carcass.

01:19:19.855 --> 01:19:23.258
I feel like the KFC version
is maybe a bit bonier.

01:19:23.258 --> 01:19:26.128
So, this is probably the
Sichuan version then.

01:19:26.128 --> 01:19:27.763
Let's take one of these fellas out.

01:19:27.763 --> 01:19:29.631
I think preferable to the original.

01:19:29.631 --> 01:19:30.832
This is pretty interesting.

01:19:30.832 --> 01:19:34.503
This actually looks like
original-recipe chicken.

01:19:34.503 --> 01:19:37.205
This, in fact, is called the

01:19:37.205 --> 01:19:40.375
aoao big chicken carcass.

01:19:40.375 --> 01:19:44.746
Aoao is onomatopoeic,

01:19:44.746 --> 01:19:47.716
and it's from the
northeastern region of China.

01:19:47.716 --> 01:19:50.418
Basically it's slang for "howling."

01:19:50.418 --> 01:19:52.154
You know, that is
gigantic, and you're just,

01:19:52.154 --> 01:19:53.522
you're dying to eat it.

01:19:53.522 --> 01:19:56.358
So, Joe, if you come to China
and you want to order this,

01:19:56.358 --> 01:19:57.993
you know what you gotta do.

01:19:57.993 --> 01:20:00.061
You just go up to the counter and be like,

01:20:00.061 --> 01:20:02.264
I want that [howls] chicken.

01:20:02.264 --> 01:20:03.098
Got it.

01:20:03.098 --> 01:20:05.233
And then they'll know
exactly what you want.

01:20:05.233 --> 01:20:06.835
You can also get fried chicken feet,

01:20:06.835 --> 01:20:09.171
but we've done one better and gotten

01:20:09.171 --> 01:20:13.975
the fried chicken feet
and fragrant bones box.

01:20:13.975 --> 01:20:17.012
This is the chicken feet, obviously.

01:20:17.012 --> 01:20:20.448
There's also chicken neck,

01:20:20.448 --> 01:20:24.219
there's chicken wing tip,

01:20:24.219 --> 01:20:25.787
scapular meat.

01:20:25.787 --> 01:20:28.990
So all of the fiddly parts of the chicken

01:20:28.990 --> 01:20:32.127
in one convenient box
for you to nibble on.

01:20:32.127 --> 01:20:35.730
These are all of our
exclusive breakfast options.

01:20:35.730 --> 01:20:36.698
OK, so first off,

01:20:36.698 --> 01:20:38.767
I just want to draw
your attention to this.

01:20:38.767 --> 01:20:41.903
KFC has xiao long bao.

01:20:41.903 --> 01:20:43.672
This is incredible because this is

01:20:43.672 --> 01:20:46.241
a super-popular breakfast item.

01:20:46.241 --> 01:20:49.778
If you wake up early,
you'll see lots of sellers

01:20:49.778 --> 01:20:53.648
with bamboo steamers
about as tall as you are

01:20:53.648 --> 01:20:55.984
filled with these sorts of little bao.

01:20:55.984 --> 01:20:58.153
The KFC xiao long bao.

01:21:00.188 --> 01:21:04.292
Oh, that's even better than my
neighborhood breakfast place.

01:21:04.292 --> 01:21:05.126
Color me impressed.

01:21:05.126 --> 01:21:08.296
I'm very, very, very smitten with this.

01:21:08.296 --> 01:21:12.067
Plus they also provided a pack of vinegar,

01:21:12.067 --> 01:21:14.336
because you can't eat bao without vinegar.

01:21:14.336 --> 01:21:15.704
Next we have the congees.

01:21:15.704 --> 01:21:17.005
In terms of flavors,

01:21:17.005 --> 01:21:21.476
we've got the century egg
and pork, a staple congee.

01:21:21.476 --> 01:21:25.580
This would be sour pickle and chicken.

01:21:25.580 --> 01:21:28.550
And over here we've got
the chicken and egg.

01:21:28.550 --> 01:21:33.555
This is the century egg and pork.

01:21:33.989 --> 01:21:36.524
In goes — I don't
actually like century egg.

01:21:36.524 --> 01:21:37.959
It's stanky,

01:21:37.959 --> 01:21:42.464
but not as stanky as the
authentic century egg.

01:21:42.464 --> 01:21:44.299
And the youtiao,

01:21:44.299 --> 01:21:47.869
the crispy Chinese
cruller, or dough stick.

01:21:47.869 --> 01:21:49.905
I mean, there are so many
different names for this thing,

01:21:49.905 --> 01:21:54.409
but this is the heart of
every Chinese breakfast.

01:21:54.409 --> 01:21:55.944
This goes well with soy milk.

01:21:55.944 --> 01:21:56.945
You can dip it in soy milk,

01:21:56.945 --> 01:21:58.446
you can dip it in congee.

01:21:58.446 --> 01:22:00.415
It's like a churro but not sweet.

01:22:01.816 --> 01:22:02.918
A bit chewy.

01:22:02.918 --> 01:22:06.855
These things are always
best right out the wok.

01:22:06.855 --> 01:22:10.292
Continuing on with our Chinese breakfasts,

01:22:10.292 --> 01:22:12.227
this is just super cute.

01:22:12.227 --> 01:22:14.796
This is something that's called a tea egg.

01:22:14.796 --> 01:22:17.532
You get these in one or four.

01:22:19.234 --> 01:22:23.104
And you're eating a tea egg,
you gotta have some youtiao.

01:22:24.472 --> 01:22:27.742
And if you're having youtiao,
you gotta have some congee.

01:22:29.010 --> 01:22:30.078
Mm-hmm.

01:22:30.078 --> 01:22:31.446
That's the trifecta.

01:22:31.446 --> 01:22:33.648
It's the holy trinity
of Chinese breakfasts.

01:22:33.648 --> 01:22:37.352
We have the crispy chicken spring rolls,

01:22:37.352 --> 01:22:41.723
although they've lost a bit of spring.

01:22:41.723 --> 01:22:42.991
What is --

01:22:42.991 --> 01:22:45.126
I feel like one of those
sausage-finger people

01:22:45.126 --> 01:22:47.429
from "Everything Everywhere All at Once."

01:22:49.831 --> 01:22:51.733
I didn't realize we were in the

01:22:51.733 --> 01:22:55.003
floppy-crispy-spring-roll universe.

01:22:55.003 --> 01:22:57.572
There's also a

01:22:57.572 --> 01:23:01.076
chicken chop and egg Chinese-style roll,

01:23:01.076 --> 01:23:03.745
although really this is more of a wrap.

01:23:03.745 --> 01:23:04.713
And what do we have in here?

01:23:04.713 --> 01:23:06.881
We've got chicken breast.

01:23:06.881 --> 01:23:10.585
It looks like cucumber, leek.

01:23:10.585 --> 01:23:12.654
This is what's known as a báo cuì,

01:23:12.654 --> 01:23:15.623
which literally translates
to "thin and crispy"

01:23:15.623 --> 01:23:16.992
and is meant to be thin and crispy,

01:23:16.992 --> 01:23:20.228
but it's more like thin
and flaccid right now.

01:23:20.228 --> 01:23:21.629
I think this is tianmian sauce,

01:23:21.629 --> 01:23:26.368
which is a sweet bean paste.

01:23:26.368 --> 01:23:27.602
I have to say this.

01:23:27.602 --> 01:23:32.140
The Chinese breakfast
at KFC is next level.

01:23:32.140 --> 01:23:34.009
I want all of that.

01:23:34.009 --> 01:23:35.377
Are you kidding me?

01:23:35.377 --> 01:23:36.711
All of that looks incredible.

01:23:36.711 --> 01:23:39.748
Next, let's talk about the
non-Chinese breakfasts.

01:23:39.748 --> 01:23:42.350
So, we've got our panini
offering right here.

01:23:42.350 --> 01:23:45.353
We're going to begin with the
cheese and sausage panini.

01:23:45.353 --> 01:23:48.757
Just your regular — I think
it's actually ciabatta bread.

01:23:48.757 --> 01:23:53.261
Now we've got the
cheese, sausage, and egg.

01:23:53.261 --> 01:23:57.232
The cheese and chicken panini.

01:23:57.232 --> 01:24:02.070
The cheese and thick omelet panini.

01:24:02.070 --> 01:24:05.907
Now, this is interesting
because this is a rolled omelet.

01:24:05.907 --> 01:24:08.610
I think in Japan they
would call it a tamagoyaki.

01:24:08.610 --> 01:24:11.846
Here we've got the chicken chop

01:24:11.846 --> 01:24:15.717
thick-rolled-omelet double panini.

01:24:15.717 --> 01:24:17.385
These three are special.

01:24:17.385 --> 01:24:18.553
We got them just for you.

01:24:18.553 --> 01:24:20.789
They are new offerings on the KFC menu.

01:24:20.789 --> 01:24:23.758
In fact, KFC has been really
good at updating its menu.

01:24:23.758 --> 01:24:26.995
Pretty much every month they're
going to have new stuff.

01:24:26.995 --> 01:24:30.532
This is their soufflé lineup.

01:24:30.532 --> 01:24:33.868
The cheese and egg soufflé panini.

01:24:33.868 --> 01:24:38.440
It's basically the same eggy thing,

01:24:38.440 --> 01:24:41.743
but it looks like it's
worked out more in the gym.

01:24:41.743 --> 01:24:43.511
It's got a better pump.

01:24:43.511 --> 01:24:48.516
Next we've got the chicken
chop and egg soufflé panini.

01:24:48.983 --> 01:24:51.219
I just want to do a
side-by-side comparison.

01:24:51.219 --> 01:24:52.921
Is it not the same thing?

01:24:52.921 --> 01:24:55.957
And I saved the fanciest
of them all for last.

01:24:55.957 --> 01:25:00.328
This is the beef fillet egg soufflé.

01:25:00.328 --> 01:25:01.162
Oh, look at that.

01:25:01.162 --> 01:25:03.131
They even made it rhyme.

01:25:03.131 --> 01:25:07.202
OK, comes in its very own special box.

01:25:07.202 --> 01:25:11.106
OK, so we've got the fluffy soufflé,

01:25:11.106 --> 01:25:15.210
and then there's mashed potato

01:25:15.210 --> 01:25:16.978
in my panini

01:25:16.978 --> 01:25:18.413
and the beef fillet.

01:25:18.413 --> 01:25:22.317
Now we have le French again. Le Français.

01:25:22.317 --> 01:25:23.551
That was really bad.

01:25:23.551 --> 01:25:26.020
I'm pretty bad at the
French accent. Sorry.

01:25:26.020 --> 01:25:30.558
We have the smoked chicken
French-style croissant bread.

01:25:30.558 --> 01:25:32.127
It's basically a Croissan'wich.

01:25:32.127 --> 01:25:36.197
It's a square croissant with sesame seeds.

01:25:36.197 --> 01:25:40.301
And le bacon and egg

01:25:40.301 --> 01:25:42.337
French-style croissant bread.

01:25:42.337 --> 01:25:44.572
The bacon and egg
French-style croissant bread,

01:25:44.572 --> 01:25:46.174
if my accent was terrible.

01:25:46.174 --> 01:25:48.009
Not as impressive with the paninis.

01:25:49.010 --> 01:25:50.278
We've kind of got those here.

01:25:50.278 --> 01:25:51.346
And, of course,

01:25:51.346 --> 01:25:54.182
if you can't get enough of
the Western-style breakfast,

01:25:54.182 --> 01:25:56.284
you can also get single add-on items

01:25:56.284 --> 01:25:59.587
such as an egg, sunny-side up.

01:25:59.587 --> 01:26:03.091
You can also get a nice juicy sausage.

01:26:03.091 --> 01:26:04.526
Hash browns.

01:26:05.660 --> 01:26:06.494
Always a must.

01:26:06.494 --> 01:26:09.430
This is the egg and vegetable soup.

01:26:09.430 --> 01:26:12.333
Here we've got the Hong Kong-style

01:26:12.333 --> 01:26:14.736
big crispy chicken thigh rice.

01:26:14.736 --> 01:26:19.541
This section beneath it is just
literally filled with rice.

01:26:19.541 --> 01:26:24.012
And this is the spicy meat
sauce grilled chicken rice.

01:26:24.012 --> 01:26:28.316
Here are two additional
non-chicken sides that we have.

01:26:28.316 --> 01:26:31.152
Corn and wavy fries.

01:26:31.152 --> 01:26:32.720
I get a whole chocolate cake.

01:26:32.720 --> 01:26:35.089
KFC in the US.

01:26:35.089 --> 01:26:37.058
I don't know why they
don't sell it by slices.

01:26:37.058 --> 01:26:39.227
Guess it's for the whole
family or whatever.

01:26:39.227 --> 01:26:40.295
What can I say about chocolate cake?

01:26:40.295 --> 01:26:43.298
It's chocolate. It's got
frosting on it. It's very good.

01:26:43.298 --> 01:26:44.365
I'm not going to bite into it.

01:26:44.365 --> 01:26:46.568
We're going to donate it, so
I don't want to screw it up.

01:26:46.568 --> 01:26:47.735
Trust me, it's good.

01:26:47.735 --> 01:26:50.705
These are our exclusive desserts.

01:26:50.705 --> 01:26:53.441
Let's begin with KFC's bestseller,

01:26:53.441 --> 01:26:55.877
the Portuguese-style egg tarts,

01:26:55.877 --> 01:26:57.912
or just the egg tarts for short.

01:26:57.912 --> 01:27:00.515
And if you can't eat two whole egg tarts,

01:27:00.515 --> 01:27:04.786
then you can go for the baby egg tarts.

01:27:04.786 --> 01:27:07.155
Oh, look how cute they are! They're tiny.

01:27:07.155 --> 01:27:10.191
KFC offers a Basque cheesecake,

01:27:10.191 --> 01:27:13.761
and this is the red bean pie.

01:27:15.897 --> 01:27:16.898
That's delicious.

01:27:16.898 --> 01:27:20.835
KFC offers an original ice cream cone,

01:27:20.835 --> 01:27:23.371
but because we got it delivered,

01:27:23.371 --> 01:27:28.276
that's the cone, and
this is the ice cream.

01:27:28.276 --> 01:27:29.544
Ah!

01:27:29.544 --> 01:27:31.913
OK, I guess that's how I'm
supposed to take it out.

01:27:31.913 --> 01:27:33.748
I'm just going to drink
the ice cream. Here we go.

01:27:33.748 --> 01:27:35.617
This is a first.

01:27:35.617 --> 01:27:37.752
Oh! Oh! Oh! OK.

01:27:37.752 --> 01:27:38.886
OK, all right.

01:27:38.886 --> 01:27:40.154
We're going to put it back.

01:27:40.154 --> 01:27:43.091
Sundaes, we've got four of them.

01:27:43.091 --> 01:27:46.661
Strawberry. Brown sugar and bubble sauce.

01:27:46.661 --> 01:27:49.264
I assume bubble as in bubble tea.

01:27:49.264 --> 01:27:54.068
This here is the mango
grapefruit sundae.

01:27:54.068 --> 01:27:58.940
New on the menu, the North
American blueberry sauce.

01:27:58.940 --> 01:28:03.511
Here, we've also got
supersoft-mochi sundaes.

01:28:03.511 --> 01:28:06.447
This is the strawberry flavor,

01:28:06.447 --> 01:28:09.584
and this is the one that I guess

01:28:09.584 --> 01:28:12.387
is basically the milk-tea version,

01:28:12.387 --> 01:28:14.355
but with mochi balls on top.

01:28:14.355 --> 01:28:17.425
Following on in the footsteps
of the mochi sundae,

01:28:17.425 --> 01:28:21.629
there's also supersoft
KFC mochi ice cream,

01:28:21.629 --> 01:28:22.997
which comes in four flavors.

01:28:22.997 --> 01:28:25.566
This one is strawberry.

01:28:25.566 --> 01:28:27.835
Ah, no, this one's strawberry Oreo.

01:28:27.835 --> 01:28:30.938
You can also get regular strawberry, Oreo,

01:28:30.938 --> 01:28:33.875
and taro flavor.

01:28:33.875 --> 01:28:35.443
That's actually pretty tasty.

01:28:35.443 --> 01:28:38.579
Drinks. We got a bunch
of them here in the US,

01:28:38.579 --> 01:28:39.547
starting down here.

01:28:39.547 --> 01:28:41.783
Something that is new to America,

01:28:41.783 --> 01:28:45.286
a lemon-lime beverage called Starry.

01:28:45.286 --> 01:28:49.023
Sierra Mist is out. Starry's in. And ...

01:28:52.327 --> 01:28:54.162
tastes almost exactly like 7Up.

01:28:54.162 --> 01:28:55.863
You can also get Mountain Dew.

01:28:55.863 --> 01:28:56.864
Oh, yeah.

01:28:56.864 --> 01:29:00.068
A personal favorite:
Mountain Dew Sweet Lightning.

01:29:00.068 --> 01:29:01.636
I think you can only get it at KFC.

01:29:01.636 --> 01:29:03.137
It's, like, peach Mountain Dew.

01:29:04.806 --> 01:29:06.808
I know it's not good for
me, but man, it's so good.

01:29:06.808 --> 01:29:09.310
This is supposed to be a lemonade but

01:29:11.913 --> 01:29:14.682
is in fact more Sweet
Lightning. Not complaining,

01:29:14.682 --> 01:29:16.317
but you can also get
the Colonel's lemonade.

01:29:16.317 --> 01:29:19.487
And last but not least, sweet tea.

01:29:19.487 --> 01:29:20.555
Oh, yeah.

01:29:22.423 --> 01:29:24.525
The sweet tea actually is good.

01:29:24.525 --> 01:29:25.760
Love all these beverages.

01:29:25.760 --> 01:29:28.996
These are all of our exclusive drinks.

01:29:28.996 --> 01:29:33.534
Let's begin over here with
the most Chinese of them all.

01:29:33.534 --> 01:29:34.802
Soy milk.

01:29:34.802 --> 01:29:36.904
We have Budweiser.

01:29:36.904 --> 01:29:41.376
The nine-fruits orange juice.

01:29:41.376 --> 01:29:43.911
Then you've got your milk tea

01:29:43.911 --> 01:29:46.781
with a very cute Colonel Sanders,

01:29:46.781 --> 01:29:50.618
and a bubble tea, which is just as cute

01:29:50.618 --> 01:29:53.621
and has the little tapioca
pearls at the bottom too.

01:29:53.621 --> 01:29:56.824
Over here, the three-lemon tea,

01:29:56.824 --> 01:30:00.728
consisting of lemon, lime, and orange.

01:30:00.728 --> 01:30:02.630
It's basically just lemon juice.

01:30:02.630 --> 01:30:04.832
Yeah, I can see why
it's called three lemon.

01:30:05.833 --> 01:30:08.102
The heartwarming

01:30:08.102 --> 01:30:11.873
three black goji oat drink.

01:30:11.873 --> 01:30:14.776
Oh, if you can see the little

01:30:14.776 --> 01:30:16.677
bits of red stuff floating in there,

01:30:16.677 --> 01:30:18.880
it's got actual goji berries.

01:30:20.381 --> 01:30:24.352
It makes me feel like a
middle-aged Chinese auntie

01:30:24.352 --> 01:30:26.020
with curlers in my hair.

01:30:26.020 --> 01:30:28.956
But in the best way possible.
I feel, I don't know,

01:30:28.956 --> 01:30:30.958
I feel like I'm wearing PJs.

01:30:30.958 --> 01:30:35.062
I think was the snow-top coffee,

01:30:35.062 --> 01:30:38.933
which is basically an iced latte
with a dollop of ice cream.

01:30:38.933 --> 01:30:42.103
And this also would've looked different

01:30:42.103 --> 01:30:43.204
when it first arrived.

01:30:43.204 --> 01:30:46.441
This is called the cute bubble milk.

01:30:46.441 --> 01:30:48.342
Basically it's just straight-up milk

01:30:48.342 --> 01:30:49.877
with a layer of milk foam,

01:30:49.877 --> 01:30:54.282
and it would've had a smiley
face dusted in cocoa powder.

01:30:54.282 --> 01:30:55.283
Oh, and I forgot to mention,

01:30:55.283 --> 01:30:59.020
there's also a hot lemon drink
that we weren't able to get.

01:30:59.020 --> 01:31:00.421
These are the K coffees.

01:31:00.421 --> 01:31:03.391
K coffees come in hot or cold varieties.

01:31:03.391 --> 01:31:06.394
You can get Americano,
your standard latte,

01:31:06.394 --> 01:31:07.862
your oat-milk latte,

01:31:07.862 --> 01:31:11.199
your rich-milk latte, your coconut latte.

01:31:11.199 --> 01:31:14.435
Then you can also get the vanilla latte,

01:31:14.435 --> 01:31:18.906
a hazelnut latte, sea salt
and macadamia nut latte,

01:31:18.906 --> 01:31:21.742
and there's also your regular cappuccino

01:31:21.742 --> 01:31:23.911
and caramel macchiatos.

01:31:26.614 --> 01:31:29.116
Let's talk cultural perceptions.

01:31:29.116 --> 01:31:32.553
In terms of prestige,
KFC really is the OG.

01:31:32.553 --> 01:31:35.590
They opened in 1987, before Macky D's,

01:31:35.590 --> 01:31:37.692
and back then they would've also been seen

01:31:37.692 --> 01:31:39.660
as sort of a window to the West,

01:31:39.660 --> 01:31:43.331
this fancy cosmopolitan place to be seen.

01:31:43.331 --> 01:31:44.765
But over time,

01:31:44.765 --> 01:31:48.536
they've really become quite entrenched

01:31:48.536 --> 01:31:50.171
here in China,

01:31:50.171 --> 01:31:53.140
and they're now seen as
a foreign fast-food brand

01:31:53.140 --> 01:31:57.345
that I would say has a lot
of Chinese characteristics.

01:31:57.345 --> 01:32:00.081
For example, the congee, the
breakfast menu, et cetera.

01:32:00.081 --> 01:32:02.817
KFC's rep in this country, they're No. 1.

01:32:02.817 --> 01:32:05.286
They're No. 1 with fast-food chicken.

01:32:05.286 --> 01:32:07.054
We got Popeyes, we got,

01:32:07.054 --> 01:32:08.489
I guess you'd want to put Chick-fil-A,

01:32:08.489 --> 01:32:09.957
but that's more sandwiches.

01:32:09.957 --> 01:32:14.395
As far as fast chicken-on-the-bone places,

01:32:14.395 --> 01:32:18.533
Wingstop is wings, and Popeyes, and KFC.

01:32:18.533 --> 01:32:20.668
Reputation is pretty much,
like, you're going to get

01:32:20.668 --> 01:32:24.405
a decent piece of chicken
and a lot of sides.

01:32:24.405 --> 01:32:25.840
In terms of convenience,

01:32:25.840 --> 01:32:27.542
KFC has its own delivery service,

01:32:27.542 --> 01:32:31.979
but it also uses third-party
suppliers like everybody else.

01:32:31.979 --> 01:32:33.748
But unlike in the US,

01:32:33.748 --> 01:32:36.450
where KFC is very much takeout-focused,

01:32:36.450 --> 01:32:39.687
here in China, they're more
about the dine-in experience,

01:32:39.687 --> 01:32:41.756
especially with the extended family.

01:32:41.756 --> 01:32:45.159
KFC is incredibly convenient, reliable.

01:32:45.159 --> 01:32:47.061
I wouldn't hang out at one or dine there.

01:32:47.061 --> 01:32:48.195
I would take it to go.

01:32:48.195 --> 01:32:50.097
One thing I should say about KFC,

01:32:50.097 --> 01:32:52.667
as much as they work on
having quality control,

01:32:52.667 --> 01:32:54.902
you could tell if a KFC is good or bad

01:32:54.902 --> 01:32:57.471
by how dark the chicken
is when it comes out.

01:32:57.471 --> 01:32:59.540
Like, the one that we did today,

01:32:59.540 --> 01:33:02.910
I don't think they changed
the oil in a while.

01:33:02.910 --> 01:33:04.946
The chicken was looking a
little darker than it should.

01:33:04.946 --> 01:33:08.749
So that's kind of a
thing you gotta consider.

01:33:08.749 --> 01:33:11.319
Convenience, usually the
service is pretty quick.

01:33:11.319 --> 01:33:13.454
But it's April 27th,

01:33:13.454 --> 01:33:16.257
so if somebody watching
this happened to get KFC

01:33:16.257 --> 01:33:20.995
from Uber or DoorDash on
April 27th around 11:30

01:33:20.995 --> 01:33:25.099
and your meal took longer
than you wanted, my fault.

01:33:25.099 --> 01:33:27.034
Our big order pretty much
backed everything up.

01:33:27.034 --> 01:33:29.637
Anyway, so it's usually
convenient when you don't live

01:33:29.637 --> 01:33:31.772
in a neighborhood where
they shoot a "Food Wars."

01:33:31.772 --> 01:33:35.376
So, in terms of adaptability,
KFC, as we mentioned before,

01:33:35.376 --> 01:33:40.014
was the first to offer
congee and Chinese cruller,

01:33:40.014 --> 01:33:41.949
soy milk on their breakfast menus.

01:33:41.949 --> 01:33:44.285
Also, unlike McDonald's,

01:33:44.285 --> 01:33:47.054
which kind of played up its
foreignness a little bit,

01:33:47.054 --> 01:33:49.190
KFC when they came to the China market

01:33:49.190 --> 01:33:53.060
had high-level managers who
actually spoke the language,

01:33:53.060 --> 01:33:54.962
and so they adapted very quickly.

01:33:54.962 --> 01:33:57.965
For example, there are lots
of regional differences

01:33:57.965 --> 01:34:01.235
in terms of how much spicy people can eat.

01:34:01.235 --> 01:34:03.337
Like, people over in
Shanghai were complaining

01:34:03.337 --> 01:34:05.773
that the spicy chicken was too spicy,

01:34:05.773 --> 01:34:08.609
but people over in Hunan in Central China

01:34:08.609 --> 01:34:10.678
were complaining that
it wasn't spicy enough.

01:34:10.678 --> 01:34:12.546
So they were very quick to react.

01:34:12.546 --> 01:34:15.349
I think KFC, Kentucky
Fried Chicken, Kentucky,

01:34:15.349 --> 01:34:16.417
Kentucky's in the United States,

01:34:16.417 --> 01:34:19.153
so pretty much is local country tastes.

01:34:20.187 --> 01:34:21.856
Yeah, they do the Nashville hot thing,

01:34:21.856 --> 01:34:24.825
they occasionally bring
sauces in and out, but.

01:34:24.825 --> 01:34:27.662
Rivals, KFC basically has none.

01:34:27.662 --> 01:34:29.563
I mean, it's numero uno.

01:34:29.563 --> 01:34:31.298
Over 9,000 stores.

01:34:31.298 --> 01:34:33.634
Double the market share of McDonald's.

01:34:33.634 --> 01:34:36.637
Way, way, way far ahead in the distance.

01:34:36.637 --> 01:34:38.472
Unless they sit on their laurels,

01:34:38.472 --> 01:34:42.276
they're probably going to be
cruising at No. 1 for a while.

01:34:42.276 --> 01:34:44.011
KFC versus Popeyes,

01:34:44.011 --> 01:34:47.181
I would say KFC has in America

01:34:47.181 --> 01:34:51.686
at least four times as many locations.

01:34:51.686 --> 01:34:55.856
Yeah, I think Popeyes tastes better, but,

01:34:55.856 --> 01:34:57.158
I mean, as far as business is concerned,

01:34:57.158 --> 01:34:58.426
KFC's not sweating it.

01:35:00.795 --> 01:35:03.030
In China, this spicy chicken burger

01:35:03.030 --> 01:35:07.601
is 19.5 yuan, or 2.83 US dollars.

01:35:07.601 --> 01:35:10.504
A US spicy chicken sandwich is $6.99,

01:35:10.504 --> 01:35:12.940
or 48.10 yuan.

01:35:12.940 --> 01:35:16.410
That is a 147% price increase.

01:35:16.410 --> 01:35:21.415
Make it a meal. Add a medium
fries and a medium Pepsi,

01:35:21.415 --> 01:35:25.653
and the cost goes up to 42 yuan, or $6.10.

01:35:25.653 --> 01:35:29.290
Still less than the cost
of a sandwich in the US.

01:35:29.290 --> 01:35:33.027
Our US combo with tax is $13.75,

01:35:33.027 --> 01:35:35.563
or 94.61 yuan.

01:35:35.563 --> 01:35:40.267
That is a 125.4% increase
compared to China.

01:35:40.267 --> 01:35:42.503
Our most expensive single menu item

01:35:42.503 --> 01:35:46.340
is the fried-chicken
bucket and Budweiser meal,

01:35:46.340 --> 01:35:49.543
which is 146 yuan, or $21,

01:35:49.543 --> 01:35:52.379
and it gets you eight spicy wings,

01:35:52.379 --> 01:35:56.851
eight New Orleans wings,
and four Budweisers.

01:35:56.851 --> 01:35:59.620
I mean, I don't know where
the other three went.

01:35:59.620 --> 01:36:01.422
Honestly, they must have just gotten lost

01:36:01.422 --> 01:36:03.424
on the road or something.

01:36:03.424 --> 01:36:07.795
In the US, we have two
menu items costing $49.99,

01:36:07.795 --> 01:36:11.265
or 343.97 yuan.

01:36:11.265 --> 01:36:13.400
That's either the 16-piece chicken meal

01:36:13.400 --> 01:36:15.402
or the 16-piece tenders meal.

01:36:15.402 --> 01:36:18.506
Both come with four large
sides and eight biscuits.

01:36:20.908 --> 01:36:23.711
Unfortunately, KFC doesn't
share its nutrition data

01:36:23.711 --> 01:36:24.578
with the public.

01:36:24.578 --> 01:36:28.048
But what we do know is
that in 2020, Yum China,

01:36:28.048 --> 01:36:31.085
which owns KFC and
Pizza Hut here in China,

01:36:31.085 --> 01:36:34.955
partnered with the Chinese
Nutrition Society to research

01:36:34.955 --> 01:36:37.758
and apply best nutritional
practices for the brand.

01:36:37.758 --> 01:36:40.628
KFC in the US does have
nutrition info available.

01:36:40.628 --> 01:36:42.530
Here are a few stats. All right.

01:36:42.530 --> 01:36:45.633
If you get the Kentucky
grilled chicken drumstick,

01:36:45.633 --> 01:36:46.967
it's 80 calories.

01:36:46.967 --> 01:36:49.136
Crisp it up a little bit
with the original recipe

01:36:49.136 --> 01:36:50.137
or the spicy,

01:36:50.137 --> 01:36:51.806
now it's 130 calories.

01:36:51.806 --> 01:36:55.042
Want to make it extra crispy,
like this one in my stomach?

01:36:55.910 --> 01:36:58.279
Now you've increased the calories to 170.

01:36:58.279 --> 01:37:02.316
That's 112.5% more calories
than the Kentucky grilled.

01:37:02.316 --> 01:37:04.952
Get real, though. It's
Kentucky Fried Chicken.

01:37:04.952 --> 01:37:05.853
If you want grilled chicken,

01:37:05.853 --> 01:37:07.621
go dust off your George Foreman.

01:37:07.621 --> 01:37:10.291
Speaking of calories, what
menu items have the most?

01:37:10.291 --> 01:37:11.559
If you're going with the chicken,

01:37:11.559 --> 01:37:14.895
the extra crispy, a
breast is 530 calories.

01:37:14.895 --> 01:37:18.365
Sandwich, the recently
discontinued Double Down

01:37:18.365 --> 01:37:20.367
has 950 calories.

01:37:20.367 --> 01:37:23.637
For reference, a Big Mac has 550.

01:37:23.637 --> 01:37:25.906
And for sides, the fries
are the top of the list.

01:37:25.906 --> 01:37:28.309
An individual has 320 calories.

01:37:28.309 --> 01:37:29.310
And then the family size,

01:37:29.310 --> 01:37:31.045
which, let's be honest,
it's for one person,

01:37:31.045 --> 01:37:33.047
has 840 calories.

01:37:33.047 --> 01:37:34.215
I have been informed

01:37:34.215 --> 01:37:36.650
that my fellow producer Yuelei Song

01:37:36.650 --> 01:37:39.787
said that their favorite
thing on the KFC menu

01:37:39.787 --> 01:37:41.755
is in fact the pot pie.

01:37:41.789 --> 01:37:42.790
Would've been nice if you said something

01:37:42.790 --> 01:37:44.091
while was going off about it.

01:37:44.091 --> 01:37:46.060
Oh, God. There's peas in it?

01:37:46.060 --> 01:37:48.562
What else is in here? What is this?

01:37:48.629 --> 01:37:50.364
Tianran: From calorie
counts to portion sizes,

01:37:50.364 --> 01:37:52.166
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:37:52.166 --> 01:37:54.869
between Lay's in the US and in China.

01:37:54.869 --> 01:37:57.071
This is "Food Wars."

01:37:59.273 --> 01:38:02.576
In China, Lay's chips come in 14,

01:38:02.576 --> 01:38:05.112
that's right, 14 sizes.

01:38:05.112 --> 01:38:08.816
Coming in at our smallest
chip bag, 12 grams,

01:38:08.816 --> 01:38:12.987
23, 40, there's a 45 but
we couldn't get that,

01:38:12.987 --> 01:38:15.823
60, 65, 70,

01:38:15.823 --> 01:38:18.025
75 grams, 80, 90,

01:38:18.025 --> 01:38:22.263
104, 116, 135,

01:38:22.263 --> 01:38:25.633
and 220 grams

01:38:25.633 --> 01:38:27.668
for our largest chip packet.

01:38:27.668 --> 01:38:30.070
In the US, Lay's come in six sizes.

01:38:30.070 --> 01:38:31.772
There's only four. Let me explain.

01:38:31.772 --> 01:38:33.207
Down here, the smallest bag

01:38:33.207 --> 01:38:36.844
is the multipack 28-gram
bag, the vending-machine bag.

01:38:36.844 --> 01:38:40.247
Move one up to a 2.625 ounce,

01:38:40.247 --> 01:38:43.617
or 74.4 grams. So specific.

01:38:43.617 --> 01:38:45.119
Then, in the middle,
which I couldn't find,

01:38:45.119 --> 01:38:47.721
is the 2.75-ounce, or 78-gram, bag.

01:38:47.721 --> 01:38:48.689
In the middle here, the classic, I mean,

01:38:48.689 --> 01:38:50.324
this is the one you see everywhere.

01:38:50.324 --> 01:38:53.527
The 8-ounce, or 226-gram, bag.

01:38:53.527 --> 01:38:56.430
In the middle here,
missing, is the family size.

01:38:56.430 --> 01:38:59.166
Too tragic for the American
family. They don't get to see

01:38:59.166 --> 01:39:03.737
the 10.5-ounce, or 297.6-gram, bag.

01:39:03.737 --> 01:39:06.540
But of course, the size
that we always have,

01:39:06.540 --> 01:39:10.678
old reliable, the biggest
size, the party size,

01:39:10.678 --> 01:39:12.246
368 grams.

01:39:12.246 --> 01:39:14.148
That means the biggest bag in the US

01:39:14.148 --> 01:39:18.052
is 67.3% larger than the
biggest bag in China.

01:39:18.052 --> 01:39:21.488
Oh, it's not the size that
matters, Joe, it's ...

01:39:21.488 --> 01:39:23.290
no, wait, no, actually it is the size.

01:39:23.290 --> 01:39:25.526
In the US, our flavored bags weigh less

01:39:25.526 --> 01:39:26.794
than the original-flavored bags.

01:39:26.794 --> 01:39:29.596
Take this bag of barbecue Lay's.

01:39:29.596 --> 01:39:33.233
It weighs 7.75 ounces,

01:39:33.233 --> 01:39:36.070
compared to the 8 ounces you
get with the original bag.

01:39:36.070 --> 01:39:38.839
Same price, but less product.

01:39:38.839 --> 01:39:41.108
Back in 2014, PepsiCo claimed, quote,

01:39:41.108 --> 01:39:43.544
"The reason for the slightly higher price

01:39:43.544 --> 01:39:45.346
per ounce for flavored chips

01:39:45.346 --> 01:39:46.947
is the added seasoning."

01:39:46.947 --> 01:39:48.215
Interesting!

01:39:48.215 --> 01:39:52.653
So, Lay's, can you
explain to me why this bag

01:39:52.653 --> 01:39:56.523
of lightly salted chips is

01:39:56.523 --> 01:40:00.894
7.75, or 7 ¾, like the flavored bags,

01:40:00.894 --> 01:40:04.064
and not 8 ounces, like
the regular salted bags,

01:40:04.064 --> 01:40:07.334
where all this has for "seasoning"

01:40:07.334 --> 01:40:09.603
is less salt than the original?

01:40:09.603 --> 01:40:10.637
Yo, Lay's!

01:40:10.637 --> 01:40:11.705
Where's my salt?

01:40:11.705 --> 01:40:15.976
A 28-gram bag in the US
supposedly contains 15 chips,

01:40:15.976 --> 01:40:17.311
according to Lay's website.

01:40:18.679 --> 01:40:20.014
Let's see how accurate this is.

01:40:20.014 --> 01:40:21.181
I hate doing this.

01:40:21.181 --> 01:40:22.349
I really hate doing this.

01:40:22.349 --> 01:40:23.984
We don't have a 28-gram bag,

01:40:23.984 --> 01:40:26.754
so I'll count the number of
chips in a 40-gram packet

01:40:26.754 --> 01:40:28.222
as a comparison.

01:40:28.222 --> 01:40:32.026
It's 1.43 times heavier,

01:40:32.026 --> 01:40:34.294
but is it just as plentiful?

01:40:35.295 --> 01:40:36.397
Joe: Four.

01:40:36.397 --> 01:40:37.798
Tianran: 10. 11.

01:40:37.798 --> 01:40:40.768
I'm running out of big chips
now. It's all the small ones.

01:40:40.768 --> 01:40:43.170
Yeah, it seems like a lot more than 15.

01:40:43.170 --> 01:40:44.938
Closer to 21.

01:40:44.938 --> 01:40:46.774
That was very generous of you, Lay's.

01:40:46.774 --> 01:40:47.875
I see the finish line.

01:40:47.875 --> 01:40:49.877
That's roughly 24.

01:40:49.877 --> 01:40:51.111
And ...

01:40:51.111 --> 01:40:52.046
oh!

01:40:52.946 --> 01:40:56.950
25 chips in a 40-gram packet.

01:40:56.950 --> 01:40:58.685
OK, I'm already incredibly impressed

01:40:58.685 --> 01:41:00.988
at the number of chips they
managed to fit into this bag,

01:41:00.988 --> 01:41:03.690
but they really could've
put more in there,

01:41:03.690 --> 01:41:06.026
and we all know that Lay's chip bags

01:41:06.026 --> 01:41:08.128
are mostly filled with air anyway.

01:41:08.128 --> 01:41:10.097
It's actually nitrogen gas,

01:41:10.097 --> 01:41:11.298
which helps preserve the chips

01:41:11.298 --> 01:41:13.133
and also acts a cushion to stop them

01:41:13.133 --> 01:41:14.601
from getting smashed in transit.

01:41:14.601 --> 01:41:15.636
I mean ...

01:41:16.703 --> 01:41:17.538
OK.

01:41:17.538 --> 01:41:20.340
But what is the
air-to-chip ratio, you ask?

01:41:21.475 --> 01:41:23.143
It's a rhetorical
question. Let's find out.

01:41:23.143 --> 01:41:25.813
I'm going to take the
smallest packet that we have,

01:41:25.813 --> 01:41:27.347
the 12 grams.

01:41:27.347 --> 01:41:32.152
So that's 533.3 milliliters.

01:41:32.152 --> 01:41:33.854
I feel like I'm on the Food Network.

01:41:33.854 --> 01:41:38.125
OK, now we need to find out
the volume of the chips.

01:41:38.125 --> 01:41:39.293
15.

01:41:39.293 --> 01:41:42.763
Our ratio is

01:41:42.763 --> 01:41:46.533
0.028 chips to air,

01:41:46.533 --> 01:41:49.470
which makes it 2.8% chips,

01:41:49.470 --> 01:41:51.238
and the rest of it is all air.

01:41:51.238 --> 01:41:55.442
Incredibly scientifically
accurate experiment yields

01:41:55.442 --> 01:41:57.444
525 milliliters in the bag.

01:41:57.444 --> 01:42:01.849
Let's do five bags, and then
we'll just get a bigger number,

01:42:01.849 --> 01:42:04.651
then divide that by five,
because we'll have an average.

01:42:04.651 --> 01:42:06.487
Smart? Great.

01:42:06.487 --> 01:42:07.988
Oh, yeah!

01:42:07.988 --> 01:42:10.190
You guys have no idea
how satisfying this is.

01:42:12.359 --> 01:42:15.896
425 divided by five equals

01:42:15.896 --> 01:42:17.664
85.

01:42:17.664 --> 01:42:18.532
I forgot what it was.

01:42:18.532 --> 01:42:21.535
Can someone do that
on-screen for us, please?

01:42:21.535 --> 01:42:23.904
And there's the number
we've been trying to get.

01:42:26.173 --> 01:42:28.509
Here are all the Lay's chips from China

01:42:28.509 --> 01:42:30.978
that you won't find in the US.

01:42:30.978 --> 01:42:34.248
And here are most of the
Lay's chips from the US

01:42:34.248 --> 01:42:35.782
you won't find in China.

01:42:35.782 --> 01:42:38.519
All right, let's start
with the exclusive flavors

01:42:38.519 --> 01:42:40.420
for the classic chip style.

01:42:40.420 --> 01:42:42.956
Now, these four are
the most common flavors

01:42:42.956 --> 01:42:45.292
that you'll find here
on the Chinese market,

01:42:45.292 --> 01:42:48.896
beginning with Italian red meat.

01:42:48.896 --> 01:42:50.264
Wow, it's nice and red.

01:42:50.264 --> 01:42:52.766
They were probably going
for Bolognese sauce here.

01:42:54.334 --> 01:42:56.303
It's not offensive.

01:42:56.303 --> 01:42:57.704
But you also can't quite place

01:42:57.704 --> 01:42:59.439
what exactly they were trying to do.

01:42:59.439 --> 01:43:03.677
Next, we have the Mexican chicken tomato.

01:43:05.846 --> 01:43:07.247
Mm!

01:43:07.247 --> 01:43:09.616
Oh, that is delicious!

01:43:09.616 --> 01:43:12.486
Next, we have the

01:43:12.486 --> 01:43:15.556
Texas grilled barbecue flavor.

01:43:18.091 --> 01:43:19.793
It tastes savory.

01:43:19.793 --> 01:43:23.830
Last but not least, cucumber flavor.

01:43:24.698 --> 01:43:26.800
Why? Just why?

01:43:28.335 --> 01:43:29.870
I don't know what I'm eating.

01:43:29.870 --> 01:43:30.837
What is this?

01:43:30.837 --> 01:43:33.040
It's sweet. It's refreshing.

01:43:33.040 --> 01:43:36.243
It has an aftertaste of cucumber.

01:43:36.243 --> 01:43:39.046
I want to ask why,

01:43:39.046 --> 01:43:41.481
but I also kind of, I'm OK with it.

01:43:41.481 --> 01:43:43.617
It's kind of nice.

01:43:43.617 --> 01:43:45.152
You know, I wonder if these are popular

01:43:45.152 --> 01:43:47.054
because they're "foreign" flavors.

01:43:47.054 --> 01:43:49.389
Because we don't know
what Italian red meat

01:43:49.389 --> 01:43:52.459
or Mexican chicken tomato
is supposed to taste like,

01:43:52.459 --> 01:43:55.195
and apparently neither do you guys.

01:43:55.195 --> 01:43:59.933
All right, let's move to
our exclusive local flavors.

01:43:59.933 --> 01:44:04.705
The spicy crayfish, or
as you guys in the US

01:44:04.705 --> 01:44:07.207
would call them, crawfish.

01:44:07.207 --> 01:44:08.842
Yes!

01:44:08.842 --> 01:44:11.545
That smells legit.

01:44:11.545 --> 01:44:12.346
Ugh.

01:44:12.346 --> 01:44:13.714
It tastes a little bit less crayfish

01:44:13.714 --> 01:44:15.182
than it smells like crayfish.

01:44:16.450 --> 01:44:17.584
No, no, that's good, that's good.

01:44:17.584 --> 01:44:18.952
Oh, it's got that aftertaste.

01:44:18.952 --> 01:44:20.020
Mm.

01:44:20.020 --> 01:44:22.089
Wow, that is pretty authentic.

01:44:22.089 --> 01:44:24.891
Roasted cumin lamb skewer.

01:44:24.891 --> 01:44:28.495
Hands down my
all-time-favorite street food.

01:44:28.495 --> 01:44:30.564
This is iconic.

01:44:30.564 --> 01:44:31.965
Especially in summer,

01:44:31.965 --> 01:44:34.234
you'll see people
hanging out in the alleys

01:44:34.234 --> 01:44:36.770
with their tank top rolled up

01:44:36.770 --> 01:44:38.005
so their belly is exposed.

01:44:38.005 --> 01:44:40.274
We call that the "Beijing bikini" here.

01:44:40.274 --> 01:44:41.875
And then they'll be holding

01:44:41.875 --> 01:44:44.378
a bunch of these skewers with meat,

01:44:44.378 --> 01:44:47.114
just ripping them off and
slamming back the beers.

01:44:47.114 --> 01:44:49.750
Ugh! Best things about China

01:44:49.750 --> 01:44:51.318
is street food, honestly.

01:44:53.620 --> 01:44:54.788
Mm.

01:44:54.788 --> 01:44:56.089
No, I can see it's there.

01:44:56.089 --> 01:44:57.691
It's not as meaty as I would like,

01:44:57.691 --> 01:44:59.393
but then, look, it's a
potato chip, all right?

01:44:59.393 --> 01:45:00.794
I think they've done pretty well.

01:45:00.794 --> 01:45:02.863
What do we have here?

01:45:03.764 --> 01:45:05.132
Seaweed flavor.

01:45:05.132 --> 01:45:07.768
Roast-garlic oyster.

01:45:07.768 --> 01:45:09.836
I think they should
just rename this lineup

01:45:09.836 --> 01:45:11.505
to the street-food edition.

01:45:13.874 --> 01:45:15.075
Wasabi flavor.

01:45:16.810 --> 01:45:19.713
Oh! Oh!

01:45:19.713 --> 01:45:20.947
Ooh-hoo!

01:45:20.947 --> 01:45:22.549
If you finish a bag of this,

01:45:22.549 --> 01:45:24.084
blocked nose, gone.

01:45:24.084 --> 01:45:25.218
Mm.

01:45:25.218 --> 01:45:26.486
Fried crab.

01:45:31.758 --> 01:45:33.026
Holy crab!

01:45:33.927 --> 01:45:36.963
Wow, they've done really well.

01:45:36.963 --> 01:45:40.467
Numb and spicy hot pot.

01:45:40.467 --> 01:45:41.301
Mm!

01:45:51.712 --> 01:45:53.313
Ho-hoo!

01:45:53.313 --> 01:45:54.214
Mm!

01:45:54.214 --> 01:45:55.682
It's spicy.

01:45:55.682 --> 01:45:58.318
I haven't got the numb yet.

01:45:58.318 --> 01:45:59.486
Maybe I need to eat more?

01:45:59.486 --> 01:46:01.388
The more you eat hot pot,

01:46:01.388 --> 01:46:03.724
the more the broth simmers down,

01:46:03.724 --> 01:46:05.559
the spicier it becomes.

01:46:05.559 --> 01:46:06.893
So at the end,

01:46:06.893 --> 01:46:10.330
your hot pot is way
spicier than at the start.

01:46:10.330 --> 01:46:12.799
This feels a little bit
like that right now.

01:46:12.799 --> 01:46:17.104
Here we have another popular
flavor from the south,

01:46:17.104 --> 01:46:19.606
from Sichuan. This is roast fish.

01:46:19.606 --> 01:46:23.677
And we've got a special flavor

01:46:23.677 --> 01:46:25.979
from a past season.

01:46:25.979 --> 01:46:27.080
Truffle.

01:46:28.982 --> 01:46:29.816
Oh!

01:46:33.887 --> 01:46:34.721
OK.

01:46:34.721 --> 01:46:37.023
Maybe I'm just lowbrow. I don't
like the flavor of truffle.

01:46:37.023 --> 01:46:39.393
It tastes like a wet forest.

01:46:39.393 --> 01:46:40.627
Ugh. No, thank you.

01:46:40.627 --> 01:46:43.163
Hold these up. We have so
many exclusive flavors.

01:46:43.163 --> 01:46:46.433
It's quite robust. I was
not able to get all of them,

01:46:46.433 --> 01:46:47.968
so these are the ones I could find

01:46:47.968 --> 01:46:49.636
here in Southern California.

01:46:49.636 --> 01:46:51.738
First one, salt and vinegar.

01:46:51.738 --> 01:46:52.739
Come on, China.

01:46:52.739 --> 01:46:55.509
I like salt and vinegar better
than plain potato chips.

01:46:56.476 --> 01:46:59.312
Sweet Southern heat barbecue.

01:46:59.312 --> 01:47:01.348
Different than our regular barbecue.

01:47:01.348 --> 01:47:02.783
Sweet and barbecue flavored?

01:47:02.783 --> 01:47:05.419
I think I like these better
than regular barbecue chips.

01:47:05.419 --> 01:47:06.253
Let's compare.

01:47:06.253 --> 01:47:07.254
Regular US barbecue.

01:47:08.755 --> 01:47:09.956
Sweet Southern heat.

01:47:12.192 --> 01:47:13.226
These are better.

01:47:13.226 --> 01:47:15.896
Speaking of barbecue, honey barbecue.

01:47:19.866 --> 01:47:22.536
That's just OK. You know,
this is not very honey-ish.

01:47:22.536 --> 01:47:23.904
The one with the sweet is sweeter

01:47:23.904 --> 01:47:25.739
than the one with honey.

01:47:25.739 --> 01:47:26.773
Go figure.

01:47:26.773 --> 01:47:27.941
Oh, yeah.

01:47:27.941 --> 01:47:29.609
Cheddar and sour cream.

01:47:29.609 --> 01:47:30.677
I mean, this thing ...

01:47:32.646 --> 01:47:34.981
Yo, top five over here.

01:47:34.981 --> 01:47:35.816
These are really good.

01:47:35.816 --> 01:47:37.651
We got limón flavor.

01:47:37.651 --> 01:47:40.053
These are lime-flavored chips with

01:47:40.053 --> 01:47:41.188
I don't know who this person is.

01:47:41.188 --> 01:47:42.322
Is this the guy in "Ted Lasso"?

01:47:42.322 --> 01:47:43.323
I don't know who this is.

01:47:43.323 --> 01:47:45.892
Sazonado. Is that his name?

01:47:45.892 --> 01:47:47.027
It's, like, a one —

01:47:47.027 --> 01:47:49.996
Yuelei: Doesn't that mean
seasoned or something?

01:47:49.996 --> 01:47:51.465
I have no idea.

01:47:53.200 --> 01:47:54.034
Yeah.

01:47:54.935 --> 01:47:55.869
What?

01:47:55.869 --> 01:47:57.437
Lime and potato together?

01:47:57.437 --> 01:47:58.472
Who would've thought?

01:47:59.372 --> 01:48:00.807
I hate pickles.

01:48:01.808 --> 01:48:03.910
But I like dill.

01:48:03.910 --> 01:48:05.645
But I should, in theory, like this.

01:48:06.913 --> 01:48:08.682
Nope. Ugh.

01:48:08.682 --> 01:48:09.516
Go away forever.

01:48:09.516 --> 01:48:11.718
Do not like dill-flavored chips.

01:48:11.718 --> 01:48:14.654
They also have Flamin'
Hot dill pickle chips.

01:48:14.654 --> 01:48:15.755
Couldn't get my hands on a bag.

01:48:15.755 --> 01:48:17.390
But I did get my hands on a bag

01:48:17.390 --> 01:48:19.192
of just the Flamin' Hot chips.

01:48:19.192 --> 01:48:20.260
Oh, man.

01:48:20.260 --> 01:48:21.461
That's, like, really red.

01:48:26.533 --> 01:48:27.367
Flamin' Hot?

01:48:28.201 --> 01:48:30.303
Yeah. Yep.

01:48:30.303 --> 01:48:32.706
Spicy, yes. Flavorful, not so much.

01:48:32.706 --> 01:48:35.809
Ones I think I'm going
to like. Chili limón.

01:48:35.809 --> 01:48:38.245
Not as spicy. Way more flavorful.

01:48:38.245 --> 01:48:39.946
Oh, yeah, and the lime aftertaste.

01:48:39.946 --> 01:48:40.814
Wow, these are fantastic.

01:48:40.814 --> 01:48:42.315
These might be my favorite.

01:48:42.315 --> 01:48:46.853
If I had to organize
these in my favorites,

01:48:46.853 --> 01:48:49.556
these are my favorite.
These are delicious.

01:48:49.556 --> 01:48:50.390
These are all really good.

01:48:50.390 --> 01:48:54.628
Everything to here on is
like, would grab, do enjoy.

01:48:54.628 --> 01:48:56.897
The honey barbecue is not that sweet.

01:48:56.897 --> 01:48:57.731
Flamin' Hot.

01:48:57.731 --> 01:48:59.933
Yeah, hot but not really flavorful.

01:48:59.933 --> 01:49:02.102
And dill pickle's ... pickles suck.

01:49:02.102 --> 01:49:05.739
You can also get the adobadas flavor,

01:49:05.739 --> 01:49:08.775
the Dorito's Cool Ranch Lay's flavor,

01:49:08.775 --> 01:49:11.177
and a cheddar jalapeño,
which I really wanted to get.

01:49:11.177 --> 01:49:12.646
Couldn't get my hands on
it. I was really bummed.

01:49:12.646 --> 01:49:15.649
All right, on to our regional limited,

01:49:15.649 --> 01:49:17.317
starting with

01:49:18.518 --> 01:49:21.655
the spicy chicken with rattan pepper.

01:49:21.655 --> 01:49:24.424
Now, this a very popular
dish from Sichuan Province,

01:49:24.424 --> 01:49:25.692
down in Southwest China.

01:49:25.692 --> 01:49:28.795
That aroma is legit.

01:49:28.795 --> 01:49:30.130
Very legit.

01:49:33.667 --> 01:49:37.170
This is way more numbing than
the spicy and numbing hot pot.

01:49:38.371 --> 01:49:39.739
And more spicy too.

01:49:39.739 --> 01:49:41.274
The hot pot strikes back.

01:49:41.274 --> 01:49:44.144
This time it's the spicy hot pot.

01:49:46.479 --> 01:49:47.314
Nah.

01:49:47.314 --> 01:49:49.482
I don't taste the beef oil in there.

01:49:49.482 --> 01:49:50.517
I don't get the savory.

01:49:50.517 --> 01:49:51.885
Nah, this is meh.

01:49:51.885 --> 01:49:53.787
Sesame sauce hot pot.

01:49:54.688 --> 01:49:58.358
This is a Cantonese flavor!

01:49:58.358 --> 01:50:00.126
Ah!

01:50:00.126 --> 01:50:01.194
For once.

01:50:01.194 --> 01:50:05.632
This is Sham Tseng roast goose flavor.

01:50:07.133 --> 01:50:08.468
Oh!

01:50:08.468 --> 01:50:09.936
Oh, well done!

01:50:09.936 --> 01:50:10.804
Mm!

01:50:10.804 --> 01:50:13.139
Yes! Yes!

01:50:13.139 --> 01:50:15.775
Ha! Sham Tseng represent!

01:50:15.775 --> 01:50:16.576
Mm!

01:50:16.576 --> 01:50:19.312
Marinated chicken feet.

01:50:19.312 --> 01:50:21.114
Linyi stir-fried chicken.

01:50:21.114 --> 01:50:23.617
Now, this originates
from Shandong Province,

01:50:23.617 --> 01:50:25.552
which is over in Eastern China.

01:50:25.552 --> 01:50:28.488
They're quite fond of their
stews and braises over there,

01:50:28.488 --> 01:50:30.423
meats and vegetables that have been cooked

01:50:30.423 --> 01:50:31.391
for a very long time,

01:50:31.391 --> 01:50:34.194
so hopefully this will be very flavorful.

01:50:34.194 --> 01:50:37.697
OK, so I can taste the
sort of roast-meat flavor.

01:50:37.697 --> 01:50:39.733
Especially when you
cook with a Chinese wok,

01:50:39.733 --> 01:50:42.902
there's a bit of smokiness
that is attached to the meat

01:50:42.902 --> 01:50:44.371
after you've cooked it.

01:50:44.371 --> 01:50:45.605
I feel like I'm getting that here.

01:50:45.605 --> 01:50:47.841
We're back to the
Sichuanese flavors again.

01:50:47.841 --> 01:50:49.643
This is,

01:50:49.643 --> 01:50:50.844
it's called laziji.

01:50:50.844 --> 01:50:52.812
So it's basically stir-fried chicken

01:50:52.812 --> 01:50:56.016
in a mountain of chilies.

01:50:56.016 --> 01:50:59.119
You know, the whole point of laziji

01:50:59.119 --> 01:51:01.254
is not to eat tons of chicken,

01:51:01.254 --> 01:51:06.192
but to find chicken from
within the mountain of chilies.

01:51:06.192 --> 01:51:11.164
It's a dish that goes
especially well with beer.

01:51:12.098 --> 01:51:12.932
There we go.

01:51:14.534 --> 01:51:15.835
We have another hot pot.

01:51:15.835 --> 01:51:18.838
This, I think, is the most
pointless kind of hot pot.

01:51:18.838 --> 01:51:20.774
This is hot pot for people who can't eat

01:51:20.774 --> 01:51:22.575
spicy or numbing hot pot.

01:51:22.575 --> 01:51:26.212
For people like you out
there, we have tomato hot pot.

01:51:26.212 --> 01:51:27.580
OK, fair enough.

01:51:28.682 --> 01:51:29.949
It's quite tasty.

01:51:29.949 --> 01:51:33.486
And now for our 2023

01:51:33.486 --> 01:51:35.689
spring lineup,

01:51:35.689 --> 01:51:37.691
beginning with,

01:51:37.691 --> 01:51:38.825
oh!

01:51:39.959 --> 01:51:43.997
Salt and pepper mantis shrimp.

01:51:43.997 --> 01:51:44.931
What do we have next?

01:51:44.931 --> 01:51:47.434
Oh, beef Wellington!

01:51:47.434 --> 01:51:50.103
Oh, my God.

01:51:50.103 --> 01:51:52.105
Oh.

01:51:52.105 --> 01:51:53.206
I'm speechless.

01:51:55.608 --> 01:51:57.210
This leaves me very confused.

01:51:59.279 --> 01:52:01.014
It just tastes like butter.

01:52:01.014 --> 01:52:02.482
And last but not least,

01:52:02.482 --> 01:52:06.052
we've got the takoyaki-flavored chips.

01:52:06.052 --> 01:52:08.088
These are a Japanese street food.

01:52:09.556 --> 01:52:10.490
Mm.

01:52:10.490 --> 01:52:11.591
Oh, yeah.

01:52:11.591 --> 01:52:14.227
Oh, the smokiness is on point.

01:52:14.227 --> 01:52:18.465
We have a bunch of chip-style
varieties in the US,

01:52:18.465 --> 01:52:22.368
starting with another thick
chip variety, kettle cooked.

01:52:22.368 --> 01:52:23.269
I don't know what it means.

01:52:23.269 --> 01:52:24.604
I'm assuming they cook them in a kettle.

01:52:24.604 --> 01:52:26.439
I don't know how. I don't know
how they make regular chips.

01:52:26.439 --> 01:52:27.841
So many flavors to choose from.

01:52:27.841 --> 01:52:28.875
Sea salt and vinegar.

01:52:28.875 --> 01:52:31.044
Sea salt and cracked pepper.

01:52:31.044 --> 01:52:32.245
Mesquite barbecue.

01:52:32.245 --> 01:52:33.046
Jalapeño.

01:52:33.046 --> 01:52:35.215
Everyone not in the US, I
want to tell you right now,

01:52:35.215 --> 01:52:36.983
these chips, fantastic.

01:52:36.983 --> 01:52:38.451
These might be my favorite chips.

01:52:38.451 --> 01:52:39.385
These are so good.

01:52:41.421 --> 01:52:42.255
Mm!

01:52:43.656 --> 01:52:48.161
Other flavors include original,
Flamin' Hot, and Maui onion.

01:52:48.161 --> 01:52:49.963
All right, now on to our selection

01:52:49.963 --> 01:52:53.466
of wavy and wavy limited,

01:52:53.466 --> 01:52:56.436
beginning with our roast chicken wing.

01:52:56.436 --> 01:52:59.773
This feels thicker than the
regular chip. Very crunchy.

01:53:01.441 --> 01:53:03.343
I'm starting to get the
roast chicken in there.

01:53:03.343 --> 01:53:04.444
Yeah, that's decent.

01:53:04.444 --> 01:53:05.745
The roast squid.

01:53:07.147 --> 01:53:09.415
Not that big a fan of
roast squid, to be honest,

01:53:09.415 --> 01:53:13.653
but I will try the roast pork.

01:53:13.653 --> 01:53:18.158
It's tasty, but I can't
really get the pork in there.

01:53:18.158 --> 01:53:19.692
I think the chicken is still better.

01:53:19.692 --> 01:53:23.563
This just says pure spicy,

01:53:23.563 --> 01:53:27.801
as if we haven't already
eaten enough spicy chips.

01:53:27.801 --> 01:53:29.235
And tomato.

01:53:29.235 --> 01:53:30.970
Nah. Nah.

01:53:32.005 --> 01:53:33.740
This can stay unopened.

01:53:33.740 --> 01:53:36.276
Moving on to our wavy limited.

01:53:36.276 --> 01:53:39.179
These are a collaboration
with another snack brand

01:53:39.179 --> 01:53:40.914
here in China called Huang Fei Hong,

01:53:40.914 --> 01:53:43.416
who make spicy peanuts.

01:53:43.416 --> 01:53:47.854
This one is hot and sour chicken feet.

01:53:47.854 --> 01:53:51.324
This is the spicy peanut flavor

01:53:51.324 --> 01:53:54.928
for which the Huang Fei
Hong brand is best known.

01:53:56.229 --> 01:53:57.363
Mm!

01:53:57.363 --> 01:54:00.567
Tastes like spicy
peanuts, but in chip form.

01:54:00.567 --> 01:54:03.336
OK, I'm sure many of you
must be super curious

01:54:03.336 --> 01:54:05.205
as to what this is.

01:54:05.205 --> 01:54:08.174
This is Lay's Chocoridge,

01:54:08.174 --> 01:54:10.343
which is a collab with a brand

01:54:10.343 --> 01:54:13.413
that's literally called Le Cake.

01:54:13.413 --> 01:54:16.115
This is their
cheesecake-flavored Chocoridge.

01:54:16.115 --> 01:54:17.884
I've never had this either.

01:54:17.884 --> 01:54:21.855
A sweet dessert Lay's, wow.

01:54:21.855 --> 01:54:24.524
This is so wrong that it's so right.

01:54:24.524 --> 01:54:25.358
Wow.

01:54:27.227 --> 01:54:28.461
Wow!

01:54:29.829 --> 01:54:32.365
Now I have very high
expectations for this.

01:54:32.365 --> 01:54:36.569
Now, this is the Chocoridge
chocolate truffle.

01:54:36.569 --> 01:54:38.071
Here you can actually see how

01:54:38.071 --> 01:54:41.074
it's literally just a regular Lay's crisp

01:54:42.108 --> 01:54:43.309
covered in chocolate.

01:54:43.309 --> 01:54:44.777
Well done.

01:54:44.777 --> 01:54:46.045
This is a good collab.

01:54:46.045 --> 01:54:47.247
We have something similar.

01:54:47.247 --> 01:54:49.382
Our wavy-style chips.

01:54:49.382 --> 01:54:50.783
These are three of the many options

01:54:50.783 --> 01:54:51.985
you can get here in the US.

01:54:51.985 --> 01:54:54.254
Of course, starting with original.

01:54:54.254 --> 01:54:56.823
We also have hickory barbecue.

01:54:56.823 --> 01:54:57.991
And I don't even know what this is.

01:54:57.991 --> 01:55:01.294
This is like they combined
Funyuns and wavy together.

01:55:01.294 --> 01:55:02.295
Oh, these are weird.

01:55:04.764 --> 01:55:05.598
Skip those.

01:55:05.598 --> 01:55:07.800
You can also get wavy,
reduced-fat original,

01:55:07.800 --> 01:55:09.669
wavy ranch, wavy salt and pepper,

01:55:09.669 --> 01:55:11.037
and wavy lightly salted.

01:55:11.037 --> 01:55:13.506
Now on to our non-potato options,

01:55:13.506 --> 01:55:15.975
of which we have a lot.

01:55:15.975 --> 01:55:18.711
These are all yam.

01:55:18.711 --> 01:55:22.315
Yams have subcategories of yam crisps

01:55:22.315 --> 01:55:24.851
and yam rolls as well.

01:55:24.851 --> 01:55:29.756
These are the black sesame
and chia seed yam crisps.

01:55:29.756 --> 01:55:32.025
Man, they sound healthy, don't they?

01:55:32.025 --> 01:55:33.760
So, in traditional Chinese medicine,

01:55:33.760 --> 01:55:36.496
black sesame is thought
to help with hair growth.

01:55:36.496 --> 01:55:40.166
I've been recommended it a lot.

01:55:40.166 --> 01:55:42.802
I can taste the nuttiness
of the black sesame.

01:55:42.802 --> 01:55:44.304
Mm.

01:55:44.304 --> 01:55:47.874
And I feel like my hairline
is coming back any moment now.

01:55:47.874 --> 01:55:49.876
This is also something that adheres

01:55:49.876 --> 01:55:51.744
to traditional Chinese medicine.

01:55:51.744 --> 01:55:54.614
Chinese dates and goji berries.

01:55:54.614 --> 01:55:56.582
These are delicious.

01:55:56.582 --> 01:55:58.117
Wow.

01:55:58.117 --> 01:56:02.255
Here we have pastoral tomatoes?

01:56:03.189 --> 01:56:04.424
Roast chicken wing.

01:56:04.424 --> 01:56:07.327
On to our yam rolls.

01:56:07.327 --> 01:56:10.763
These are an upgraded version
of the crisps that you see.

01:56:10.763 --> 01:56:15.368
This is steak with Tartary buckwheat.

01:56:15.368 --> 01:56:17.103
These things are so wafer thin.

01:56:17.103 --> 01:56:19.405
They have this amazing crunch.

01:56:19.405 --> 01:56:21.140
They're airy, they're light.

01:56:21.140 --> 01:56:23.142
The very slight bitterness
of the buckwheat

01:56:23.142 --> 01:56:25.044
lends itself very well to the steak.

01:56:25.044 --> 01:56:28.314
Fragrant red stew,

01:56:28.314 --> 01:56:31.884
consisting of yam and highland barley,

01:56:31.884 --> 01:56:33.252
which is the main cereal

01:56:33.252 --> 01:56:35.455
planted on the Tibetan High Plateau.

01:56:35.455 --> 01:56:40.026
We also have taro and sweet potato chips.

01:56:40.026 --> 01:56:43.896
This is one with black
pepper and sea salt.

01:56:47.567 --> 01:56:49.736
It's very thin, yet it's not crispy.

01:56:49.736 --> 01:56:51.804
It feels almost a little bit soggy.

01:56:52.672 --> 01:56:55.041
Refreshing lime. [sighs]

01:56:56.042 --> 01:56:58.111
What's with all the refreshing chips?

01:57:02.615 --> 01:57:03.449
Pass.

01:57:03.449 --> 01:57:04.283
Sweet potato chips.

01:57:04.283 --> 01:57:05.551
Natural flavor.

01:57:07.253 --> 01:57:10.823
I know this probably
frustrates some of you at home,

01:57:10.823 --> 01:57:13.526
but the majority of people here in China

01:57:13.526 --> 01:57:16.229
open crisp packets like this,

01:57:16.229 --> 01:57:19.032
as opposed to horizontally,
like in the West,

01:57:19.032 --> 01:57:23.336
because it's easier to open
this way, easier to share.

01:57:23.336 --> 01:57:26.239
When you reach in, you don't
get salt stuck to your hand.

01:57:26.239 --> 01:57:28.574
And it's also just less effort.

01:57:28.574 --> 01:57:30.910
We don't need to brute
way our way into things.

01:57:33.513 --> 01:57:35.214
Not going to lie. It's not so bad.

01:57:35.214 --> 01:57:39.118
So, we had the regular
sweet sweet-potato chips.

01:57:39.118 --> 01:57:43.523
Now we have sweet potato
chips with added brown sugar.

01:57:44.724 --> 01:57:45.658
Ugh!

01:57:48.961 --> 01:57:50.430
Why? No!

01:57:52.832 --> 01:57:55.068
I'm going to waste as little
time as possible on these,

01:57:55.068 --> 01:57:56.869
baked chips. They're just for people

01:57:56.869 --> 01:58:00.273
who want their chips to be
more brittle and less flavored.

01:58:00.273 --> 01:58:01.407
I don't know. These suck.

01:58:01.407 --> 01:58:03.242
You have original or barbecue.

01:58:03.242 --> 01:58:04.844
Here's original.

01:58:04.844 --> 01:58:06.512
I mean, this is the third
time we've done this.

01:58:06.512 --> 01:58:07.346
Don't bother.

01:58:07.346 --> 01:58:08.714
Just trust me, don't bother.

01:58:08.714 --> 01:58:09.615
Listen to this.

01:58:09.615 --> 01:58:10.716
[chips rattling]

01:58:10.716 --> 01:58:12.051
They're all destroyed in there.

01:58:12.051 --> 01:58:14.654
They have no taste. They're flimsy.

01:58:14.654 --> 01:58:15.655
The baked are bad.

01:58:15.655 --> 01:58:18.424
There's the Better for
You and Simply brand.

01:58:18.424 --> 01:58:19.959
The Better for You is the lightly salted,

01:58:19.959 --> 01:58:22.428
lightly salted barbecue,
wavy lightly salted.

01:58:22.428 --> 01:58:23.563
All these right here.

01:58:23.563 --> 01:58:24.564
I get it.

01:58:24.564 --> 01:58:26.532
Sodium can be an issue
for snacking chips a lot,

01:58:26.532 --> 01:58:28.434
so why not go with the lightly salted?

01:58:29.335 --> 01:58:32.305
I mean, 50% less sodium?

01:58:32.305 --> 01:58:33.773
That's pretty good, right?

01:58:33.773 --> 01:58:35.508
I mean, how do these,

01:58:35.508 --> 01:58:38.511
I'm curious how these compare to ...

01:58:40.246 --> 01:58:42.348
These have 50% less?

01:58:42.348 --> 01:58:43.649
This is 100% less.

01:58:43.649 --> 01:58:45.084
I don't taste anything.

01:58:45.084 --> 01:58:46.486
Also, the Simply,

01:58:48.521 --> 01:58:52.558
I guess the whole deal is they
just use simpler ingredients.

01:58:52.558 --> 01:58:54.260
"Made with three simple ingredients,

01:58:54.260 --> 01:58:56.696
potato, sunflower oil, and sea salt."

01:58:56.696 --> 01:58:58.865
There's also the Simply
barbecue thick cut.

01:58:59.699 --> 01:59:01.033
I mean, how much better could it be?

01:59:01.033 --> 01:59:05.404
We also have two exclusives
from the Simply lineup,

01:59:05.404 --> 01:59:09.041
which have 50% less saturated fat.

01:59:09.041 --> 01:59:12.078
The refreshing lime and the seaweed.

01:59:12.078 --> 01:59:13.112
Guess what?

01:59:13.112 --> 01:59:16.983
We even have Lay's french fries.

01:59:16.983 --> 01:59:20.286
Let's go with the original flavor.

01:59:20.286 --> 01:59:22.655
These come in really
big packets, by the way.

01:59:31.397 --> 01:59:33.666
It's so incredibly salty.

01:59:33.666 --> 01:59:37.103
I am so glad that they only
gave us this tiny packet,

01:59:37.103 --> 01:59:38.271
because I am going to just ...

01:59:38.271 --> 01:59:39.372
no, I don't want the rest.

01:59:39.372 --> 01:59:40.206
Ugh.

01:59:40.206 --> 01:59:43.176
Cheese and butter french fries.

01:59:43.176 --> 01:59:44.710
Pink grapefruit flavor.

01:59:44.710 --> 01:59:48.548
I mean, you can't see this and not try it.

01:59:52.685 --> 01:59:54.520
This is really good!

01:59:57.924 --> 02:00:00.993
This is so weird, but it's really good.

02:00:00.993 --> 02:00:04.197
Hot pink grapefruit Lay's.

02:00:07.733 --> 02:00:09.902
I'm going to pick that up and eat it.

02:00:09.902 --> 02:00:11.404
It's that good.

02:00:11.404 --> 02:00:12.672
Mm!

02:00:16.142 --> 02:00:20.479
We also have seaweed-flavor french fries

02:00:20.479 --> 02:00:25.351
and tomato-flavor french fries.

02:00:25.351 --> 02:00:29.789
But I am dying to try this.

02:00:31.290 --> 02:00:34.193
Purple potato french fries.

02:00:37.663 --> 02:00:38.497
Ugh.

02:00:39.498 --> 02:00:42.201
I don't even know what that tastes like.

02:00:42.201 --> 02:00:43.035
No.

02:00:43.936 --> 02:00:46.672
Now, we have one more

02:00:46.672 --> 02:00:49.709
non-potato-chip Lay's.

02:00:50.776 --> 02:00:54.213
The air-fried chicken breast.

02:00:54.213 --> 02:00:58.751
I have absolutely no idea
how much chicken is in here.

02:00:58.751 --> 02:01:03.756
It looks like very tiny
pizzas or little crackers.

02:01:11.364 --> 02:01:13.432
It leaves me very confused.

02:01:14.300 --> 02:01:16.235
I do taste the chicken.

02:01:16.235 --> 02:01:18.204
But, hey, this is an interesting flavor.

02:01:19.372 --> 02:01:20.906
Ugh!

02:01:20.906 --> 02:01:21.974
Stax.

02:01:21.974 --> 02:01:23.743
Stax!

02:01:23.743 --> 02:01:25.278
Stax.

02:01:25.278 --> 02:01:28.281
If you've seen any other
Lay's "Food Wars" we've done,

02:01:28.281 --> 02:01:30.116
I hate these for every reason.

02:01:30.116 --> 02:01:32.952
They are Pringle-shaped chips

02:01:32.952 --> 02:01:36.188
in plastic tubes instead of plastic bags.

02:01:36.188 --> 02:01:39.258
First of all, worst container. Right?

02:01:39.258 --> 02:01:40.760
[chips rattling]

02:01:40.760 --> 02:01:44.263
Does that sound like
some chips are intact?

02:01:49.735 --> 02:01:51.470
These chips are really messed up, man.

02:01:51.470 --> 02:01:53.139
Not a pleasant experience at all,

02:01:53.139 --> 02:01:56.142
but I'm contractually
obligated to tell you,

02:01:56.142 --> 02:01:57.576
besides these two flavors,

02:01:57.576 --> 02:02:00.046
you can also get Stax
in mesquite barbecue,

02:02:00.046 --> 02:02:03.716
cheddar, salt and vinegar,
bacon and cheddar potato skins,

02:02:03.716 --> 02:02:07.186
Buffalo wings with
ranch, Xtra Flamin' Hot,

02:02:07.186 --> 02:02:08.888
Flamas, and chile limón.

02:02:10.089 --> 02:02:11.123
Please don't get them.

02:02:11.123 --> 02:02:12.425
Trust me, they suck.

02:02:12.425 --> 02:02:13.559
We've got Stax too!

02:02:13.559 --> 02:02:17.663
And in many more flavors, as you can tell.

02:02:17.663 --> 02:02:20.966
Stax is basically Lay's
take on the Pringles.

02:02:20.966 --> 02:02:23.436
But whereas Pringles took 10 years

02:02:23.436 --> 02:02:25.705
to come up with their saddle-shaped chip,

02:02:25.705 --> 02:02:27.540
which is actually known as

02:02:27.540 --> 02:02:32.144
a double-curved hyperbolic paraboloid,

02:02:32.144 --> 02:02:33.913
Stax went with a

02:02:33.913 --> 02:02:37.283
single-curved hyperbolic cylinder.

02:02:37.283 --> 02:02:39.819
So you can actually see the difference

02:02:41.287 --> 02:02:43.022
in the shape of the chip right here.

02:02:43.022 --> 02:02:44.824
The Stax, by the way,

02:02:44.824 --> 02:02:48.327
comes with a fancy-schmancy

02:02:48.327 --> 02:02:50.162
plastic tray

02:02:50.162 --> 02:02:53.566
that's meant to keep it from breaking

02:02:53.566 --> 02:02:55.901
but hasn't worked very well in this case.

02:02:55.901 --> 02:02:58.604
Here is an intact Stax,

02:02:58.604 --> 02:03:01.240
and here is an intact Pringle.

02:03:01.240 --> 02:03:03.476
To be honest, they kind of look similar.

02:03:03.476 --> 02:03:06.712
The Pringle has an extra curve down here,

02:03:06.712 --> 02:03:09.815
whereas the Stax down here
appears to be a bit more flat.

02:03:09.815 --> 02:03:14.053
Now, the Stax also comes in tomato flavor.

02:03:14.053 --> 02:03:15.488
Cucumber flavor.

02:03:15.488 --> 02:03:17.723
There are some flavors
that I would love to try,

02:03:17.723 --> 02:03:22.595
such as the sizzled barbecue flavor.

02:03:22.595 --> 02:03:26.065
Da, da, da, da, da, da, da, da. Oh, wow!

02:03:26.065 --> 02:03:28.968
This is a good plastic tray.

02:03:31.003 --> 02:03:32.772
Yeah, it tastes all right.

02:03:32.772 --> 02:03:36.675
Black pepper rib eye steak.

02:03:36.675 --> 02:03:38.811
This I am actually very excited to try.

02:03:38.811 --> 02:03:41.814
Finger-licking red braised pork.

02:03:41.814 --> 02:03:44.417
There's maybe a hint of pork in there.

02:03:44.417 --> 02:03:46.585
And some sugar and some caramelizing,

02:03:46.585 --> 02:03:47.853
but that's pretty much it.

02:03:48.788 --> 02:03:50.890
OK, we've got one for
you Stax fans out there.

02:03:50.890 --> 02:03:55.594
These are the Stax
premium, the Stax black.

02:03:55.594 --> 02:03:59.265
The Chinese name actually
says "potato workshop."

02:03:59.265 --> 02:04:03.836
And apparently, it has
real food ingredients.

02:04:03.836 --> 02:04:07.506
So, this is avocado with mustard.

02:04:10.910 --> 02:04:12.211
Why?

02:04:12.211 --> 02:04:15.147
OK, now we have purple potato,

02:04:15.147 --> 02:04:17.316
so basically sweet potato,

02:04:17.316 --> 02:04:20.486
with coconut milk.

02:04:25.024 --> 02:04:26.625
Maybe it's an acquired taste.

02:04:26.625 --> 02:04:27.593
Hoo!

02:04:27.593 --> 02:04:29.695
I mean, you guys know I don't
like truffle now anyway.

02:04:29.695 --> 02:04:31.597
I'm pretty lowbrow.

02:04:31.597 --> 02:04:33.699
But this is black-truffle-

02:04:33.699 --> 02:04:36.902
and black-pepper-flavored potato chip.

02:04:36.902 --> 02:04:40.339
Spanish-ham-flavored potato chips.

02:04:40.339 --> 02:04:43.809
I love me some Ibérico jamón.

02:04:43.809 --> 02:04:47.880
I am praying that this
is going to be tasty.

02:04:51.383 --> 02:04:53.919
Fire them all. They're rubbish.

02:04:53.919 --> 02:04:55.654
This is spicy crawfish.

02:04:57.656 --> 02:04:58.791
Mm!

02:04:58.791 --> 02:05:00.359
Oh! Yes!

02:05:01.427 --> 02:05:04.296
OK, finally we have a winner

02:05:04.296 --> 02:05:05.898
from the Stax premium lineup.

02:05:05.898 --> 02:05:06.932
This is great.

02:05:06.932 --> 02:05:11.470
And I would say that this
tastes even more authentic

02:05:11.470 --> 02:05:14.440
than the regular-potato-chip version

02:05:14.440 --> 02:05:16.242
of the spicy crayfish that we had earlier.

02:05:16.242 --> 02:05:17.343
Oh!

02:05:17.343 --> 02:05:18.711
Roast chicken skewer.

02:05:18.711 --> 02:05:20.246
Wagyu beef.

02:05:20.246 --> 02:05:23.349
Sour and sweet rose petals.

02:05:24.583 --> 02:05:26.986
Oh, come on, Lay's, you are
just playing with me now.

02:05:26.986 --> 02:05:28.487
This is delicious.

02:05:31.090 --> 02:05:32.658
Wow.

02:05:32.658 --> 02:05:35.928
Imagine sitting in a nice,

02:05:35.928 --> 02:05:38.097
warm, milky bath,

02:05:38.097 --> 02:05:39.865
floating with rose petals

02:05:39.865 --> 02:05:43.402
and eating this sweet and
sour rose petal Lay's.

02:05:43.402 --> 02:05:44.603
Wow!

02:05:44.603 --> 02:05:47.072
That would be the best evening ever.

02:05:47.072 --> 02:05:47.907
Wow.

02:05:49.675 --> 02:05:51.977
This is great, fantastic.

02:05:51.977 --> 02:05:52.978
We have a seaweed flavor.

02:05:52.978 --> 02:05:55.514
I like my seaweed. We've
had too much seaweed today.

02:05:55.514 --> 02:05:57.483
I'm pretty sure this is going to be OK.

02:05:57.483 --> 02:05:58.684
We also got Poppables.

02:05:58.684 --> 02:06:00.185
These are so stupid.

02:06:00.185 --> 02:06:01.020
What is this?

02:06:01.020 --> 02:06:02.621
We don't need a new shape.

02:06:02.621 --> 02:06:04.456
Tell everyone in the biz.

02:06:04.456 --> 02:06:06.625
We don't need new shapes.

02:06:06.625 --> 02:06:08.727
So, I don't know what this
thing's supposed to be,

02:06:08.727 --> 02:06:11.330
but you can get it in
sea salt, honey barbecue,

02:06:12.665 --> 02:06:15.701
sea salt and vinegar, white cheddar.

02:06:15.701 --> 02:06:17.870
Like, look at this.
It's all hollow inside.

02:06:20.773 --> 02:06:21.607
Ugh!

02:06:25.578 --> 02:06:27.179
It's like a giant Chex.

02:06:30.382 --> 02:06:31.750
What are we doing here?

02:06:31.750 --> 02:06:33.152
Lay's, what are we doing here?

02:06:33.152 --> 02:06:34.420
Why? What? What?

02:06:34.420 --> 02:06:35.621
What?

02:06:37.156 --> 02:06:38.157
What?

02:06:38.157 --> 02:06:40.225
Now, I know, Lay's, it seems
I'm going hard on you guys.

02:06:40.225 --> 02:06:42.728
But I have to say, ending with the dips,

02:06:42.728 --> 02:06:44.630
Lay's dips are fantastic.

02:06:44.630 --> 02:06:46.665
They have three to choose from.

02:06:46.665 --> 02:06:48.801
The smooth ranch, the French onion,

02:06:48.801 --> 02:06:51.203
and the creamy jalapeño. Couldn't get it.

02:06:51.203 --> 02:06:56.175
This French onion dip is drugs.

02:06:56.275 --> 02:06:57.676
Any chip works with it.

02:06:57.676 --> 02:07:00.179
Let's do my favorite kettle, jalapeño.

02:07:05.551 --> 02:07:06.385
Stellar.

02:07:06.385 --> 02:07:10.889
This dip works on literally everything.

02:07:12.458 --> 02:07:14.760
I would put this in my coffee if I could.

02:07:14.760 --> 02:07:17.196
It is so great. Fantastic.

02:07:17.196 --> 02:07:18.964
The dips are great. Check them out.

02:07:21.166 --> 02:07:24.870
A 75-gram bag of American
classic Lay's in China

02:07:24.870 --> 02:07:27.072
is 7.3 yuan,

02:07:27.072 --> 02:07:30.175
or $1.06.

02:07:30.175 --> 02:07:32.444
Our closest size to the 75-gram bag

02:07:32.444 --> 02:07:36.615
is the 74.4-gram bag, so 0.6 grams less.

02:07:36.615 --> 02:07:41.220
And it's $2.48, or 17.04 yuan.

02:07:41.220 --> 02:07:45.524
That is a 134% cost increase in the US.

02:07:45.524 --> 02:07:47.993
Right, but then if you take into account

02:07:47.993 --> 02:07:49.261
purchasing-power parity,

02:07:49.261 --> 02:07:52.865
then Lay's charges the
highest price in the world

02:07:52.865 --> 02:07:55.200
for its chips here in China.

02:07:57.436 --> 02:08:00.873
So, here in China, even
though the chip market

02:08:00.873 --> 02:08:04.677
only accounts for 15%
of the snack industry,

02:08:04.677 --> 02:08:08.547
Lay's accounts for 50%
of that chip market.

02:08:08.547 --> 02:08:11.550
These guys are definitely
the crème de la crème

02:08:11.550 --> 02:08:14.086
when it comes to potato
chips here in China,

02:08:14.086 --> 02:08:17.389
and they've got such a
wide variety of flavors

02:08:17.389 --> 02:08:19.925
that you will see them always

02:08:19.925 --> 02:08:22.995
in a prime shelf location

02:08:22.995 --> 02:08:25.698
in every convenience
store across the country.

02:08:25.698 --> 02:08:28.767
Lay's in the US, Lay's
is, like, the chip, right?

02:08:28.767 --> 02:08:31.370
There's other chip brands, but Lay's,

02:08:31.370 --> 02:08:33.706
probably the most ubiquitous.
You see them everywhere.

02:08:33.706 --> 02:08:35.808
They have so many different
options and styles.

02:08:35.808 --> 02:08:37.509
I think any type of potato chip

02:08:37.509 --> 02:08:39.111
that is even remotely popular,

02:08:39.111 --> 02:08:41.513
Lay's has a knockoff version of it.

02:08:41.513 --> 02:08:44.650
Always good, always available,

02:08:44.650 --> 02:08:46.885
always decently priced, I guess?

02:08:46.885 --> 02:08:48.487
I think Lay's has been incredible

02:08:48.487 --> 02:08:50.155
in adapting to the Chinese market.

02:08:50.155 --> 02:08:52.424
They've basically gone and found

02:08:52.424 --> 02:08:56.128
all of the popular flavors
and combinations in China,

02:08:56.128 --> 02:08:58.464
whether it's street
food or restaurant food,

02:08:58.464 --> 02:09:03.268
and put them into a convenient
and portable chip packet.

02:09:03.268 --> 02:09:04.937
Lay's is incredible at adapting

02:09:04.937 --> 02:09:06.105
because, as you saw before,

02:09:06.105 --> 02:09:09.308
every style they have, besides
the regular potato chip,

02:09:09.308 --> 02:09:11.977
is a style that another chip brand had

02:09:11.977 --> 02:09:13.312
that they just took on.

02:09:13.312 --> 02:09:16.782
The kettle chips, they taste
just like Miss Vickie's.

02:09:16.782 --> 02:09:19.551
They got the wavy ones,
which was Ruffles, right?

02:09:20.619 --> 02:09:21.954
The Poppables, which, I don't know,

02:09:21.954 --> 02:09:25.390
Bugles, Chex, you tell me.
Any three-dimensional chip.

02:09:25.390 --> 02:09:27.392
The Stax, which is going after Pringles.

02:09:27.392 --> 02:09:30.529
I mean, they're
bloodthirsty, this company.

02:09:30.529 --> 02:09:32.297
They will go after anyone!

02:09:34.666 --> 02:09:37.603
Our classic Lay's, aka
the American flavor,

02:09:37.603 --> 02:09:40.005
are made of potatoes, oil,

02:09:40.005 --> 02:09:42.541
American classic original seasoning,

02:09:42.541 --> 02:09:46.512
which is comprised of edible
salt, monosodium glutamate,

02:09:46.512 --> 02:09:50.149
5'-flavor nucleotide disodium,

02:09:50.149 --> 02:09:51.884
and silicon dioxide.

02:09:51.884 --> 02:09:54.586
Our classic Lay's are made up of potatoes;

02:09:54.586 --> 02:09:57.055
vegetable oil, which is canola, corn,

02:09:57.055 --> 02:10:01.093
soybean, and/or sunflower oil; and salt.

02:10:01.093 --> 02:10:03.295
Now, there are two ingredients
we wanted to highlight,

02:10:03.295 --> 02:10:06.899
which are monosodium glutamate, aka MSG,

02:10:06.899 --> 02:10:10.202
and 5'-flavor nucleotide disodium.

02:10:10.202 --> 02:10:12.437
These two ingredients are
used to give our chips

02:10:12.437 --> 02:10:14.740
a savory, umami flavor.

02:10:14.740 --> 02:10:15.774
Ah, MSG.

02:10:15.774 --> 02:10:18.544
It's the black sheep of condiments.

02:10:18.544 --> 02:10:21.046
Now, for those of you who
don't know what MSG is,

02:10:21.046 --> 02:10:23.315
it's used to add savoriness to food

02:10:23.315 --> 02:10:26.151
and was also associated
with something called

02:10:26.151 --> 02:10:27.553
"Chinese restaurant syndrome,"

02:10:27.553 --> 02:10:30.255
which has since been debunked many times.

02:10:30.255 --> 02:10:31.723
Turns out it was a hoax.

02:10:31.723 --> 02:10:33.392
But basically, the gist is,

02:10:33.392 --> 02:10:34.960
when you go to a Chinese restaurant,

02:10:34.960 --> 02:10:38.197
after eating its food,
you'll feel headaches,

02:10:38.197 --> 02:10:41.233
dizziness, sore throat, loss of appetite.

02:10:41.233 --> 02:10:43.502
You know, MSG is not the culprit.

02:10:43.502 --> 02:10:46.738
It's naturally occurring in
tomatoes, in bone broths;

02:10:46.738 --> 02:10:49.975
it's found in fermented foods, from cheese

02:10:49.975 --> 02:10:52.044
to Worcestershire sauce to soy sauce;

02:10:52.044 --> 02:10:55.581
and actually the vast
majority of MSG in the world

02:10:55.581 --> 02:10:57.115
is made through fermentation,

02:10:57.115 --> 02:10:58.584
just like yogurt or vinegar.

02:10:58.584 --> 02:11:02.321
MSG was a cause for health
concerns in the US for decades.

02:11:02.321 --> 02:11:03.956
And concern still lingers today,

02:11:03.956 --> 02:11:07.793
even though the FDA considers
the addition of MSG to foods

02:11:07.793 --> 02:11:11.663
as being generally
recognized as safe, GRAS.

02:11:11.663 --> 02:11:13.532
Both countries use the food coloring

02:11:13.532 --> 02:11:16.468
caramel color in our barbecue chips.

02:11:16.468 --> 02:11:18.337
Now, certain types of caramel color

02:11:18.337 --> 02:11:20.672
contain a byproduct called 4-MeI.

02:11:20.672 --> 02:11:23.475
4-Methylimidazole.

02:11:23.475 --> 02:11:26.511
And studies found that it
caused cancer in rats and mice,

02:11:26.511 --> 02:11:29.381
which led to campaigns calling for it

02:11:29.381 --> 02:11:30.749
to be banned from foods.

02:11:30.749 --> 02:11:33.852
But it's also worth
noting that this byproduct

02:11:33.852 --> 02:11:38.123
is found when you roast
foods like coffee and meat.

02:11:38.123 --> 02:11:40.192
And the FDA was like, "Eh, it's fine."

02:11:43.228 --> 02:11:45.564
Humans don't come close
to the levels of exposure

02:11:45.564 --> 02:11:47.299
that caused the rat tumors.

02:11:47.299 --> 02:11:48.834
That didn't stop the state of California

02:11:48.834 --> 02:11:52.704
adding it to its Proposition
65 list of chemicals, quote,

02:11:52.704 --> 02:11:55.207
"Known to the state of
California to cause cancer

02:11:55.207 --> 02:11:57.175
or reproductive toxicity."

02:11:57.175 --> 02:11:58.010
End quote.

02:12:00.479 --> 02:12:04.082
A 30-gram of packet of China Lay's

02:12:04.082 --> 02:12:07.185
American classic-flavor chips

02:12:07.185 --> 02:12:10.889
contains 162 calories,

02:12:10.889 --> 02:12:13.292
1.7 grams of protein,

02:12:13.292 --> 02:12:16.094
10.5 grams of fat,

02:12:16.094 --> 02:12:20.198
of which 5.3 grams are saturated fats,

02:12:20.198 --> 02:12:22.668
15.1 grams of carbs,

02:12:22.668 --> 02:12:25.804
of which 0.4 grams are sugars,

02:12:25.804 --> 02:12:28.206
0.8 grams of fiber,

02:12:28.206 --> 02:12:31.643
and 170 milligrams of sodium.

02:12:31.643 --> 02:12:34.579
A 20-gram bag of classic
Lay's in the US contains

02:12:34.579 --> 02:12:36.782
160 calories, total fat 10 grams,

02:12:36.782 --> 02:12:39.584
of which saturated, 1.5 grams.

02:12:39.584 --> 02:12:43.555
Carbs, 15 grams, and 170
milligrams of sodium.

02:12:43.555 --> 02:12:46.191
We did find that the 160-calorie chips

02:12:46.191 --> 02:12:47.793
with the highest fat content

02:12:47.793 --> 02:12:50.228
are the cheddar and sour cream chips.

02:12:50.228 --> 02:12:51.163
Here's what's in a bag of those.

02:12:51.163 --> 02:12:53.899
160 calories, 10 grams of fat,

02:12:53.899 --> 02:12:56.335
of which 1.5 are saturated.

02:12:56.335 --> 02:13:00.072
15 grams of carbs, and
170 milligrams of sodium.

02:13:00.072 --> 02:13:02.307
Dun, dun, dun!

02:13:02.307 --> 02:13:05.243
We have a very shocking discovery.

02:13:05.243 --> 02:13:08.513
Apparently, Lay's "healthiest" chips

02:13:08.513 --> 02:13:11.183
are in fact their least healthy,

02:13:11.183 --> 02:13:13.852
in that they have more calories on average

02:13:13.852 --> 02:13:17.556
than any other Lay's
product here in China.

02:13:17.556 --> 02:13:19.491
And the worst offender

02:13:24.162 --> 02:13:26.164
is my hair-growth serum,

02:13:26.164 --> 02:13:30.469
the black sesame and chia seed yam crisps.

02:13:30.469 --> 02:13:32.871
Now, 100 grams of this will equal

02:13:32.871 --> 02:13:36.241
598.7 calories,

02:13:36.241 --> 02:13:38.777
or 168 calories

02:13:38.777 --> 02:13:41.613
for a 28-gram packet.

02:13:41.613 --> 02:13:44.249
Now, in a 30-gram portion,

02:13:44.249 --> 02:13:48.587
you'll have 179.6 calories,

02:13:48.587 --> 02:13:50.822
1.6 grams of protein,

02:13:50.822 --> 02:13:53.592
13.3 grams of fat,

02:13:53.592 --> 02:13:57.262
of which 6.6 are saturated fat,

02:13:57.262 --> 02:14:00.098
13.7 grams of carbs,

02:14:00.098 --> 02:14:04.002
and 212 milligrams of sodium.

02:14:04.002 --> 02:14:06.638
Which means that the healthy yam chips

02:14:06.638 --> 02:14:09.408
are on average 11% more calorific

02:14:09.408 --> 02:14:11.443
than any other Lay's chips,

02:14:11.443 --> 02:14:14.379
containing less protein and carbs

02:14:14.379 --> 02:14:17.182
and more sodium and fat.

02:14:17.182 --> 02:14:21.486
You know, I always thought
healthy just meant not tasty,

02:14:21.486 --> 02:14:25.290
but in Lay's case, apparently,
it also means less healthy.

02:14:25.290 --> 02:14:27.092
What a plot twist.

02:14:27.125 --> 02:14:28.794
From calorie count to portion sizes,

02:14:28.794 --> 02:14:30.695
we wanted to find out all the differences

02:14:30.695 --> 02:14:33.965
between Burger King in
the US and in China.

02:14:33.965 --> 02:14:35.767
This is "Food Wars."

02:14:36.635 --> 02:14:38.070
Hey, it's Joe.

02:14:38.070 --> 02:14:40.205
I'm busy working on some
cool new videos for you.

02:14:40.205 --> 02:14:41.606
I will not be able to host today,

02:14:41.606 --> 02:14:44.042
but I want to introduce
you to my good friend Nico.

02:14:44.042 --> 02:14:46.144
I trust Nico's going
to do a fantastic job.

02:14:46.144 --> 02:14:48.914
All the "Food Wars"-heads
watching, make her feel welcome.

02:14:48.914 --> 02:14:50.082
Take it away, Nico.

02:14:51.450 --> 02:14:54.853
Here in China, our Burger King
drinks come in three sizes:

02:14:54.853 --> 02:14:58.056
small, medium, and large.

02:14:58.056 --> 02:15:01.326
In the US, our Burger King
drinks come in four sizes:

02:15:01.326 --> 02:15:03.995
value, which we weren't able to get,

02:15:03.995 --> 02:15:06.364
small, medium, and large.

02:15:06.364 --> 02:15:10.202
Let's see how much our largest
drink actually contains.

02:15:10.202 --> 02:15:11.870
I'm kind of OK with it.

02:15:12.838 --> 02:15:14.840
They're lying to me.

02:15:14.840 --> 02:15:17.809
Our Burger King fries
also come in three sizes:

02:15:17.809 --> 02:15:20.278
small, medium, and large.

02:15:20.278 --> 02:15:22.114
Our fries come in four sizes:

02:15:22.114 --> 02:15:24.916
value, small, medium, and large.

02:15:24.916 --> 02:15:28.120
Let's weigh our largest fries. 120.

02:15:28.120 --> 02:15:32.657
140 grams. Liars again.

02:15:32.657 --> 02:15:35.927
This is the second lie I've
been told in like five minutes.

02:15:35.927 --> 02:15:38.063
I think Joe and Harry
have beef with Burger King

02:15:38.063 --> 02:15:40.699
ever since #frygate2020.

02:15:40.699 --> 02:15:43.201
They discovered the small and medium sizes

02:15:43.201 --> 02:15:46.338
were the same size, allegedly.

02:15:46.338 --> 02:15:48.373
Allegedly. I do not want to get sued.

02:15:48.373 --> 02:15:51.643
But let's see if both of them
actually do weigh the same.

02:15:51.643 --> 02:15:54.980
I don't think that I have to
count every individual fry,

02:15:54.980 --> 02:15:58.016
because that is a very big difference.

02:15:58.016 --> 02:16:01.653
I think there's clearly
some discrepancies going on.

02:16:01.653 --> 02:16:05.190
Just for fun, let's
weigh these value fries.

02:16:05.190 --> 02:16:06.691
These are 98.

02:16:06.691 --> 02:16:07.759
What's happening?

02:16:07.759 --> 02:16:09.728
What's going on at Burger King?

02:16:09.728 --> 02:16:12.230
So I guess you can get away
with just ordering a value size

02:16:12.230 --> 02:16:15.100
for, like, way less money
if this is what's going on.

02:16:15.100 --> 02:16:17.869
Our chicken fries come in one size only

02:16:17.869 --> 02:16:20.705
and should contain six fries.

02:16:20.705 --> 02:16:21.540
Ta-da.

02:16:22.474 --> 02:16:25.544
No way to escape from giving
us the full amount here, BK.

02:16:25.544 --> 02:16:26.945
There's only six of them.

02:16:26.945 --> 02:16:30.315
Ours is also one size: nine chicken fries.

02:16:30.315 --> 02:16:33.919
One, two, three, four, five,
six, seven, eight, nine.

02:16:33.919 --> 02:16:34.753
This is the first time

02:16:34.753 --> 02:16:37.155
that Burger King hasn't
lied straight to my face.

02:16:39.024 --> 02:16:41.560
Let's begin with our beef burgers.

02:16:41.560 --> 02:16:44.062
We can start with the King's Collection,

02:16:44.062 --> 02:16:47.532
which I guess are BK's premium burgers.

02:16:47.532 --> 02:16:50.235
Whereas the Whoppers
are known as Emperors,

02:16:50.235 --> 02:16:52.304
but they're cheaper than the kings.

02:16:52.304 --> 02:16:54.306
I can just hear the nationalists

02:16:54.306 --> 02:16:56.541
starting to get angry already.

02:16:56.541 --> 02:16:58.243
How could a king be more powerful

02:16:58.243 --> 02:17:00.178
and more expensive than an emperor?

02:17:00.178 --> 02:17:01.179
What gives?

02:17:01.179 --> 02:17:03.281
You obviously haven't
localized properly, BK.

02:17:03.281 --> 02:17:04.783
You need to know your audience.

02:17:04.783 --> 02:17:08.119
Beginning with the pastrami Angus.

02:17:08.119 --> 02:17:10.188
It's not something that you see very often

02:17:10.188 --> 02:17:11.957
here in China to begin with.

02:17:11.957 --> 02:17:13.091
So in in Chinese,

02:17:13.091 --> 02:17:15.627
the name is called the
"bigmouth Angus burger,"

02:17:15.627 --> 02:17:16.928
because the burger itself is

02:17:16.928 --> 02:17:18.797
meant to be quite a tall burger.

02:17:18.797 --> 02:17:21.900
But this is a very beautiful
burger, and I must say,

02:17:21.900 --> 02:17:26.805
I am very impressed that it
has not come to us sloppy

02:17:26.805 --> 02:17:29.140
and completely crushed into paste,

02:17:29.140 --> 02:17:31.476
which was the case that we found

02:17:31.476 --> 02:17:33.211
with other fast-food chains.

02:17:33.211 --> 02:17:34.846
I'm not going to name
names. [cough] [bleep]

02:17:37.315 --> 02:17:38.416
Very dense.

02:17:38.416 --> 02:17:40.552
I did have to open my mouth pretty wide.

02:17:40.552 --> 02:17:42.654
And I can't quite taste the pastrami,

02:17:42.654 --> 02:17:44.055
but I like that it's there.

02:17:44.055 --> 02:17:46.124
Here we've got the classic Angus.

02:17:46.124 --> 02:17:48.326
You can also get the spicy version,

02:17:48.326 --> 02:17:50.095
which is what I've opted for.

02:17:50.095 --> 02:17:53.632
Ooh, ooh.

02:17:53.632 --> 02:17:55.267
Oh, that's a spicy fella.

02:17:55.267 --> 02:17:57.202
This is actually pretty interesting.

02:17:57.202 --> 02:18:00.138
It's not the Sichuan spicy kind of heat

02:18:00.138 --> 02:18:01.473
that I've gotten used to here

02:18:01.473 --> 02:18:03.742
eating other localized burgers in China,

02:18:03.742 --> 02:18:06.544
but this is more sort of a
straight-up, in-your-face heat.

02:18:06.544 --> 02:18:09.748
Lot of black pepper, and
the caramelized onions,

02:18:09.748 --> 02:18:12.050
oh, they pair very well in this burger.

02:18:12.050 --> 02:18:17.055
Introducing the heavy cheese beef King.

02:18:17.255 --> 02:18:21.359
So heavy, actually, it even
crushed the box that it came in.

02:18:21.359 --> 02:18:26.364
Well, hello. The spicy bamboo
shoots beef chicken Whopper.

02:18:27.132 --> 02:18:29.567
That is such a long name.

02:18:29.567 --> 02:18:31.636
It came in this box.

02:18:31.636 --> 02:18:35.073
These are characters from
a massive game in China

02:18:35.073 --> 02:18:37.976
called the Honor of Kings. It's a MOBA.

02:18:37.976 --> 02:18:40.745
The company that makes
this bought Riot Games,

02:18:40.745 --> 02:18:42.314
which made "League of Legends."

02:18:42.314 --> 02:18:44.215
The fact that it has this collab,

02:18:44.215 --> 02:18:45.617
I mean, that means something.

02:18:47.452 --> 02:18:49.921
I just want to say it tastes very Chinese

02:18:49.921 --> 02:18:50.755
in the best possible way.

02:18:50.755 --> 02:18:53.825
It feels like I'm in
Southwest China right now,

02:18:53.825 --> 02:18:57.862
playing a game of Honor
of Kings and losing badly.

02:18:57.862 --> 02:18:58.697
Because otherwise,

02:18:58.697 --> 02:19:01.599
how would I have time to eat
burgers if I'm not respawning?

02:19:01.599 --> 02:19:04.903
Final member of the King Collection is

02:19:04.903 --> 02:19:08.807
the Italian spinach bacon Angus.

02:19:08.807 --> 02:19:11.910
Oh, one thing that irks
me a little bit about

02:19:11.910 --> 02:19:14.512
bacon in burgers in China is that

02:19:14.512 --> 02:19:16.314
they're this kind of bacon. They're wet.

02:19:16.314 --> 02:19:19.017
And what's the point of eating
bacon if it's not crispy?

02:19:21.319 --> 02:19:22.487
Oh, my God.

02:19:22.487 --> 02:19:25.523
BK burgers are so incredibly dense.

02:19:25.523 --> 02:19:27.792
They're like the burger
versions of diamonds.

02:19:27.792 --> 02:19:29.527
Moving on to our classic burgers.

02:19:29.527 --> 02:19:30.795
This is the

02:19:30.795 --> 02:19:33.064
king oyster mushroom

02:19:33.064 --> 02:19:36.134
beef Whopper Thai basil flavor.

02:19:36.134 --> 02:19:39.571
My God, not only are
their burgers mouthfuls,

02:19:39.571 --> 02:19:40.905
but so are the names.

02:19:40.905 --> 02:19:43.508
You can actually see the oyster mushrooms.

02:19:43.508 --> 02:19:44.976
Look, right here.

02:19:44.976 --> 02:19:48.513
Let's give this mouthful a mouthful.

02:19:48.513 --> 02:19:49.714
It feels like I'm in the gym

02:19:49.714 --> 02:19:52.817
about to do some really heavy lifting.

02:19:52.817 --> 02:19:54.018
[exhales]

02:19:54.018 --> 02:19:55.987
And then [grunts].

02:19:58.790 --> 02:20:02.427
Another classic, the
grilled pineapple Whopper.

02:20:02.427 --> 02:20:04.963
One gigantic pineapple ring.

02:20:06.598 --> 02:20:09.000
If I had two more hands so, oh.

02:20:09.000 --> 02:20:12.137
The pork cubes and beef burger.

02:20:12.137 --> 02:20:13.805
Who names these things?

02:20:13.805 --> 02:20:17.142
The pork cubes that it refers to is

02:20:17.142 --> 02:20:18.977
pork neck.

02:20:18.977 --> 02:20:20.512
It's a meat lover's heaven, isn't it?

02:20:20.512 --> 02:20:21.479
I can do this!

02:20:22.847 --> 02:20:24.682
Feeling like my jaw's about to break.

02:20:27.318 --> 02:20:28.386
Oh, yes.

02:20:29.521 --> 02:20:30.855
Wow.

02:20:32.223 --> 02:20:33.658
That is amazing.

02:20:33.658 --> 02:20:37.896
This pork neck is just
absolutely delicious.

02:20:37.896 --> 02:20:40.532
Moving on to our value section,

02:20:40.532 --> 02:20:43.701
we've got the spicy Whopper Jr.

02:20:43.701 --> 02:20:46.037
Oh, look at this little guy.

02:20:46.037 --> 02:20:50.241
You can also get the
pineapple bacon Whopper Jr.

02:20:50.241 --> 02:20:51.776
also in this size.

02:20:51.776 --> 02:20:53.711
This is our bacon corner.

02:20:53.711 --> 02:20:57.282
So we have the bacon King, and
there is a bacon cheeseburger

02:20:57.282 --> 02:20:59.083
and the double bacon cheeseburger.

02:20:59.083 --> 02:21:02.120
I really want to taste the bacon King.

02:21:02.120 --> 02:21:04.656
That's, like, a big burger
for fast food, right?

02:21:04.656 --> 02:21:05.824
That is heavy, too.

02:21:05.824 --> 02:21:06.724
My face is bigger,

02:21:06.724 --> 02:21:09.527
but it doesn't smell as
good as this burger does.

02:21:10.895 --> 02:21:13.298
Kind of tastes like a
burger right off the grill.

02:21:13.298 --> 02:21:16.201
This is, like, insane how big they are.

02:21:16.201 --> 02:21:17.769
Now let's move on to the Whoppers.

02:21:17.769 --> 02:21:20.705
I think these are definitely
Burger King's claim to fame.

02:21:20.705 --> 02:21:22.440
It's what they're most known for.

02:21:22.440 --> 02:21:25.844
This is the Texas Double Whopper.

02:21:25.844 --> 02:21:30.014
This kind of looks like the
Mondo Burger from "Good Burger."

02:21:32.150 --> 02:21:33.284
That is not ASMR.

02:21:33.284 --> 02:21:35.153
What's the opposite of ASMR?

02:21:35.153 --> 02:21:37.856
And the last Whopper we have
is the Impossible Whopper,

02:21:37.856 --> 02:21:40.925
which I actually think
tastes pretty delicious.

02:21:40.925 --> 02:21:42.827
Like, this looks like a hamburger

02:21:42.827 --> 02:21:45.330
from a play food set I had as a child.

02:21:45.330 --> 02:21:47.932
It just doesn't look very real.

02:21:47.932 --> 02:21:49.667
This looks like a monster.

02:21:49.667 --> 02:21:52.036
I do want to take a bite of
the Texas double Whopper,

02:21:52.036 --> 02:21:54.839
just because it's got
a lot of stuff in it.

02:21:56.207 --> 02:21:57.208
That is so good.

02:21:57.208 --> 02:21:58.877
Oh my God, it's really spicy.

02:21:58.877 --> 02:22:03.715
And here we have our single
Rodeo Clown King burger.

02:22:03.715 --> 02:22:04.749
[camera crew laughs]

02:22:04.749 --> 02:22:07.452
Single Rodeo Burger King pounder.

02:22:07.452 --> 02:22:10.755
All of them share the exact
same words. It's crazy.

02:22:10.755 --> 02:22:12.891
And here we have the
single quarter-pound King

02:22:12.891 --> 02:22:16.895
and the Rodeo burger, which I
think has onion rings in it.

02:22:16.895 --> 02:22:18.062
I was wrong.

02:22:18.062 --> 02:22:21.032
OK, pretend I said the opposite.

02:22:21.032 --> 02:22:23.768
So this is the Rodeo burger,
and it's got onion rings

02:22:23.768 --> 02:22:27.038
and what looks like sticky barbecue sauce.

02:22:27.038 --> 02:22:29.274
It's just a little congealed in there.

02:22:30.708 --> 02:22:32.343
I think it could be good.

02:22:32.343 --> 02:22:33.845
It's just not very good.

02:22:33.845 --> 02:22:37.415
Now let's move on to the
chicken sandwiches, or burgers,

02:22:37.415 --> 02:22:38.516
whichever you prefer.

02:22:38.516 --> 02:22:41.252
As for chicken, you can
get the chicken Whopper,

02:22:41.252 --> 02:22:44.355
coming in classic or spicy flavors.

02:22:44.355 --> 02:22:48.493
You can get the grilled pineapple
chicken Whopper as well.

02:22:48.493 --> 02:22:50.795
Next we've got the chicken Big King.

02:22:50.795 --> 02:22:54.566
Now the Big King is a
collection, and we have beef,

02:22:54.566 --> 02:22:56.034
which is not exclusive here in China,

02:22:56.034 --> 02:22:58.169
but chicken and fish are.

02:22:58.169 --> 02:23:02.307
And it's basically kind
of like a Big Mac in that

02:23:02.307 --> 02:23:05.877
there are two patties
and a bun in the middle.

02:23:07.679 --> 02:23:08.947
That's a lot of bread.

02:23:08.947 --> 02:23:13.952
This here is the fruitwood
grilled chicken burger.

02:23:13.952 --> 02:23:15.420
Spicy chicken burger.

02:23:15.420 --> 02:23:18.389
The chicken is threatening to escape.

02:23:19.791 --> 02:23:21.559
Oh, yeah, the more you chew it, mm.

02:23:21.559 --> 02:23:24.996
The more you chew it, the
more flavorful it becomes.

02:23:24.996 --> 02:23:25.997
And now I can,

02:23:25.997 --> 02:23:28.166
it's almost like a
thermometer in my mouth.

02:23:28.166 --> 02:23:29.634
I can,

02:23:29.634 --> 02:23:32.870
I can feel the spiciness rising up.

02:23:32.870 --> 02:23:36.207
I swallowed just now,
and my saliva is spicy.

02:23:36.207 --> 02:23:38.643
We have the crispy chicken sandwich.

02:23:38.643 --> 02:23:43.648
But what makes this a
sandwich and this a burger?

02:23:43.648 --> 02:23:44.849
I have no idea.

02:23:44.849 --> 02:23:48.753
There's also a double version of that,

02:23:48.753 --> 02:23:50.254
excuse my lettuce,

02:23:50.254 --> 02:23:54.258
that is called the double chicken burger.

02:23:54.258 --> 02:23:56.527
So if it's a single, it's
a crispy chicken sandwich,

02:23:56.527 --> 02:23:59.764
but if it's a double, then it
just becomes something else.

02:23:59.764 --> 02:24:04.369
Anyway, this also comes in
original or rattan pepper flavor.

02:24:04.369 --> 02:24:06.371
Here we have the chicken version

02:24:06.371 --> 02:24:09.674
of the Italian spinach bacon Whopper.

02:24:09.674 --> 02:24:10.842
A surprise for you all,

02:24:13.378 --> 02:24:14.612
this is new on the menu.

02:24:14.612 --> 02:24:16.848
Da-da-da.

02:24:16.848 --> 02:24:21.719
The black cheese and
crispy chicken sandwich.

02:24:21.719 --> 02:24:23.921
So this thing is not nori.

02:24:23.921 --> 02:24:26.824
This is actually a slice of cheddar cheese

02:24:26.824 --> 02:24:30.094
that's been dyed black with squid ink,

02:24:30.094 --> 02:24:32.363
because just why not?

02:24:32.363 --> 02:24:35.299
So if you thought this
was weird, check this out.

02:24:36.734 --> 02:24:41.739
This is the black cheese
and crispy chicken burger.

02:24:42.206 --> 02:24:46.477
Most importantly, instead of the bun,

02:24:46.477 --> 02:24:51.049
they've replaced it with
two pieces of black cheese.

02:24:51.049 --> 02:24:52.083
Mind blown.

02:24:53.851 --> 02:24:56.754
I think this is basically
just an excuse for you

02:24:56.754 --> 02:24:59.090
to not feel guilty about eating

02:24:59.090 --> 02:25:02.326
a piece of spicy chicken by
itself without the bread.

02:25:02.326 --> 02:25:07.131
It's basically just there as, like, tissue

02:25:07.131 --> 02:25:08.800
to help you eat this thing.

02:25:08.800 --> 02:25:10.768
We have two chicken exclusives,

02:25:10.768 --> 02:25:13.705
the original chicken
sandwich and the Chicken Jr.

02:25:13.705 --> 02:25:17.675
This shape is actually very
unique and pretty iconic.

02:25:17.675 --> 02:25:20.344
In a world of circular chicken sandwiches,

02:25:20.344 --> 02:25:21.879
this stands out to me.

02:25:21.879 --> 02:25:24.949
Usually the chicken sandwiches
I see look like this.

02:25:24.949 --> 02:25:26.651
Just you know, nothing special.

02:25:26.651 --> 02:25:28.820
But this is special.

02:25:28.820 --> 02:25:31.522
BK also offers fish exclusives.

02:25:31.522 --> 02:25:34.125
Here we've got the Fish'N Crisp,

02:25:34.125 --> 02:25:36.861
which I believe uses a cod fillet.

02:25:36.861 --> 02:25:41.866
And of course, the fish
version of the Big King.

02:25:42.133 --> 02:25:44.736
And of course, we also have a pork section

02:25:44.736 --> 02:25:46.471
comprising of two burgers,

02:25:46.471 --> 02:25:48.406
the pork neck and beef burger,

02:25:48.406 --> 02:25:52.143
which I took a nice big
chunk out of before.

02:25:52.143 --> 02:25:55.113
And the chicken version
of this pork burger.

02:25:55.113 --> 02:25:59.417
And here is our fish option, the Big Fish.

02:25:59.417 --> 02:26:03.054
This is the smoothest bun I've ever seen.

02:26:03.054 --> 02:26:05.123
Look how shiny and beautiful that is.

02:26:06.624 --> 02:26:09.994
It's not offensive,
not particularly great.

02:26:09.994 --> 02:26:14.899
These are our exclusive snacks
here in Burger King China.

02:26:14.899 --> 02:26:15.967
I feel like they're encroaching

02:26:15.967 --> 02:26:17.435
on KFC territory a little bit,

02:26:17.435 --> 02:26:20.071
because all of this is chicken.

02:26:20.071 --> 02:26:23.141
We've got the mala chicken drumstick.

02:26:23.141 --> 02:26:26.744
So "mala" literally just
means numb and spicy,

02:26:26.744 --> 02:26:29.881
and it's referring to the
Sichuanese style of cooking

02:26:29.881 --> 02:26:31.015
with the peppercorn,

02:26:31.015 --> 02:26:33.818
which gives you the
numbness and the chili heat.

02:26:34.685 --> 02:26:36.854
Oh, wow.

02:26:36.854 --> 02:26:41.859
I feel like this is probably
the strongest mala flavor

02:26:43.861 --> 02:26:46.130
that I've had thus far on Food Wars.

02:26:46.130 --> 02:26:48.633
It's starting to turn my tongue numb.

02:26:48.633 --> 02:26:50.434
I'm quite pleasantly surprised.

02:26:50.434 --> 02:26:54.005
Here we've got the petite
version, the mala chicken wings.

02:26:54.005 --> 02:26:58.042
This here, the King hot
and spicy chicken wings.

02:26:58.876 --> 02:27:02.346
Oh, man, I much prefer it
over the mala to be honest.

02:27:02.346 --> 02:27:04.515
This is a lot more balanced,

02:27:04.515 --> 02:27:06.484
it's more flavorful, it's meatier.

02:27:06.484 --> 02:27:11.189
So these are called the
spicy flavor chicken slices.

02:27:11.189 --> 02:27:14.525
Apparently it's 4-millimeter thin

02:27:14.525 --> 02:27:16.227
slices of chicken breast.

02:27:16.227 --> 02:27:18.963
It just kind of looks like mini
chicken nuggets, doesn't it?

02:27:18.963 --> 02:27:21.265
This is the chicken box,

02:27:21.265 --> 02:27:26.170
which contains a medley of
what we sampled earlier.

02:27:26.170 --> 02:27:29.140
So Burger King also has other versions of

02:27:29.140 --> 02:27:30.975
the bucket, the box, whatever
you'd like to call it.

02:27:30.975 --> 02:27:33.878
They've got the King chicken
bucket, the King bucket,

02:27:33.878 --> 02:27:35.613
and the King bucket plus.

02:27:35.613 --> 02:27:38.249
They're basically the BK version of

02:27:38.249 --> 02:27:40.318
the party bucket or family bucket.

02:27:40.318 --> 02:27:43.721
For those of you who
could not get enough of

02:27:43.721 --> 02:27:45.823
the black cheese,

02:27:45.823 --> 02:27:48.826
you can also get it as a standalone piece.

02:27:48.826 --> 02:27:51.662
Just one piece of good old cheddar cheese

02:27:51.662 --> 02:27:53.798
dyed black with squid ink.

02:27:53.798 --> 02:27:56.100
Oh, BK, you are so funny.

02:27:57.501 --> 02:28:00.404
You can always opt for the garden salad.

02:28:00.404 --> 02:28:02.006
And here in Chinese it actually says,

02:28:02.006 --> 02:28:07.011
"Mama is shouting at you,
telling you to eat more veggies."

02:28:07.745 --> 02:28:10.414
And these are our exclusive side options.

02:28:10.414 --> 02:28:12.416
We have onion rings.

02:28:13.351 --> 02:28:14.752
Don't mind if I do.

02:28:16.354 --> 02:28:17.521
They're soggy.

02:28:18.723 --> 02:28:21.125
And we also have mozzarella sticks,

02:28:21.125 --> 02:28:24.528
which I feel like at this
point are fully congealed

02:28:24.528 --> 02:28:26.998
back into their, like, frozen state.

02:28:29.500 --> 02:28:31.669
These were supposed to
come with a marinara sauce.

02:28:31.669 --> 02:28:32.870
I don't think I got one.

02:28:32.870 --> 02:28:35.139
We also have Mott's applesauce as a side,

02:28:35.139 --> 02:28:37.308
but they unfortunately ran out.

02:28:37.308 --> 02:28:42.046
And here are our exclusive sauces.

02:28:43.447 --> 02:28:48.319
We have buffalo, ranch,
honey mustard, and zesty.

02:28:48.319 --> 02:28:50.788
I know what pretty much all
of these sauces taste like,

02:28:50.788 --> 02:28:52.857
except for zesty.

02:28:52.857 --> 02:28:55.893
I'm very confused as
to what this could be.

02:28:55.893 --> 02:28:57.495
Just watch this one for you guys,

02:28:57.495 --> 02:29:02.066
just so you can see what it
looks like on my skin tone.

02:29:03.200 --> 02:29:06.337
This is the most disturbing,
stupid thing I've ever done.

02:29:09.774 --> 02:29:11.309
Horseradish-y.

02:29:11.309 --> 02:29:13.744
I feel like zesty gives
me like, ooh, zesty.

02:29:13.744 --> 02:29:15.980
This is like, ugh, zesty.

02:29:15.980 --> 02:29:17.014
It's nasty.

02:29:17.014 --> 02:29:19.383
Time for dessert.

02:29:19.383 --> 02:29:22.019
We can start with the
Ovaltine King Fusion.

02:29:22.019 --> 02:29:24.455
This comes in original strawberry

02:29:24.455 --> 02:29:28.025
and brown sugar bubble flavor.

02:29:29.060 --> 02:29:33.631
The Ovaltine was the little
sort of brown flakes on top.

02:29:33.631 --> 02:29:35.566
That's what tastes like milk chocolate.

02:29:35.566 --> 02:29:38.402
Not bad. It's not as sweet
as I thought it would be.

02:29:38.402 --> 02:29:41.439
Ovaltine King Fusion,
brown sugar bubble edition.

02:29:41.439 --> 02:29:43.941
Very elusive these days.

02:29:43.941 --> 02:29:44.875
Where are they?

02:29:44.875 --> 02:29:45.710
Ah, here we go.

02:29:47.078 --> 02:29:49.113
Mm, delicious.

02:29:49.113 --> 02:29:50.281
Once upon a time,

02:29:50.281 --> 02:29:55.052
this was the Hokkaido flavor
ice cream waffle cone.

02:29:56.520 --> 02:29:57.922
It tastes like melted ice cream.

02:29:57.922 --> 02:29:58.889
I can't tell.

02:29:59.991 --> 02:30:03.094
If you say it's Hokkaido,
I'm none the wiser.

02:30:03.094 --> 02:30:06.831
This is the crispy
chocolate and nuts sundae.

02:30:06.831 --> 02:30:09.000
Häagen-Dazs, Ben and Jerry,

02:30:09.000 --> 02:30:10.901
get out the way, BK's in town.

02:30:10.901 --> 02:30:12.903
Look at that. That looks luxe.

02:30:12.903 --> 02:30:15.406
Look at how much chocolate is in here.

02:30:15.406 --> 02:30:18.242
This is basically half a bar
of chocolate in ice cream.

02:30:18.242 --> 02:30:20.344
There's nothing that
could be better than this.

02:30:20.344 --> 02:30:22.546
I think it's peanut.
I'm not sure. Who cares?

02:30:22.546 --> 02:30:23.514
Oh, it's delicious.

02:30:24.615 --> 02:30:27.618
And the strawberry pulp sundae.

02:30:27.618 --> 02:30:30.187
Actual strawberry in the sundae.

02:30:30.187 --> 02:30:31.455
Color me impressed.

02:30:31.455 --> 02:30:34.959
Now this pie comes in
two different flavors:

02:30:34.959 --> 02:30:38.963
dark chocolate or mango and coconut.

02:30:38.963 --> 02:30:40.798
Let me check which one this is.

02:30:40.798 --> 02:30:42.066
I think it's a telltale sign.

02:30:42.066 --> 02:30:43.968
I think it's probably the chocolate.

02:30:43.968 --> 02:30:46.437
Deep-fried chocolate, what could go wrong?

02:30:46.437 --> 02:30:50.107
These are called crispy thick milk bars.

02:30:51.842 --> 02:30:55.679
It's creamy, but it doesn't
really taste like much.

02:30:55.679 --> 02:30:58.916
This is the soft mochi ice cream.

02:30:58.916 --> 02:31:00.351
And it comes in two flavors,

02:31:00.351 --> 02:31:03.988
strawberry yogurt and salted egg.

02:31:08.826 --> 02:31:10.294
Wow.

02:31:10.294 --> 02:31:12.063
It's kind of like a custard.

02:31:13.564 --> 02:31:17.034
Oh, this kind of tastes like

02:31:17.034 --> 02:31:20.471
what would happen if you took
the heart out of a moon cake

02:31:20.471 --> 02:31:23.808
and liquefied it and just drank it.

02:31:23.808 --> 02:31:24.708
Oh, my God,

02:31:24.708 --> 02:31:29.013
I think I'm seeing stars from
my blood sugar spiking. Oh.

02:31:29.013 --> 02:31:31.916
Let's talk about desserts.
At Burger King in the US,

02:31:31.916 --> 02:31:33.818
you can get a soft-serve cup,

02:31:33.818 --> 02:31:38.189
a soft-serve cone, or
the Hershey's sundae pie.

02:31:38.189 --> 02:31:40.825
This was one of my favorite
things ever as a kid.

02:31:40.825 --> 02:31:43.360
I would always get it every
time we went to Burger King.

02:31:43.360 --> 02:31:44.195
Look at this.

02:31:44.195 --> 02:31:48.132
It literally says yum on every
side, because it's that good.

02:31:48.132 --> 02:31:50.835
They look exactly the
same as when I was little.

02:31:52.536 --> 02:31:55.239
That is so delicious.

02:31:55.239 --> 02:31:57.675
These are the exclusive drinks

02:31:57.675 --> 02:32:00.010
on the Burger King China menu.

02:32:00.010 --> 02:32:00.845
Looks weird, doesn't it?

02:32:00.845 --> 02:32:02.279
It just looks like 7Up.

02:32:02.279 --> 02:32:07.284
But this is actually coconut-flavored
lemon sparkling drink.

02:32:08.219 --> 02:32:10.654
Peach-flavored oolong tea.

02:32:10.654 --> 02:32:14.258
This is the brown sugar boba milk tea.

02:32:14.258 --> 02:32:16.026
You can get this hot or cold.

02:32:16.026 --> 02:32:19.830
And also, if you take away the boba balls,

02:32:19.830 --> 02:32:23.033
it'll just basically become
the Hong Kong-style milk tea,

02:32:23.033 --> 02:32:26.604
which you can also get hot or cold.

02:32:26.604 --> 02:32:30.774
The crispy chocolate snow-top milk tea.

02:32:30.774 --> 02:32:33.978
You can also get Ceylon tea,
which is just black tea,

02:32:33.978 --> 02:32:37.581
or hot or cold soy milk, which this is.

02:32:37.581 --> 02:32:39.049
You can get juice too,

02:32:39.049 --> 02:32:42.753
grapefruit juice and mixed-berries juice.

02:32:42.753 --> 02:32:45.389
Next we have the King coffee collection.

02:32:45.389 --> 02:32:48.125
And this is just honestly
the cutest cup ever.

02:32:48.125 --> 02:32:51.228
You can get your latte or your flat white,

02:32:51.228 --> 02:32:53.697
your hazelnut latte, or cappuccino

02:32:53.697 --> 02:32:57.635
in this very, very cute squat cup.

02:32:57.635 --> 02:33:00.070
Or if you don't like being cute,

02:33:00.070 --> 02:33:04.041
you can just opt for a
regular-sized Americano.

02:33:04.041 --> 02:33:06.410
Drink exclusives in the US include

02:33:06.410 --> 02:33:09.713
Coke zero, Sprite zero, Barq's root beer,

02:33:09.713 --> 02:33:14.318
Dr Pepper, Fanta orange,
Mellow Yello, Powerade zero,

02:33:14.318 --> 02:33:17.788
High-C fruit punch, and
High-C pink lemonade.

02:33:17.788 --> 02:33:19.056
It's a fast food restaurant,

02:33:19.056 --> 02:33:20.524
so of course they also offer

02:33:20.524 --> 02:33:22.593
milkshakes and frozen beverages.

02:33:22.593 --> 02:33:25.563
We have a vanilla milkshake,
a chocolate milkshake,

02:33:25.563 --> 02:33:27.198
an Oreo milkshake,

02:33:27.198 --> 02:33:29.300
a chocolate Oreo milkshake.

02:33:29.300 --> 02:33:31.769
This is a frozen Fanta wild cherry.

02:33:31.769 --> 02:33:34.104
And this is supposed to be a frozen Coke,

02:33:34.104 --> 02:33:36.640
but it's another frozen Fanta wild cherry.

02:33:36.640 --> 02:33:38.309
We've been putting the
people at Burger King

02:33:38.309 --> 02:33:41.245
through a lot today, so
some mistakes were made.

02:33:41.245 --> 02:33:43.881
They also supposedly offer
a strawberry milkshake,

02:33:43.881 --> 02:33:47.051
but that wasn't available
at our Burger King.

02:33:47.051 --> 02:33:49.787
[bleep] has a better vanilla milkshake.

02:33:49.787 --> 02:33:52.723
All right, let's try this
frozen Fanta wild cherry.

02:33:52.723 --> 02:33:55.993
Is this, this is basically
just a slushy, right?

02:33:55.993 --> 02:33:57.294
That's very good.

02:33:57.294 --> 02:34:02.233
These are Burger King China's
exclusive breakfast menus.

02:34:02.233 --> 02:34:04.835
OK, so just like McDonald's and KFC,

02:34:04.835 --> 02:34:06.036
Burger King also does

02:34:06.036 --> 02:34:08.806
a pretty decent breakfast
menu here in China.

02:34:08.806 --> 02:34:12.543
Not quite as extensive as KFC,

02:34:12.543 --> 02:34:15.746
and nowhere near as
exhaustive as McDonald's,

02:34:15.746 --> 02:34:19.483
but what Burger King has over both of them

02:34:19.483 --> 02:34:21.151
is the Croissan'wich.

02:34:21.151 --> 02:34:23.354
I love croissant sandwiches.

02:34:23.354 --> 02:34:26.156
Although it's kind of weird how in China,

02:34:26.156 --> 02:34:28.659
they're not called by their actual names,

02:34:28.659 --> 02:34:30.427
but they're called croissants.

02:34:30.427 --> 02:34:34.031
So this is the standard Croissan'wich,

02:34:34.031 --> 02:34:35.733
or as we call it here in China,

02:34:35.733 --> 02:34:38.302
the pork, egg, and cheese croissant.

02:34:38.302 --> 02:34:43.207
Next, we have the pastrami
and scrambled egg croissant.

02:34:43.207 --> 02:34:45.276
In Chinese, we would call it yangqi,

02:34:45.276 --> 02:34:48.946
which kind of means like
Western style of BK.

02:34:48.946 --> 02:34:51.215
I mean, obviously it's Western style,

02:34:51.215 --> 02:34:54.118
but the fact that you have
pastrami and scrambled egg,

02:34:54.118 --> 02:34:56.720
this combination just
seems very, very foreign

02:34:56.720 --> 02:34:58.289
to Chinese culture.

02:34:58.289 --> 02:35:00.958
And I think in a cool way, this is great,

02:35:00.958 --> 02:35:02.760
just staying true to BK's roots.

02:35:03.994 --> 02:35:06.297
Mm, I love pastrami.

02:35:06.297 --> 02:35:07.131
What do we got here?

02:35:07.131 --> 02:35:09.600
The beef, egg, cheese croissant.

02:35:09.600 --> 02:35:10.934
And last but not least

02:35:10.934 --> 02:35:14.204
in our croissant series, butter croissant,

02:35:14.204 --> 02:35:15.673
which is just ...

02:35:18.075 --> 02:35:21.011
All right, BK, you made
this a seasonal menu item.

02:35:21.011 --> 02:35:23.013
I don't understand what
it has to do with seasons.

02:35:23.013 --> 02:35:25.849
It's literally just two pieces
of your croissant bread.

02:35:25.849 --> 02:35:29.720
This is the double egg and beef burger.

02:35:29.720 --> 02:35:34.058
Two eggs with two beef patties

02:35:34.058 --> 02:35:36.694
sandwiched in between.
No bread whatsoever.

02:35:36.694 --> 02:35:39.263
There is no way you can safely
get away with eating this

02:35:39.263 --> 02:35:41.065
without making a mess of yourself.

02:35:41.065 --> 02:35:43.567
Now on to your more standard fare,

02:35:43.567 --> 02:35:47.037
the grilled beef cheese muffin.

02:35:47.037 --> 02:35:51.608
You can also get this grilled
beef, cheese, egg muffin.

02:35:51.608 --> 02:35:53.110
Oh, now we have something special.

02:35:53.110 --> 02:35:57.514
The tamagoyaki and fruitwood flavor

02:35:57.514 --> 02:36:00.017
grilled chicken muffin.

02:36:00.017 --> 02:36:01.285
Look at that.

02:36:01.285 --> 02:36:02.119
Mm.

02:36:02.119 --> 02:36:03.454
Oh, this is delicious.

02:36:03.454 --> 02:36:04.621
Well, I highly recommend it.

02:36:04.621 --> 02:36:06.790
And if you don't want beef in your muffin,

02:36:06.790 --> 02:36:10.160
you can get it as a cheese egg muffin.

02:36:10.160 --> 02:36:12.363
If you don't want egg nor beef,

02:36:12.363 --> 02:36:15.532
then you can get it as
a grilled pork muffin.

02:36:15.532 --> 02:36:18.702
BK also has an assortment
of breakfast wraps.

02:36:18.702 --> 02:36:21.939
The scrambled egg and cheese sausage wrap.

02:36:21.939 --> 02:36:25.909
Beijing-style roasted chicken wrap.

02:36:25.909 --> 02:36:30.914
No leek. Just the cucumbers
and the tianmian sauce.

02:36:31.115 --> 02:36:33.317
We're missing the last item

02:36:33.317 --> 02:36:36.053
on the holy trinity of
the Beijing-style wrap.

02:36:37.921 --> 02:36:41.158
You know, it's inoffensive.
That's all I can say.

02:36:41.158 --> 02:36:44.328
This is something special.

02:36:44.328 --> 02:36:47.030
Salted egg yolk chicken wrap.

02:36:47.030 --> 02:36:50.334
The salted egg yolk is actually smeared

02:36:50.334 --> 02:36:53.036
all over the chicken here.

02:36:53.036 --> 02:36:55.305
Wow, that's very ingenious of BK.

02:36:57.474 --> 02:37:00.377
There's no mistaking that salted egg, wow.

02:37:00.377 --> 02:37:02.179
Texture-wise, it's like,

02:37:02.179 --> 02:37:05.015
it's an egg yolk that has been matured.

02:37:05.015 --> 02:37:07.785
Kind of like a fine vintage
egg, if that makes sense.

02:37:07.785 --> 02:37:08.852
And last but not least,

02:37:08.852 --> 02:37:13.424
we've got the mixed vegetable
and roasted chicken wrap.

02:37:13.424 --> 02:37:15.959
And of course, we've got to have congee.

02:37:15.959 --> 02:37:19.830
Two types, this is century
egg and this is salted egg.

02:37:19.830 --> 02:37:21.231
Give the century egg a try.

02:37:22.299 --> 02:37:23.300
Whoo.

02:37:23.300 --> 02:37:24.802
Oh, yeah, that's pretty strong.

02:37:24.802 --> 02:37:28.972
There's a very, very fine
line between tasty and stinky,

02:37:28.972 --> 02:37:31.842
and century egg firmly
straddles that line.

02:37:31.842 --> 02:37:36.547
I've never had salted egg
yolk in a congee before.

02:37:38.015 --> 02:37:40.684
Congee's not my favorite breakfast item,

02:37:40.684 --> 02:37:42.820
but I think with this kind of flavoring,

02:37:42.820 --> 02:37:44.488
like, yeah, I can dig it.

02:37:44.488 --> 02:37:46.924
And of course, on every
single breakfast menu,

02:37:46.924 --> 02:37:51.295
there's going to be crispy
Chinese cruller, the youtiao.

02:37:51.295 --> 02:37:52.529
They all look the same

02:37:52.529 --> 02:37:54.565
no matter which fast food chain you go to.

02:37:54.565 --> 02:37:56.834
BK also has a sunny-side-up egg,

02:37:56.834 --> 02:38:00.471
although again, you can't
really tell where the sun is.

02:38:00.471 --> 02:38:02.940
Ho ho, this is pretty interesting.

02:38:02.940 --> 02:38:06.543
The bean paste glutinous rice balls.

02:38:06.543 --> 02:38:07.544
We call them matuan,

02:38:07.544 --> 02:38:11.014
which kind of means sesame pile, mound.

02:38:11.014 --> 02:38:12.516
These have a really interesting history.

02:38:12.516 --> 02:38:14.852
They originated in the Tang dynasty

02:38:14.852 --> 02:38:16.386
over 1,000 years ago

02:38:16.386 --> 02:38:19.990
and were served up in
the imperial kitchen.

02:38:19.990 --> 02:38:21.425
And actually, you'll find that

02:38:21.425 --> 02:38:23.760
a lot of traditional Chinese desserts,

02:38:23.760 --> 02:38:25.295
especially here in Beijing,

02:38:25.295 --> 02:38:27.231
were originally served to the emperor.

02:38:27.231 --> 02:38:30.033
The sort of stuff that we eat now

02:38:30.033 --> 02:38:34.404
would have been the crème de
la crème back in the old days,

02:38:34.404 --> 02:38:37.441
centuries ago, when emperors ruled China.

02:38:37.441 --> 02:38:39.243
History in a mouthful.

02:38:41.044 --> 02:38:42.312
I'd say it's OK.

02:38:42.312 --> 02:38:45.682
It's probably not the tastiest
sesame mound I've ever had,

02:38:45.682 --> 02:38:46.950
but, you know,

02:38:46.950 --> 02:38:48.585
this isn't made for emperors,

02:38:48.585 --> 02:38:50.187
because otherwise it'll
be [clicks tongue].

02:38:50.187 --> 02:38:51.154
Off with your head.

02:38:51.154 --> 02:38:52.856
Egg bacon pie.

02:38:55.025 --> 02:38:56.393
Oh, that's pretty tasty.

02:38:56.393 --> 02:38:58.228
The nostalgia's coming back in.

02:38:58.228 --> 02:39:00.430
I just remember growing up in the UK

02:39:00.430 --> 02:39:01.665
and then going down to Greggs

02:39:01.665 --> 02:39:03.967
and getting a nice pasty
in the morning, oh.

02:39:03.967 --> 02:39:06.270
I've actually never had
Burger King breakfast.

02:39:06.270 --> 02:39:08.005
In the US, our breakfast sandwiches

02:39:08.005 --> 02:39:09.573
all come with different variations of

02:39:09.573 --> 02:39:12.509
sausage, bacon, ham, egg, and cheese.

02:39:12.509 --> 02:39:15.712
And they come in either a
croissant, biscuit or melt form.

02:39:15.712 --> 02:39:17.381
We couldn't get the melt form,

02:39:17.381 --> 02:39:20.117
but we do have the
croissant and the biscuit

02:39:20.117 --> 02:39:21.718
in the loaded versions.

02:39:21.718 --> 02:39:25.155
Loaded just means that they
come with all of the toppings.

02:39:25.155 --> 02:39:26.890
They look like they're about to burst.

02:39:26.890 --> 02:39:29.393
So I believe that's true.

02:39:29.393 --> 02:39:31.428
In America, this is a biscuit.

02:39:33.897 --> 02:39:35.732
The salt that just got into,

02:39:35.732 --> 02:39:37.768
I'm like, I felt all
the moisture in my body

02:39:37.768 --> 02:39:39.603
just disappear with that one bite.

02:39:39.603 --> 02:39:41.104
That was crazy.

02:39:41.104 --> 02:39:44.074
Here are all the different
breakfast sandwich combinations

02:39:44.074 --> 02:39:46.276
that you can make at
Burger King in the US.

02:39:46.276 --> 02:39:48.979
So you can also get
the Egg-Normous burrito

02:39:48.979 --> 02:39:51.915
or its baby, if you don't
want that much of a burrito

02:39:51.915 --> 02:39:53.517
before like 10 a.m.

02:39:53.517 --> 02:39:55.385
We also have sweeter breakfast options,

02:39:55.385 --> 02:39:57.721
like these pancakes with the sausage

02:39:57.721 --> 02:39:59.122
and the French toast sticks.

02:40:00.991 --> 02:40:03.393
It literally feels like I
am chewing gum right now.

02:40:03.393 --> 02:40:06.463
That is crazy how stretchy

02:40:06.463 --> 02:40:08.932
and bouncy it is right now.

02:40:08.932 --> 02:40:13.170
They smell a little old,
like they were just refried.

02:40:13.170 --> 02:40:15.872
It's also chewy, just like the pancakes,

02:40:15.872 --> 02:40:19.209
but a lot less disturbing in the mouth.

02:40:21.111 --> 02:40:23.780
So Burger King entered China in 2005,

02:40:23.780 --> 02:40:26.350
which actually makes it late to the game.

02:40:26.350 --> 02:40:28.218
KFC and McD's had already been here

02:40:28.218 --> 02:40:29.853
for a decade by that point.

02:40:29.853 --> 02:40:31.321
And Chinese consumers know

02:40:31.321 --> 02:40:33.457
what Western fast food is like already.

02:40:33.457 --> 02:40:36.126
BK cultivates a slightly different image,

02:40:36.126 --> 02:40:39.162
one of slightly more prestige.

02:40:39.162 --> 02:40:41.798
And you'll find them
mostly in major cities,

02:40:41.798 --> 02:40:43.667
top-tier cities like Beijing, Shanghai,

02:40:43.667 --> 02:40:45.302
less so in smaller cities.

02:40:45.302 --> 02:40:46.803
I feel like in the US,

02:40:46.803 --> 02:40:50.407
Burger King has the reputation
of being somewhat fresher

02:40:50.407 --> 02:40:52.175
when it comes to ingredients.

02:40:52.175 --> 02:40:54.778
Maybe it's considered
on the more fresher side

02:40:54.778 --> 02:40:56.546
when it comes to American fast food,

02:40:56.546 --> 02:40:58.982
even though it's probably not.

02:40:58.982 --> 02:40:59.816
It's pretty funny.

02:40:59.816 --> 02:41:02.319
In the past, Burger
King has been criticized

02:41:02.319 --> 02:41:06.156
for its bad customer service,
for its rude servers.

02:41:06.156 --> 02:41:08.625
And the main thing was you
couldn't even complain,

02:41:08.625 --> 02:41:10.594
because they didn't have
a complaints hotline.

02:41:10.594 --> 02:41:13.497
So they're kind of like,
take it or leave it.

02:41:13.497 --> 02:41:15.198
Convenience, speed of service,

02:41:15.198 --> 02:41:18.969
that totally depends on
your specific Burger King.

02:41:18.969 --> 02:41:20.637
Is it fast food still? Yes.

02:41:20.637 --> 02:41:23.974
You still get the food in
around 10 to 15 minutes.

02:41:23.974 --> 02:41:26.376
It's just, will you be
getting what you ordered?

02:41:27.244 --> 02:41:28.378
Who knows?

02:41:28.378 --> 02:41:29.713
That's part of the fun.

02:41:29.713 --> 02:41:31.915
I would say that Burger King,

02:41:31.915 --> 02:41:35.886
out of McDonald's and KFC,
is the least localized.

02:41:35.886 --> 02:41:37.821
And so they're cultivating

02:41:37.821 --> 02:41:40.924
maybe the image of being
a gourmet burger joint,

02:41:40.924 --> 02:41:43.960
a sort of a go-between
regular fast food chain

02:41:43.960 --> 02:41:47.397
and an actual gourmet burger restaurant.

02:41:47.397 --> 02:41:50.200
When it comes to how they
adapt to local taste,

02:41:50.200 --> 02:41:53.403
I feel like there's nothing
that special on the menu.

02:41:53.403 --> 02:41:55.906
It's pretty normal American fast food.

02:41:55.906 --> 02:41:58.909
They did have that one
special Texas Whopper,

02:41:58.909 --> 02:42:00.744
which, I've never been to Texas,

02:42:00.744 --> 02:42:03.580
so I can't really speak
on how accurate that is.

02:42:03.580 --> 02:42:04.981
But it tasted really good.

02:42:04.981 --> 02:42:07.784
So in terms of competition,

02:42:07.784 --> 02:42:09.920
Burger King is actually fifth in China,

02:42:09.920 --> 02:42:12.422
behind KFC, McDonald's,

02:42:12.422 --> 02:42:14.825
Wallace Burger and Chicken,
which is a local brand,

02:42:14.825 --> 02:42:16.727
and Dicos, another local brand.

02:42:16.727 --> 02:42:19.863
McDonald's has to be Burger
King's biggest rival.

02:42:19.863 --> 02:42:21.798
As we're filming this in early May,

02:42:21.798 --> 02:42:23.600
we've gotten word that Burger King is

02:42:23.600 --> 02:42:26.636
closing around 300 to 400 locations.

02:42:28.271 --> 02:42:30.841
A Whopper is 27 yuan. That's $3.92.

02:42:33.543 --> 02:42:35.912
In the US, a Whopper costs $7.89,

02:42:35.912 --> 02:42:39.015
which is an 101.3% price increase

02:42:39.015 --> 02:42:41.084
compared to China's Whopper.

02:42:41.084 --> 02:42:44.354
Make it a meal with a medium
fry and a medium drink,

02:42:44.354 --> 02:42:48.759
and the price goes up to
40 yuan, which is $5.80.

02:42:48.759 --> 02:42:50.994
Add a medium fry and
a drink to your order,

02:42:50.994 --> 02:42:53.497
and that brings the price up to $11.99,

02:42:53.497 --> 02:42:56.800
which is an 106.7% increase in price.

02:42:56.800 --> 02:42:58.668
And if you want to upgrade to large,

02:42:58.668 --> 02:43:03.106
then that's 44 yuan, which is $6.38.

02:43:03.106 --> 02:43:06.042
Make it a large in the US, and
the price goes up to $12.59,

02:43:06.042 --> 02:43:08.879
which is a 97% increase in price.

02:43:08.879 --> 02:43:11.114
Just in general, I've
found that Burger King

02:43:11.114 --> 02:43:15.252
tends to be slightly more
expensive than McDonald's and KFC.

02:43:17.287 --> 02:43:18.755
China's Burger King doesn't share

02:43:18.755 --> 02:43:20.157
its nutritional information,

02:43:20.157 --> 02:43:22.359
but here are a few noteworthy moments

02:43:22.359 --> 02:43:24.094
from the last couple of years.

02:43:24.094 --> 02:43:27.364
In 2020, Burger King
apologized to its customers

02:43:27.364 --> 02:43:28.265
when it was reported that

02:43:28.265 --> 02:43:31.501
some of their locations
had sold expired food.

02:43:31.501 --> 02:43:33.303
So a Burger King in Nanchang,

02:43:33.303 --> 02:43:36.173
which is a major city in eastern China,

02:43:36.173 --> 02:43:38.909
had used expired ingredients
to make its burgers.

02:43:38.909 --> 02:43:42.179
And get this, there was
actually video footage of staff

02:43:42.179 --> 02:43:45.415
replacing the date labels
on the expired bread

02:43:45.415 --> 02:43:46.583
with new ones.

02:43:46.583 --> 02:43:49.352
And another Burger King
in exactly the same city

02:43:49.352 --> 02:43:51.888
did the same thing with expired chicken.

02:43:51.888 --> 02:43:54.224
Burger King responded with, and I quote,

02:43:54.224 --> 02:43:56.059
"Our mismanagement has betrayed

02:43:56.059 --> 02:43:57.861
the trust of consumers to Burger King,

02:43:57.861 --> 02:44:01.264
and we express our deepest
apologies for this."

02:44:01.264 --> 02:44:02.265
End quote.

02:44:02.265 --> 02:44:03.633
This caused China to probe further

02:44:03.633 --> 02:44:07.204
into other US fast food chains
like KFC and McDonald's.

02:44:07.204 --> 02:44:09.773
Burger King, along with
McDonald's, was sued last year

02:44:09.773 --> 02:44:11.208
for using PFAS,

02:44:11.208 --> 02:44:13.376
or "forever chemicals,"
in their packaging.

02:44:13.376 --> 02:44:15.278
Forever chemicals?

02:44:15.278 --> 02:44:16.947
It's in my body forever?

02:44:16.947 --> 02:44:20.417
Consumer reports found PFAS in
the French toast sticks bags,

02:44:20.417 --> 02:44:23.186
Whopper wrappers, and chicken nugget bags.

02:44:23.186 --> 02:44:26.423
We ate like two out of
those three things today.

02:44:26.423 --> 02:44:27.991
Oh, my God.

02:44:27.991 --> 02:44:30.560
PFAS are chemicals that
are hard to break down

02:44:30.560 --> 02:44:31.828
and last a long time,

02:44:31.828 --> 02:44:33.830
which are not good for the environment.

02:44:33.830 --> 02:44:35.866
And PFAS exposure has been linked

02:44:35.866 --> 02:44:38.268
to health problems in humans.

02:44:38.268 --> 02:44:41.204
Burger King has responded
in saying, quote,

02:44:55.151 --> 02:44:56.453
That's not soon enough.

02:44:56.486 --> 02:44:58.321
- From calorie counts to portion sizes.

02:44:58.321 --> 02:45:01.024
We wanted to find out all the
differences between Subway

02:45:01.024 --> 02:45:03.260
in the US and in China.

02:45:03.260 --> 02:45:05.061
This is Food Wars.

02:45:06.863 --> 02:45:08.832
Here in China standard Subway subs

02:45:08.832 --> 02:45:12.702
come in two sizes, six inch and

02:45:15.338 --> 02:45:16.439
twelve inch.

02:45:17.274 --> 02:45:18.608
They've done us the favor of

02:45:18.608 --> 02:45:22.579
cutting our 12 inch sub in half.

02:45:22.579 --> 02:45:23.446
How very kind.

02:45:23.446 --> 02:45:26.249
In the US, our subs also come in two sizes

02:45:26.249 --> 02:45:29.452
a six inch or a twelve inch,
also known as the foot long.

02:45:29.452 --> 02:45:30.553
We're gonna measure both of these

02:45:30.553 --> 02:45:31.688
with the tape measure to make sure

02:45:31.688 --> 02:45:33.857
that those lengths are actually correct.

02:45:33.857 --> 02:45:35.058
What does it look like?

02:45:35.058 --> 02:45:36.393
Is it right?

02:45:36.393 --> 02:45:37.794
Is it good?

02:45:37.794 --> 02:45:39.996
I would say it's like
maybe a few centimeters

02:45:39.996 --> 02:45:41.464
off of 12 inches

02:45:41.464 --> 02:45:43.166
but it's close enough
like I don't think you're

02:45:43.166 --> 02:45:45.602
gonna notice a few centimeters
of sandwich missing.

02:45:45.602 --> 02:45:48.471
I'll give you a pass
Subway, that's that's fine.

02:45:48.471 --> 02:45:52.075
That's about 30.8 centimeters.

02:45:52.075 --> 02:45:56.680
12.12598 inches.

02:45:56.680 --> 02:45:58.949
That one is six inches for sure.

02:45:58.949 --> 02:46:01.484
About 15 centimeters.

02:46:01.484 --> 02:46:06.122
5.9055 inches.

02:46:06.122 --> 02:46:08.425
We can also get sub platters in the us.

02:46:08.425 --> 02:46:10.260
Ours are the exact same size.

02:46:10.260 --> 02:46:13.096
Five 12 inch subs cut into 15 pieces.

02:46:13.096 --> 02:46:14.564
That is a lot of sandwich.

02:46:14.564 --> 02:46:15.699
It's very, very heavy.

02:46:15.699 --> 02:46:17.867
It's really heavy.

02:46:17.867 --> 02:46:19.269
I'm gonna leave it there.

02:46:19.269 --> 02:46:21.805
We used to have sub
platters and party subs

02:46:21.805 --> 02:46:23.139
but shows over folks.

02:46:23.139 --> 02:46:25.342
No more parties on this
side of the Pacific.

02:46:25.342 --> 02:46:26.710
How's it look for Nico?

02:46:26.710 --> 02:46:29.079
We used to have party subs in the US

02:46:29.079 --> 02:46:31.915
but Subway overhauled and
streamlined its menu last year

02:46:31.915 --> 02:46:34.317
and now seems to have
stopped offering them.

02:46:34.317 --> 02:46:36.386
Somebody check on Joe right now

02:46:36.386 --> 02:46:38.989
'cause I know he is devastated.

02:46:44.661 --> 02:46:45.962
Moving on from subs.

02:46:45.962 --> 02:46:50.967
Drinks at a Chinese Subway
only come in one size medium.

02:46:50.967 --> 02:46:53.036
That's just sad.

02:46:53.036 --> 02:46:57.207
Drinks at a US Subway come in
four sizes, small 21 ounces

02:46:57.207 --> 02:47:00.744
medium 30 ounces or
large, which is 40 ounces.

02:47:00.744 --> 02:47:01.878
You may have noticed I said

02:47:01.878 --> 02:47:04.681
we have four drink sizes
that only showed you three.

02:47:04.681 --> 02:47:07.217
That's because on Subway's
catering menu in the US

02:47:07.217 --> 02:47:10.887
you'll find this, thank you
to my beautiful assistant.

02:47:10.887 --> 02:47:13.156
It's a gallon of Hubert's Lemonade.

02:47:13.156 --> 02:47:15.658
This supposedly serves eight people,

02:47:15.658 --> 02:47:17.894
which would be 16 fluid ounces each.

02:47:17.894 --> 02:47:20.397
Why is the recommended
serving size for this lemonade

02:47:20.397 --> 02:47:23.033
smaller than the usual small size

02:47:23.033 --> 02:47:26.002
that's very suspicious Subway,
but I do love this lemonade.

02:47:26.002 --> 02:47:28.405
So the large is supposed to be 40 ounces.

02:47:28.405 --> 02:47:29.372
We're gonna measure it

02:47:29.372 --> 02:47:31.641
to see if I'm being lied to basically

02:47:31.641 --> 02:47:35.678
The medium is meant to
contain 473 milliliters

02:47:35.678 --> 02:47:38.081
of your drink.

02:47:38.081 --> 02:47:40.283
Let's see how much is actually in there.

02:47:40.283 --> 02:47:41.518
The coke is really dark

02:47:41.518 --> 02:47:43.420
so it's kind of hard for
me to see the numbers

02:47:43.420 --> 02:47:46.489
but it did go slightly above 32 ounces

02:47:46.489 --> 02:47:50.360
which is significantly less
than the 40 I was promised.

02:47:50.360 --> 02:47:52.462
And by the way, this was with no ice.

02:47:52.462 --> 02:47:54.931
It's meant to be 473 milliliters

02:47:54.931 --> 02:47:56.866
but I just wanted wanted
to show you look how

02:47:56.866 --> 02:47:59.335
much is missing from the top.

02:47:59.335 --> 02:48:04.307
This here is about 425
ish and if that's the case

02:48:05.008 --> 02:48:08.845
it's missing over 50
milliliters of my soda.

02:48:08.845 --> 02:48:10.313
What gives Subway?

02:48:12.715 --> 02:48:13.983
Here's everything that you'll find

02:48:13.983 --> 02:48:17.120
at Subway China that you
won't find in the US.

02:48:17.120 --> 02:48:18.555
Here's everything that you'll find

02:48:18.555 --> 02:48:21.057
at a US Subway that you
won't find in China.

02:48:21.057 --> 02:48:23.760
Obviously Subway's menu
is highly customizable

02:48:23.760 --> 02:48:25.829
by combining different ingredients.

02:48:25.829 --> 02:48:30.033
Subway claims, you can create
over 2 million sandwiches.

02:48:30.867 --> 02:48:32.035
I don't know if I believe that

02:48:32.035 --> 02:48:35.939
but I also don't have the
time and or money to prove it.

02:48:35.939 --> 02:48:37.707
So let's just say it's true.

02:48:37.707 --> 02:48:40.677
Now let's start with the
foundation of any sandwich.

02:48:40.677 --> 02:48:41.644
The bread.

02:48:41.644 --> 02:48:44.180
Now here in China we have
a couple of options and

02:48:44.180 --> 02:48:48.184
by a couple, I mean two that
you don't have in the US.

02:48:48.184 --> 02:48:50.153
First is honey oat

02:48:50.153 --> 02:48:52.822
and the second is parmesan oregano.

02:48:53.223 --> 02:48:55.058
Now it's on the menu

02:48:55.058 --> 02:48:58.261
but of all of the stores
that we ordered from

02:48:58.261 --> 02:49:00.730
they all changed out the parmesan oregano

02:49:00.730 --> 02:49:02.265
for just regular bread.

02:49:02.265 --> 02:49:04.367
So I don't know if they're
offering it anymore

02:49:04.367 --> 02:49:05.768
or it's just still on the menu

02:49:05.768 --> 02:49:07.070
and they've forgotten to take it out.

02:49:07.070 --> 02:49:09.539
And in the US we also have
exclusive bread options

02:49:09.539 --> 02:49:11.941
like artisan flatbread
and hardy multi-grain.

02:49:11.941 --> 02:49:13.443
Once you've picked your bread

02:49:13.443 --> 02:49:15.578
then it's time to choose your fillings.

02:49:15.578 --> 02:49:18.748
These are all of China's
exclusive fillings

02:49:18.748 --> 02:49:20.917
that you won't find in the US

02:49:20.917 --> 02:49:25.889
starting with the black
pepper thick cut steak.

02:49:26.089 --> 02:49:29.025
Oh, they weren't joking
when they said thick cut.

02:49:34.297 --> 02:49:37.167
Oh yeah, that's pretty decent.

02:49:37.167 --> 02:49:44.040
Here we have the Italian sausage
and the chicken thigh chop.

02:49:44.040 --> 02:49:46.676
It's always the chicken
thigh when it comes

02:49:46.676 --> 02:49:48.778
to chicken meat in a burger

02:49:48.778 --> 02:49:52.015
because Chinese people's
thigh is the juicy part

02:49:52.015 --> 02:49:53.049
not the breast.

02:49:53.049 --> 02:49:55.718
Next we've got the egg mayo series.

02:49:55.718 --> 02:49:57.320
We love our egg mayo here.

02:49:57.320 --> 02:50:01.291
We've got salami, egg mayo.

02:50:01.291 --> 02:50:04.827
I will need to ask for
more salami next time.

02:50:04.827 --> 02:50:06.029
Four pieces just doesn't cut it

02:50:06.029 --> 02:50:08.231
when you've got a six inch sub.

02:50:08.231 --> 02:50:10.300
There's also the tuna egg mayo.

02:50:10.300 --> 02:50:12.135
I'm just gonna move swiftly onto

02:50:12.135 --> 02:50:15.138
the chicken teriyaki egg mayo.

02:50:15.138 --> 02:50:18.241
The Chinese name is quite descriptive.

02:50:18.241 --> 02:50:21.811
It's the "Parent and Child" sandwich

02:50:21.811 --> 02:50:23.813
because obviously chicken and egg.

02:50:26.249 --> 02:50:28.518
Put egg mayo in a bun, I'm happy.

02:50:28.518 --> 02:50:31.421
Here we've got the
teriyaki chicken sandwich

02:50:31.421 --> 02:50:33.823
on honey oat bread.

02:50:33.823 --> 02:50:35.291
It's not got egg mayo in it.

02:50:35.291 --> 02:50:37.193
It's an inferior teriyaki chicken.

02:50:37.193 --> 02:50:41.965
The full house, which is tuna and chicken.

02:50:44.067 --> 02:50:45.335
Oh, it's a good thing none of you

02:50:45.335 --> 02:50:47.503
can smell my breath right now. Woo!

02:50:47.503 --> 02:50:50.173
And here we've just got
the bog standard ham.

02:50:50.173 --> 02:50:52.408
Save the best for last our

02:50:52.408 --> 02:50:56.346
pulled pork limited edition sandwich

02:50:56.346 --> 02:51:00.149
with chia seeds in our bread.

02:51:00.149 --> 02:51:03.319
I'm quite pleased with the amount of meat

02:51:03.319 --> 02:51:06.089
that's found its way into the Subway Subs.

02:51:08.725 --> 02:51:10.760
A little bit too sweet for my taste

02:51:12.395 --> 02:51:13.863
but the pulled pork is there.

02:51:13.863 --> 02:51:14.797
We have a ton of subs

02:51:14.797 --> 02:51:17.033
in the US that aren't on the Chinese menu.

02:51:17.033 --> 02:51:19.168
So let's start with
the classic sandwiches.

02:51:19.168 --> 02:51:22.272
So we've got the big hot
pastrami, buffalo chicken,

02:51:22.272 --> 02:51:25.608
chicken and bacon ranch, cold cut combo

02:51:25.608 --> 02:51:28.378
meatball marinara oven
roasted Turkey and ham,

02:51:28.378 --> 02:51:30.680
steak and cheese and the veggie patty.

02:51:30.680 --> 02:51:33.516
A fast food meatball sub sounds difficult

02:51:33.516 --> 02:51:36.152
so I kind of wanna try
it and see how it tastes.

02:51:36.152 --> 02:51:39.989
This is a very heavy
sandwich I just want to say.

02:51:39.989 --> 02:51:42.258
It reminds me of school lunch

02:51:42.258 --> 02:51:45.028
like the smell of walking into a cafeteria

02:51:45.028 --> 02:51:46.929
when you're in like seventh grade.

02:51:46.929 --> 02:51:48.731
That's the vibe I'm getting from it.

02:51:51.567 --> 02:51:53.569
It's an okay meatball sub.

02:51:53.569 --> 02:51:55.738
So this is the Chicken Bacon Ranch.

02:51:55.738 --> 02:51:58.441
I love chicken, I love
bacon and I love ranch.

02:51:58.441 --> 02:52:00.677
So hopefully I like the sandwich.

02:52:00.677 --> 02:52:02.478
There's just something
about how the meat looks

02:52:02.478 --> 02:52:04.681
that's making my tummy hurt a little.

02:52:04.681 --> 02:52:07.583
I think it's just the paleness
of the chicken and bread.

02:52:12.155 --> 02:52:15.124
I mean it tastes better than it looks.

02:52:15.124 --> 02:52:18.027
Next we have the no bready bowls

02:52:18.027 --> 02:52:21.230
starting with the black pepper steak

02:52:21.230 --> 02:52:23.866
egg mayo, no bready bowl.

02:52:23.866 --> 02:52:26.002
This actually looks really good.

02:52:26.002 --> 02:52:27.737
They've got some kidney beans

02:52:27.737 --> 02:52:30.006
and some kind of coarse
grain at the bottom as well.

02:52:30.006 --> 02:52:32.075
This actually looks decent.

02:52:32.075 --> 02:52:34.977
Oh yeah, now this tastes really good.

02:52:34.977 --> 02:52:39.949
Next we have the tuna
egg mayo, no bready bowl.

02:52:40.149 --> 02:52:43.319
Oh that does not look appetizing.

02:52:43.319 --> 02:52:46.956
So teriyaki chicken egg
mayo, no bready bowl

02:52:46.956 --> 02:52:48.691
but this is actually pretty decent.

02:52:48.691 --> 02:52:50.259
I think the no bready bowls

02:52:50.259 --> 02:52:51.828
are probably actually I'd order again.

02:52:51.828 --> 02:52:53.963
We also have the no bready bowls which

02:52:53.963 --> 02:52:56.432
according to the menu are
different than a salad

02:52:56.432 --> 02:52:59.168
although they look exactly like a salad

02:52:59.168 --> 02:53:02.472
A salad hidden under a
mountain of deli meats.

02:53:02.472 --> 02:53:05.408
Here are all of the US
exclusive bready bowls.

02:53:05.408 --> 02:53:07.477
The exclusive sandwiches don't stop there.

02:53:07.477 --> 02:53:10.146
In 2022, Subway in the US launched a range

02:53:10.146 --> 02:53:12.315
of menu items known as the Subway series.

02:53:12.315 --> 02:53:14.083
It's a list of 12 subs

02:53:14.083 --> 02:53:15.518
with predetermined ingredients

02:53:15.518 --> 02:53:17.720
designed to streamline
the ordering process.

02:53:17.720 --> 02:53:19.088
So instead of going down the line

02:53:19.088 --> 02:53:20.757
and picking every individual
thing that you want

02:53:20.757 --> 02:53:22.658
you can just order these off a menu.

02:53:22.658 --> 02:53:23.893
While prepping for this shoot,

02:53:23.893 --> 02:53:27.663
we thought we had most of the
subs on the Subway series menu

02:53:27.663 --> 02:53:29.832
but since then we have found out

02:53:29.832 --> 02:53:33.269
that they have dropped more
sandwiches on this menu.

02:53:33.269 --> 02:53:34.837
The list just seems to keep growing

02:53:34.837 --> 02:53:37.140
and I don't know when they're gonna stop.

02:53:37.140 --> 02:53:38.641
So let's just focus on the subs

02:53:38.641 --> 02:53:40.176
that we have in front of us right now.

02:53:40.176 --> 02:53:42.912
I am very intrigued by the monster.

02:53:42.912 --> 02:53:44.647
That name sounds awful

02:53:44.647 --> 02:53:46.549
and I'm hoping the sandwich will not be.

02:53:46.549 --> 02:53:48.851
I think it looks pretty good to me.

02:53:48.851 --> 02:53:50.553
Okay, so this is the monster

02:53:50.553 --> 02:53:53.222
which is steak, bacon, and cheddar.

02:53:58.961 --> 02:54:01.664
That's delicious and good.

02:54:01.664 --> 02:54:02.698
The Bella Mozza.

02:54:02.698 --> 02:54:05.501
I think that if I was any of
the sandwiches on this list

02:54:05.501 --> 02:54:06.769
I would want to be this one because

02:54:06.769 --> 02:54:10.573
why wouldn't I want to be
the prettiest sandwich?

02:54:10.573 --> 02:54:13.810
This one definitely has like
a more pleasing look to it.

02:54:13.810 --> 02:54:15.478
There's just like so much color in it.

02:54:15.478 --> 02:54:18.214
It looks like it has a lot
of fresh ingredients in it.

02:54:18.214 --> 02:54:21.884
So in the Bella Mozza we have
ham, capacola and mozzarella.

02:54:21.884 --> 02:54:24.287
All delicious. Let's taste it.

02:54:28.224 --> 02:54:29.058
Oh no.

02:54:30.126 --> 02:54:31.828
And I really, really like it.

02:54:31.828 --> 02:54:35.097
This feels very classic sandwich to me.

02:54:35.097 --> 02:54:36.632
Like if I was going to a sandwich shop,

02:54:36.632 --> 02:54:38.367
I'd probably order something like this.

02:54:38.367 --> 02:54:39.769
So this is the All American,

02:54:39.769 --> 02:54:42.305
which has turkey, ham and bacon.

02:54:42.305 --> 02:54:43.606
She looks pretty good.

02:54:48.010 --> 02:54:51.013
She's not really giving, I
think it's too much onions.

02:54:51.013 --> 02:54:54.350
I really, really wanna taste
the sliced avo Mexicali.

02:54:54.350 --> 02:54:56.352
This one has rotisserie
chicken, avocado and pepper jack

02:54:56.352 --> 02:54:58.921
that all sounds so good to me.

02:54:58.921 --> 02:55:00.223
Ooh, she's saucy.

02:55:00.223 --> 02:55:03.459
I feel like I haven't
seen much sauce going on.

02:55:03.459 --> 02:55:04.827
So this is different.

02:55:04.827 --> 02:55:06.429
There's a lot of sauce in there.

02:55:10.032 --> 02:55:12.768
It's good but I think the sandwich has

02:55:12.768 --> 02:55:16.038
just been sitting here for so
long that the bread got soggy.

02:55:16.038 --> 02:55:19.342
So the bread on the bottom
is like very, very soft

02:55:19.342 --> 02:55:22.078
but the actual taste of the sandwich

02:55:22.078 --> 02:55:24.180
is really, really good.
It's honestly tasty.

02:55:24.180 --> 02:55:25.915
And Subway also offers wraps.

02:55:25.915 --> 02:55:29.519
So here we've got the
black pepper steak wrap.

02:55:29.519 --> 02:55:31.587
Oh yeah, I think I prefer this version.

02:55:31.587 --> 02:55:35.091
Mm. Next we have the
teriyaki chicken wrap.

02:55:35.091 --> 02:55:37.493
Smells a bit wet.

02:55:37.493 --> 02:55:39.962
The Turkey breast wrap

02:55:39.962 --> 02:55:44.033
there's literally one
slice of Turkey breast.

02:55:44.033 --> 02:55:47.136
Here we have the Italian sausage wrap.

02:55:47.136 --> 02:55:48.838
The sausage has been butterflied.

02:55:48.838 --> 02:55:50.373
It's just one sausage.

02:55:50.373 --> 02:55:51.841
It's actually okay.

02:55:51.841 --> 02:55:53.910
After doing all of this Subway research

02:55:53.910 --> 02:55:56.546
they actually added wraps onto our menu.

02:55:56.546 --> 02:55:59.348
Here are all of the wraps that
you can get on the US menu.

02:55:59.348 --> 02:56:00.917
We also have a couple

02:56:00.917 --> 02:56:04.620
of exclusive meat options in
the US pepperoni and capacola.

02:56:04.620 --> 02:56:07.023
Here in China we have some
meaty toppings that you

02:56:07.023 --> 02:56:08.658
won't find in the us.

02:56:08.658 --> 02:56:11.427
For example, shrimp

02:56:11.427 --> 02:56:15.798
which they literally
gave us in a paper bag.

02:56:15.798 --> 02:56:18.568
Subway will ask you if you
want cheese on your sub

02:56:18.568 --> 02:56:21.304
and we definitely have a
lot more cheese options

02:56:21.304 --> 02:56:22.572
than they have in China.

02:56:22.572 --> 02:56:25.374
Both countries offer American
or shredded mozzarella

02:56:25.374 --> 02:56:28.010
but the US also offers
pepper jack, provolone

02:56:28.010 --> 02:56:29.579
swiss or monterey cheddar.

02:56:29.579 --> 02:56:31.948
China has one sandwich topping

02:56:31.948 --> 02:56:35.117
that you won't find in the
US and that's egg mayo.

02:56:35.117 --> 02:56:36.118
We love egg mayo here.

02:56:36.118 --> 02:56:36.953
I love egg mayo.

02:56:36.953 --> 02:56:38.988
It's basically just chunky mayo

02:56:38.988 --> 02:56:41.457
with eggs inside and you'll find it

02:56:41.457 --> 02:56:44.093
in over half of our
offerings here in China.

02:56:44.093 --> 02:56:46.395
Subway, you have it in subs, you have it

02:56:46.395 --> 02:56:49.098
in wraps and you have it
in protein bowls as well.

02:56:49.098 --> 02:56:50.232
All of these are egg mayo.

02:56:50.232 --> 02:56:51.334
It's delicious.

02:56:51.334 --> 02:56:53.703
When it comes to vegetable
toppings, both the US

02:56:53.703 --> 02:56:56.772
and China offer tomatoes,
lettuce, cucumber, pickles

02:56:56.772 --> 02:57:00.743
green pepper, black olives,
red onions and jalapenos.

02:57:00.743 --> 02:57:03.613
But the US also carries banana peppers

02:57:03.613 --> 02:57:05.948
my favorite spinach and avocado.

02:57:05.948 --> 02:57:08.084
We also have some exclusive sauces

02:57:08.084 --> 02:57:11.287
like barbecue and
thousand island dressing.

02:57:11.287 --> 02:57:13.823
And then there's also mayo, honey mustard

02:57:13.823 --> 02:57:16.192
black pepper sauce and olive oil.

02:57:16.192 --> 02:57:17.226
It's kind of shocking that

02:57:17.226 --> 02:57:19.662
we don't have thousand
island dressing as an option.

02:57:19.662 --> 02:57:22.632
It's not like a super
common sandwich spread

02:57:22.632 --> 02:57:24.300
at least not in my house.

02:57:24.300 --> 02:57:26.502
But you do see it on
Rubens and stuff like that.

02:57:26.502 --> 02:57:28.537
Exclusive sauces in the US include oil

02:57:28.537 --> 02:57:32.208
red wine vinegar, creamy
sriracha, buffalo sauce,

02:57:32.208 --> 02:57:36.145
MVP Parmesan vinegarette
and roasted garlic aioli.

02:57:36.145 --> 02:57:40.082
They shove these words in everywhere.

02:57:40.082 --> 02:57:42.718
You guys are like trying to gaslight me

02:57:42.718 --> 02:57:45.688
into thinking that this is like
an athlete's favorite food.

02:57:45.688 --> 02:57:46.956
And I know that's not true.

02:57:46.956 --> 02:57:49.492
It's crazy. It's crazy
what's happening here.

02:57:49.492 --> 02:57:51.761
MVP Parmesan vinaigrette isn't real.

02:57:51.761 --> 02:57:53.262
You made that up.

02:57:53.262 --> 02:57:54.664
Speaking of trying to make me think

02:57:54.664 --> 02:57:57.633
that athletes love Subway,
here are the athlete collabs.

02:57:57.633 --> 02:58:01.303
Here we have the avocado
spike bowl by Rob Gronkowski.

02:58:01.303 --> 02:58:03.305
The No Look Chicken by Patrick Mahomes.

02:58:03.305 --> 02:58:06.142
The Front Court Feast by Charles Barkley

02:58:06.142 --> 02:58:08.577
the Meatball Marksman by Steph Curry.

02:58:08.577 --> 02:58:11.847
And then there's the Danger Witch.

02:58:11.847 --> 02:58:13.416
Let's talk about the Danger witch.

02:58:13.416 --> 02:58:14.550
Once upon a time

02:58:14.550 --> 02:58:17.653
this was Russell Wilson's
Subway collab sandwich.

02:58:17.653 --> 02:58:19.955
I don't know what happened but

02:58:19.955 --> 02:58:23.125
at some point they removed
his name from the sandwich.

02:58:23.125 --> 02:58:24.827
I think it has something to do with

02:58:24.827 --> 02:58:28.664
this weird commercial they did
promoting the Danger Witch.

02:58:28.664 --> 02:58:31.400
You ever done anything dangerous?

02:58:33.569 --> 02:58:35.337
I obviously can't confirm anything

02:58:35.337 --> 02:58:37.173
but I'm dying to try this.

02:58:37.173 --> 02:58:39.575
So let's see what the
danger witch tastes like.

02:58:45.748 --> 02:58:48.184
They probably should get rid of it

02:58:48.184 --> 02:58:51.220
in general 'cause it's also
just not a very good sandwich.

02:58:51.220 --> 02:58:53.422
It mostly just tastes like mustard.

02:58:53.422 --> 02:58:56.058
Now it's tradition on
Food Wars to combine all

02:58:56.058 --> 02:58:58.360
of one country's exclusives together.

02:58:58.360 --> 02:59:00.863
I present to you the US only sub.

02:59:00.863 --> 02:59:05.067
It has bacon, pepper jack
cheese, banana peppers, spinach

02:59:05.067 --> 02:59:08.104
buffalo sauce, all on
jalapeno cheddar bread.

02:59:08.104 --> 02:59:10.473
I think our specific Subway didn't have

02:59:10.473 --> 02:59:11.907
jalapeno cheddar bread.

02:59:11.907 --> 02:59:14.877
This is their other cheesy bread

02:59:14.877 --> 02:59:16.912
but it's the closest thing we got.

02:59:16.912 --> 02:59:20.316
It mostly just tastes like
bacon, which I'm not upset about.

02:59:20.316 --> 02:59:25.321
This is the China only sub
black pepper steak, egg mayo

02:59:27.356 --> 02:59:29.759
thousand island dressing

02:59:33.796 --> 02:59:36.365
on honey oat bread.

02:59:36.365 --> 02:59:38.267
Let's see if you guys in
the states are missing out.

02:59:38.267 --> 02:59:41.604
You know egg mayo goes
on absolutely anything

02:59:41.604 --> 02:59:46.609
and the thick cut steak
gives it a nice oomph.

02:59:47.376 --> 02:59:49.245
Yeah, I'd order this again

02:59:49.245 --> 02:59:51.614
Now let's see what side
options we have in the US.

02:59:51.614 --> 02:59:55.751
Chips in general seem to
be more of a US exclusive.

02:59:55.751 --> 02:59:58.587
Here are all of the flavors
I was able to get my hands

02:59:58.587 --> 03:00:00.356
on at our location.

03:00:00.356 --> 03:00:01.991
So we have three lay's flavors.

03:00:01.991 --> 03:00:06.662
There's sour cream and
onion, classic and barbecue.

03:00:06.662 --> 03:00:09.365
We also have two baked Lays flavors.

03:00:09.365 --> 03:00:11.433
The original and barbecue.

03:00:11.433 --> 03:00:15.805
We have Doritos in both
cool ranch and nacho cheese.

03:00:15.805 --> 03:00:17.907
Two flavors of Miss Vicky's chips.

03:00:17.907 --> 03:00:21.243
We have jalapeno and spicy dill pickle

03:00:21.243 --> 03:00:23.112
and we have three flavors of Sun Chips.

03:00:23.112 --> 03:00:27.616
We have garden salsa
original and harvest cheddar.

03:00:27.616 --> 03:00:30.753
You can also get a go-go squeeze
applesauce as a kid's side.

03:00:30.753 --> 03:00:32.521
Subway also has sides,

03:00:32.521 --> 03:00:35.791
namely Ratan pepper popcorn chicken.

03:00:35.791 --> 03:00:37.860
So I would assume that

03:00:37.860 --> 03:00:40.563
this is meant to be
Szechwanese style chicken

03:00:40.563 --> 03:00:42.231
in that it should be spicy

03:00:42.231 --> 03:00:45.434
and also make your mouth pleasantly numb.

03:00:48.137 --> 03:00:51.407
Just the tiniest hint of chili heat.

03:00:51.407 --> 03:00:54.376
Here we've got some potato balls.

03:00:55.878 --> 03:00:57.479
It just tastes like hash browns.

03:00:57.479 --> 03:00:59.148
Now this is pretty unique.

03:00:59.148 --> 03:01:03.085
This is called Western region
style roast chicken wings.

03:01:03.085 --> 03:01:06.989
Usually when you say something
is Western region flavored

03:01:06.989 --> 03:01:09.825
they usually mean lamb or cumin.

03:01:12.862 --> 03:01:14.129
No, that was pretty good.

03:01:14.129 --> 03:01:15.464
No potato chips here.

03:01:15.464 --> 03:01:18.868
We're super healthy,
but we do have cookies.

03:01:18.868 --> 03:01:20.669
Now both the US and China

03:01:20.669 --> 03:01:22.872
each have an exclusive cookie.

03:01:22.872 --> 03:01:27.877
Here in China we have the peach oolong.

03:01:29.879 --> 03:01:32.481
Hmm, that's quite pleasant.

03:01:32.481 --> 03:01:34.149
And Subway in the US offers

03:01:34.149 --> 03:01:36.285
the raspberry cheesecake cookie.

03:01:36.285 --> 03:01:38.220
I love Subway cookies.

03:01:38.220 --> 03:01:41.624
They are surprisingly soft
and definitely the best cookie

03:01:41.624 --> 03:01:44.026
in fast food in my opinion.

03:01:44.026 --> 03:01:45.728
I just think that they're so good.

03:01:48.130 --> 03:01:50.599
It's amazing as I suspected.

03:01:50.599 --> 03:01:52.868
And finally we have drinks.

03:01:52.868 --> 03:01:56.705
I am very happy that Subways
in the US carry Coke products.

03:01:56.705 --> 03:01:58.340
You can get a classic Coca-Cola

03:01:58.340 --> 03:02:03.345
a little DC, Sprite, Dasani,
which not my favorite.

03:02:03.979 --> 03:02:08.017
Vitamin Water XXX, Gold Peak Sweet Tea

03:02:08.017 --> 03:02:10.686
Simply lemonade, orange or apple.

03:02:10.686 --> 03:02:13.789
Honest Kids Superfruit
Punch or a Hubbert Lemonade.

03:02:13.789 --> 03:02:18.160
For drinks, China carries
soy milk and PepsiCo products

03:02:18.160 --> 03:02:21.764
so you can get Pepsi,
Pepsi Light 7Up Tropicana.

03:02:21.764 --> 03:02:23.699
You can also get Aquafina water

03:02:23.699 --> 03:02:26.168
and it's soda water variety,

03:02:26.168 --> 03:02:28.203
but I guess only in select stores

03:02:28.203 --> 03:02:29.638
because when we ordered we ended up

03:02:29.638 --> 03:02:32.107
getting full spring, which is kind of

03:02:32.107 --> 03:02:35.277
like the Chinese version
of Evian I would say.

03:02:35.277 --> 03:02:39.181
Now Subway entered China
relatively late in 2005

03:02:39.181 --> 03:02:42.985
and I believe nationwide
they've got about 700 stores.

03:02:42.985 --> 03:02:44.019
When they first opened

03:02:44.019 --> 03:02:48.824
they had a lot more
presence than they do now.

03:02:48.824 --> 03:02:51.493
They've kind of slid into obscurity

03:02:51.493 --> 03:02:53.529
and they're only really found

03:02:53.529 --> 03:02:56.298
in major cities like Beijing and Shanghai.

03:02:56.298 --> 03:02:59.468
Sandwiches aren't really hot in China.

03:02:59.468 --> 03:03:01.904
People don't like cold
bread, cold sandwiches

03:03:01.904 --> 03:03:04.173
of course you can ask for
your sandwich to be heated up

03:03:04.173 --> 03:03:06.275
but just the fact that it's kind of a

03:03:06.275 --> 03:03:10.212
a cold sandwich as a default
is a bit of a turnoff.

03:03:10.212 --> 03:03:13.115
I think you can tell there
hasn't been much localization

03:03:13.115 --> 03:03:14.149
on the Subway menu.

03:03:14.149 --> 03:03:15.451
I mean there's the egg mayo,

03:03:15.451 --> 03:03:16.919
there's the Western region chicken,

03:03:16.919 --> 03:03:20.789
but cold custom made sandwiches

03:03:20.789 --> 03:03:23.058
are not really the
first thing you think of

03:03:23.058 --> 03:03:25.794
when you want food in China.

03:03:25.794 --> 03:03:28.063
You can probably guess
that Subway's in a bit

03:03:28.063 --> 03:03:29.765
of a sad state here in China.

03:03:29.765 --> 03:03:32.101
In terms of competition,
I mean there's no need to

03:03:32.101 --> 03:03:35.404
even try to compete with KFC, Mackey D.

03:03:35.404 --> 03:03:38.807
They're so far ahead, completely
left Subway in the dust.

03:03:38.807 --> 03:03:42.244
Now let's see, which country
is getting their subs for less.

03:03:42.244 --> 03:03:44.480
A foot long Italian BMT

03:03:44.480 --> 03:03:48.951
from a Chinese Subway
costs 47 Yuan, that's $6.79

03:03:48.951 --> 03:03:52.755
At the time of recording
a foot long Italian BMT

03:03:52.755 --> 03:03:54.623
from a US Subway costs $9 99.

03:03:54.623 --> 03:03:57.926
I was so curious as to what BMT means

03:03:57.926 --> 03:04:01.830
and it apparently stands for
biggest meatiest, tastiest.

03:04:01.830 --> 03:04:03.499
I don't know if I like that.

03:04:03.499 --> 03:04:06.402
That makes the US sandwich
this much more expensive.

03:04:06.402 --> 03:04:08.637
Subway pricing has been
a contentious subject

03:04:08.637 --> 03:04:10.305
in the US for a while now.

03:04:10.305 --> 03:04:11.206
You guys might remember

03:04:11.206 --> 03:04:13.642
the infamous $5 foot long promotion

03:04:13.642 --> 03:04:15.978
Subway operated for a really long time.

03:04:15.978 --> 03:04:17.479
It was pulled after franchisees

03:04:17.479 --> 03:04:19.415
said it was costing them too much money.

03:04:19.415 --> 03:04:21.717
Subway has repeatedly
attempted to bring it back

03:04:21.717 --> 03:04:24.086
but it's been quickly
killed every single time.

03:04:26.121 --> 03:04:28.157
I have a feeling that US Subway

03:04:28.157 --> 03:04:30.359
will be more unhealthy
than China's Subway.

03:04:30.359 --> 03:04:32.694
So let's compare a classic Turkey sub.

03:04:32.694 --> 03:04:34.396
A six inch oven roasted Turkey sub

03:04:34.396 --> 03:04:36.265
in the US is 270 calories.

03:04:36.265 --> 03:04:38.333
Now Subway China hasn't

03:04:38.333 --> 03:04:40.502
released its nutritional information,

03:04:40.502 --> 03:04:42.905
but based on independent
third party research

03:04:42.905 --> 03:04:45.074
I can tell you that

03:04:45.074 --> 03:04:47.509
a six inch oven roasted turkey sub

03:04:47.509 --> 03:04:50.913
here in China is 252 calories

03:04:50.913 --> 03:04:54.817
or 270 depending on who you talk to.

03:04:54.817 --> 03:04:56.952
The most calorific sandwich you can get is

03:04:56.952 --> 03:04:58.153
the Chicken and Bacon Ranch,

03:04:58.153 --> 03:05:00.956
which clocks in at 570 calories.

03:05:00.956 --> 03:05:05.127
I wanna guess the most caloric
sandwich in Subway China.

03:05:05.127 --> 03:05:08.730
I think it has to be the
black pepper thick cut steak.

03:05:08.730 --> 03:05:09.898
Am I right?

03:05:09.898 --> 03:05:14.903
Close? A six inch black pepper
thick cut is 415 calories,

03:05:16.171 --> 03:05:18.373
but our heaviest hitter is in fact

03:05:18.373 --> 03:05:23.378
the six inch tuna sandwich
clocking in at 450 calories.

03:05:24.113 --> 03:05:27.382
Not only is it not tasty, it's
also incredibly calorific.

03:05:27.382 --> 03:05:28.750
Is it in my food or not?

03:05:28.750 --> 03:05:30.285
Is it in my food or not?

03:05:30.285 --> 03:05:31.787
Is it, like, touching the food?

03:05:33.622 --> 03:05:34.590
Is it in the gloves?

03:05:34.590 --> 03:05:35.457
Is it in the hats?

03:05:35.457 --> 03:05:38.127
Is it in this little crown
that I've been wearing all day?

03:05:38.127 --> 03:05:39.595
I'm so stressed out.

